SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 2:15
DESCRIPTION:וַיִּקַּח יְהוָה אֱלֹהִים אֶת־הָ
 אָדָם וַיַּנִּחֵהוּ בְגַן־עֵדֶן לְעָבְ
 דָהּ וּלְשָׁמְרָהּ׃\nVayikach Adonai Elohim et-ha'adam v
 ayanichehu vegan-eden le'avedah uleshamerah\nAnd the LORD God took the man
 \, and put him into the garden of Eden to dress it and to keep it.\n\nAdam
  was put in the garden to work it and to guard it. The earth is placed in 
 our care\, and looking after it is part of our job.\n\nOpen Aleph: https:/
 /alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20261102@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261102
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261103
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 2:18
DESCRIPTION:וַיֹּאמֶר יְהוָה אֱלֹהִים לֹא־טוֹ
 ב הֱיוֹת הָאָדָם לְבַדּוֹ אֶעֱשֶׂהּ־לּ
 וֹ עֵזֶר כְּנֶגְדּוֹ׃\nVayomer Adonai Elohim lo-tov hey
 ot ha'adam levado e'eseh-lo ezer kenegdo\nAnd the LORD God said: ‘It is 
 not good that the man should be alone\; I will make him a help meet for hi
 m.’\n\n"It is not good to be alone." People need each other. Community\,
  friendship and family are part of how we were made.\n\nOpen Aleph: https:
 //alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20261103@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261103
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261104
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 4:9
DESCRIPTION:וַיֹּאמֶר יְהוָה אֶל־קַיִן אֵי הֶ
 בֶל אָחִיךָ וַיֹּאמֶר לֹא יָדַעְתִּי הֲ
 שֹׁמֵר אָחִי אָנֹכִי׃\nVayomer Adonai el-kayin ei hevel
  achikha vayomer lo yadati hashomer achi anokhi\nAnd the LORD said unto Ca
 in: ‘Where is Abel thy brother?’ And he said: ‘I know not\; am I my 
 brother’s keeper?’\n\nCain asks\, "Am I my brother's keeper?" The rest
  of the Torah answers yes. We are responsible for one another.\n\nOpen Ale
 ph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20261104@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261104
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261105
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 12:1
DESCRIPTION:וַיֹּאמֶר יְהוָה אֶל־אַבְרָם לֶךְ
 ־לְךָ מֵאַרְצְךָ וּמִמּוֹלַדְתְּךָ וּ
 מִבֵּית אָבִיךָ אֶל־הָאָרֶץ אֲשֶׁר אַרְ
 אֶךָּ׃\nVayomer Adonai el-Avram lekh-lekha me'artzekha umimoladtekha
  umibeit avikha el-ha'aretz asher ar'eka\nNow the LORD said unto Abram: 
 ‘Get thee out of thy country\, and from thy kindred\, and from thy fathe
 r’s house\, unto the land that I will show thee.\n\nLech lecha: "go for 
 yourself." Abraham leaves everything familiar to follow God. Every new sta
 rt\, including learning Hebrew\, takes a first step like this.\n\nOpen Ale
 ph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20261105@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261105
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261106
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 12:2
DESCRIPTION:וְאֶעֶשְׂךָ לְגוֹי גָּדוֹל וַאֲבָ
 רֶכְךָ וַאֲגַדְּלָה שְׁמֶךָ וֶהְיֵה בְּ
 רָכָה׃\nVe'e'eskha legoy gadol va'avarekhkha va'agadelah shemekha ve
 hyeh berakhah\nAnd I will make of thee a great nation\, and I will bless t
 hee\, and make thy name great\; and be thou a blessing.\n\nAbraham is told
  not only that he will be blessed but that he will be a blessing. A good l
 ife is one that brings good to others.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.
 onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20261106@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261106
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261107
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 15:5
DESCRIPTION:וַיּוֹצֵא אֹתוֹ הַחוּצָה וַיֹּאמֶ
 ר הַבֶּט־נָא הַשָּׁמַיְמָה וּסְפֹר הַכּ
 וֹכָבִים אִם־תּוּכַל לִסְפֹּר אֹתָם וַ
 יֹּאמֶר לוֹ כֹּה יִהְיֶה זַרְעֶךָ׃\nVayotze 
 oto hachutzah vayomer habet-na hashamaymah usefor hakokhavim im-tukhal lis
 por otam vayomer lo koh yihyeh zar'ekha\nAnd He brought him forth abroad\,
  and said: ‘Look now toward heaven\, and count the stars\, if thou be ab
 le to count them’\; and He said unto him: ‘So shall thy seed be.’\n\
 nGod takes Abraham outside to count the stars. When things feel small or u
 ncertain\, step back and look at the bigger picture.\n\nOpen Aleph: https:
 //alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20261107@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261107
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261108
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 18:25
DESCRIPTION:חָלִלָה לְּךָ מֵעֲשֹׂת כַּדָּבָר 
 הַזֶּה לְהָמִית צַדִּיק עִם־רָשָׁע וְהָ
 יָה כַצַדִּיק כָּרָשָׁע חָלִלָה לָּךְ 
 הֲשֹׁפֵט כָּל־הָאָרֶץ לֹא יַעֲשֶׂה מִ
 שְׁפָּט׃\nChalilah lekha me'asot kadavar hazeh lehamit tzadik im-r
 asha vehayah khatzadik karasha chalilah lakh hashofet kol-ha'aretz lo ya'a
 seh mishpat\nThat be far from Thee to do after this manner\, to slay the r
 ighteous with the wicked\, that so the righteous should be as the wicked\;
  that be far from Thee\; shall not the judge of all the earth do justly?
 ’\n\nAbraham argues with God to save the people of Sodom. In Jewish trad
 ition it is right to speak up for justice\, even before the highest author
 ity.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20261108@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261108
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261109
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 28:15
DESCRIPTION:וְהִנֵּה אָנֹכִי עִמָּךְ וּשְׁמַ
 רְתִּיךָ בְּכֹל אֲשֶׁר־תֵּלֵךְ וַהֲשִׁ
 בֹתִיךָ אֶל־הָאֲדָמָה הַזֹּאת כִּי לֹא 
 אֶעֱזָבְךָ עַד אֲשֶׁר אִם־עָשִׂיתִי אֵת
  אֲשֶׁר־דִּבַּרְתִּי לָךְ׃\nVehineh anokhi imakh u
 shemartikha bekhol asher-telekh vahashivotikha el-ha'adamah hazot ki lo e'
 ezavekha ad asher im-asiti et asher-dibarti lakh\nAnd\, behold\, I am with
  thee\, and will keep thee whithersoever thou goest\, and will bring thee 
 back into this land\; for I will not leave thee\, until I have done that w
 hich I have spoken to thee of.’\n\nJacob is alone and running away\, and
  God promises: I am with you\, wherever you go. You are never as alone as 
 you feel.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20261109@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261109
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261110
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 28:16
DESCRIPTION:וַיִּיקַץ יַעֲקֹב מִשְּׁנָתוֹ וַ
 יֹּאמֶר אָכֵן יֵשׁ יְהוָה בַּמָּקוֹם הַ
 זֶּה וְאָנֹכִי לֹא יָדָעְתִּי׃\nVayikatz Ya'ako
 v mishenato vayomer akhen yesh Adonai bamakom hazeh ve'anokhi lo yada'eti\
 nAnd Jacob awaked out of his sleep\, and he said: ‘Surely the LORD is in
  this place\; and I knew it not.’\n\nJacob wakes from his dream and says
  God was in this place and he did not know it. Holiness can be right where
  you are\, if you notice it.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.c
 om/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20261110@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261110
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261111
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 32:11
DESCRIPTION:קָטֹנְתִּי מִכֹּל הַחֲסָדִים וּמִ
 כָּל־הָאֱמֶת אֲשֶׁר עָשִׂיתָ אֶת־עַבְ
 דֶּךָ כִּי בְמַקְלִי עָבַרְתִּי אֶת־הַ
 יַּרְדֵּן הַזֶּה וְעַתָּה הָיִיתִי לִ
 שְׁנֵי מַחֲנוֹת׃\nKatoneti mikol hachasadim umikol-ha'emet 
 asher asita et-avdekha ki vemakli avarti et-hayarden hazeh ve'atah hayiti 
 lishnei machanot\nI am not worthy of all the mercies\, and of all the trut
 h\, which Thou hast shown unto Thy servant\; for with my staff I passed ov
 er this Jordan\; and now I am become two camps.\n\nBefore meeting his brot
 her Esau\, Jacob says he is not worthy of all the kindness he has received
 . Gratitude and humility go together.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.o
 nrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20261111@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261111
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261112
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 45:4
DESCRIPTION:וַיֹּאמֶר יוֹסֵף אֶל־אֶחָיו גְּשׁ
 וּ־נָא אֵלַי וַיִּגָּשׁוּ וַיֹּאמֶר אֲ
 נִי יוֹסֵף אֲחִיכֶם אֲשֶׁר־מְכַרְתֶּם 
 אֹתִי מִצְרָיְמָה׃\nVayomer yosef el-echav geshu-na elai 
 vayigashu vayomer ani yosef achikhem asher-mekhartem oti mitzrayemah\nAnd 
 Joseph said unto his brethren: ‘Come near to me\, I pray you.’ And the
 y came near. And he said: ‘I am Joseph your brother\, whom ye sold into 
 Egypt.\n\nJoseph says to the brothers who sold him\, "Come close to me." I
 t is one of the great moments of forgiveness in the Torah.\n\nOpen Aleph: 
 https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20261112@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261112
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261113
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 50:20
DESCRIPTION:וְאַתֶּם חֲשַׁבְתֶּם עָלַי רָעָה 
 אֱלֹהִים חֲשָׁבָהּ לְטֹבָה לְמַעַן עֲ
 שֹׂה כַּיּוֹם הַזֶּה לְהַחֲיֹת עַם־רָב׃
 \nVe'atem chashavtem alai ra'ah Elohim chashavah letovah lema'an asoh kayo
 m hazeh lehachayot am-rav\nAnd as for you\, ye meant evil against me\; but
  God meant it for good\, to bring to pass\, as it is this day\, to save mu
 ch people alive.\n\nJoseph tells his brothers that what they meant for har
 m\, God turned to good. Hard chapters of a life can lead somewhere good.\n
 \nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20261113@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261113
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261114
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 3:5
DESCRIPTION:וַיֹּאמֶר אַל־תִּקְרַב הֲלֹם שַׁל
 ־נְעָלֶיךָ מֵעַל רַגְלֶיךָ כִּי הַמָּק
 וֹם אֲשֶׁר אַתָּה עוֹמֵד עָלָיו אַדְמַת
 ־קֹדֶשׁ הוּא׃\nVayomer al-tikrav halom shal-ne'alekha me'al ra
 glekha ki hamakom asher atah omed alav admat-kodesh hu\nAnd He said: ‘Dr
 aw not nigh hither\; put off thy shoes from off thy feet\, for the place w
 hereon thou standest is holy ground.’\n\nAt the burning bush Moses is to
 ld to take off his shoes\, because the ground is holy. Some moments call f
 or us to slow down and pay attention.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.o
 nrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20261114@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261114
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261115
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 3:14
DESCRIPTION:וַיֹּאמֶר אֱלֹהִים אֶל־מֹשֶׁה אֶ
 הְיֶה אֲשֶׁר אֶהְיֶה וַיֹּאמֶר כֹּה תֹא
 מַר לִבְנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל אֶהְיֶה שְׁלָחַ
 נִי אֲלֵיכֶם׃\nVayomer Elohim el-Mosheh ehyeh asher ehyeh vayo
 mer koh tomar livnei Yisra'el ehyeh shelachani aleikhem\nAnd God said unto
  Moses: ‘I AM THAT I AM’\; and He said: ‘Thus shalt thou say unto th
 e children of Israel: I AM hath sent me unto you.’\n\nEhyeh asher ehyeh:
  "I will be what I will be." God's name here is about being present\, in e
 very time and place.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/mor
 ning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20261115@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261115
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261116
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 13:8
DESCRIPTION:וְהִגַּדְתָּ לְבִנְךָ בַּיּוֹם הַ
 הוּא לֵאמֹר בַּעֲבוּר זֶה עָשָׂה יְהוָה 
 לִי בְּצֵאתִי מִמִּצְרָיִם׃\nVehigadta levinkha b
 ayom hahu lemor ba'avur zeh asah Adonai li betzeti mimitzrayim\nAnd thou s
 halt tell thy son in that day\, saying: It is because of that which the LO
 RD did for me when I came forth out of Egypt.\n\nThis verse is why we tell
  the Passover story at the Seder. Each generation tells it as if it happen
 ed to them.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20261116@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261116
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261117
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 14:14
DESCRIPTION:יְהוָה יִלָּחֵם לָכֶם וְאַתֶּם 
 תַּחֲרִישׁוּן׃\nAdonai yilachem lakhem ve'atem tacharishun\n
 The LORD will fight for you\, and ye shall hold your peace.’\n\nAt the S
 ea of Reeds\, Moses tells the frightened people that God will fight for th
 em. Sometimes the right move is to stay calm and trust.\n\nOpen Aleph: htt
 ps://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20261117@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261117
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261118
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 15:2
DESCRIPTION:עָזִּי וְזִמְרָת יָהּ וַיְהִי־לִי
  לִישׁוּעָה זֶה אֵלִי וְאַנְוֵהוּ אֱלֹ
 הֵי אָבִי וַאֲרֹמְמֶנְהוּ׃\nAzi vezimrat yah vayhi
 -li lishu'ah zeh eli ve'anvehu elohei avi va'aromemenhu\nThe LORD is my st
 rength and song\, And He is become my salvation\; This is my God\, and I w
 ill glorify Him\; My father’s God\, and I will exalt Him.\n\nFrom the So
 ng at the Sea: "The Lord is my strength and my song." These words are sung
  in synagogue every morning.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.c
 om/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20261118@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261118
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261119
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 15:11
DESCRIPTION:מִי־כָמֹכָה בָּאֵלִם יְהוָה מִי 
 כָּמֹכָה נֶאְדָּר בַּקֹּדֶשׁ נוֹרָא תְ
 הִלֹּת עֹשֵׂה פֶלֶא׃\nMi-khamokhah ba'elim Adonai mi kam
 okhah nedar bakodesh nora tehilot oseh fele\nWho is like unto Thee\, O LOR
 D\, among the mighty? Who is like unto Thee\, glorious in holiness\, Fearf
 ul in praises\, doing wonders?\n\nMi chamocha\, "Who is like You?" This li
 ne from the Song at the Sea is part of the daily prayers\, just after the 
 Shema.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20261119@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261119
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261120
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 19:6
DESCRIPTION:וְאַתֶּם תִּהְיוּ־לִי מַמְלֶכֶת 
 כֹּהֲנִים וְגוֹי קָדוֹשׁ אֵלֶּה הַדְּבָ
 רִים אֲשֶׁר תְּדַבֵּר אֶל־בְּנֵי יִשְׂ
 רָאֵל׃\nVe'atem tihyu-li mamlekhet kohanim vegoy kadosh eleh hadevar
 im asher tedaber el-benei Yisra'el\nand ye shall be unto Me a kingdom of p
 riests\, and a holy nation. These are the words which thou shalt speak unt
 o the children of Israel.’\n\nAt Sinai the whole people is called a king
 dom of priests and a holy nation. Holiness is meant for everyone\, not onl
 y for a few.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20261120@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261120
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261121
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 20:2
DESCRIPTION:אָנֹכִי יְהוָה אֱלֹהֶיךָ אֲשֶׁר ה
 וֹצֵאתִיךָ מֵאֶרֶץ מִצְרַיִם מִבֵּית עֲ
 בָדִים׃\nAnokhi Adonai Elohekha asher hotzetikha me'eretz Mitzrayim
  mibeit avadim\nI am the LORD thy God\, who brought thee out of the land o
 f Egypt\, out of the house of bondage.\n\nThe Ten Commandments begin with 
 who God is: the One who brought us out of slavery. Freedom comes first\, a
 nd the commandments follow.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.co
 m/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20261121@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261121
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261122
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 20:8
DESCRIPTION:זָכוֹר אֶת־יוֹם הַשַׁבָּת לְקַדְּ
 שׁוֹ\nZakhor et-yom hashabat lekadesho\nRemember the sabbath day\, to 
 keep it holy.\n\nZachor: "Remember the Shabbat day." We remember it with c
 andles\, Kiddush\, rest and time with the people we love.\n\nOpen Aleph: h
 ttps://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20261122@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261122
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261123
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 20:12
DESCRIPTION:כַּבֵּד אֶת־אָבִיךָ וְאֶת־אִמֶּ
 ךָ לְמַעַן יַאֲרִכוּן יָמֶיךָ עַל הָאֲ
 דָמָה אֲשֶׁר־יְהוָה אֱלֹהֶיךָ נֹתֵן לָ
 ךְ׃\nKabed et-avikha ve'et-imekha lema'an ya'arikhun yamekha al ha'adam
 ah asher-Adonai Elohekha noten lakh\nHonour thy father and thy mother\, th
 at thy days may be long upon the land which the LORD thy God giveth thee.\
 n\nHonour your father and your mother. It is one of the Ten Commandments\,
  and the first that comes with a promise of long life.\n\nOpen Aleph: http
 s://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20261123@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261123
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261124
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 22:20
DESCRIPTION:וְגֵר לֹא־תוֹנֶה וְלֹא תִלְחָצֶנּ
 וּ כִּי־גֵרִים הֱיִיתֶם בְּאֶרֶץ מִצְרָ
 יִם׃\nVeger lo-toneh velo tilchatzenu ki-gerim heyitem be'eretz Mitzra
 yim\nAnd a stranger shalt thou not wrong\, neither shalt thou oppress him\
 ; for ye were strangers in the land of Egypt.\n\nDo not wrong the stranger
 \, because you were strangers in Egypt. This idea comes up again and again
  in the Torah.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20261124@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261124
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261125
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 23:2
DESCRIPTION:לֹא־תִהְיֶה אַחֲרֵי־רַבִּים לְרָ
 עֹת וְלֹא־תַעֲנֶה עַל־רִב לִנְטֹת אַחֲ
 רֵי רַבִּים לְהַטֹּת׃\nLo-tihyeh acharei-rabim lera'ot 
 velo-ta'aneh al-riv lintot acharei rabim lehatot\nThou shalt not follow a 
 multitude to do evil\; neither shalt thou bear witness in a cause to turn 
 aside after a multitude to pervert justice\;\n\nDo not follow the crowd to
  do wrong. Doing the right thing sometimes means standing apart.\n\nOpen A
 leph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20261125@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261125
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261126
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 23:9
DESCRIPTION:וְגֵר לֹא תִלְחָץ וְאַתֶּם יְדַעְ
 תֶּם אֶת־נֶפֶשׁ הַגֵּר כִּי־גֵרִים הֱיִ
 יתֶם בְּאֶרֶץ מִצְרָיִם׃\nVeger lo tilchatz ve'atem 
 yedatem et-nefesh hager ki-gerim heyitem be'eretz Mitzrayim\nAnd a strange
 r shalt thou not oppress\; for ye know the heart of a stranger\, seeing ye
  were strangers in the land of Egypt.\n\n"You know the heart of the strang
 er." Our own history should make us kind to newcomers.\n\nOpen Aleph: http
 s://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20261126@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261126
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261127
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 25:8
DESCRIPTION:וְעָשׂוּ לִי מִקְדָּשׁ וְשָׁכַנְ
 תִּי בְּתוֹכָם׃\nVe'asu li mikdash veshakhanti betokham\nAnd
  let them make Me a sanctuary\, that I may dwell among them.\n\n"Make Me a
  sanctuary\, and I will dwell among them." Not "in it\," but among them: G
 od lives among people\, in the places they make holy.\n\nOpen Aleph: https
 ://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20261127@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261127
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261128
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 33:13
DESCRIPTION:וְעַתָּה אִם־נָא מָצָאתִי חֵן בְּ
 עֵינֶיךָ הוֹדִעֵנִי נָא אֶת־דְּרָכֶךָ 
 וְאֵדָעֲךָ לְמַעַן אֶמְצָא־חֵן בְּעֵי
 נֶיךָ וּרְאֵה כִּי עַמְּךָ הַגּוֹי הַ
 זֶּה׃\nVe'atah im-na matzati chen be'einekha hodi'eni na et-derakhekh
 a ve'eda'akha lema'an emtza-chen be'einekha ure'eh ki amekha hagoy hazeh\n
 Now therefore\, I pray Thee\, if I have found grace in Thy sight\, show me
  now Thy ways\, that I may know Thee\, to the end that I may find grace in
  Thy sight\; and consider that this nation is Thy people.’\n\nMoses asks
  God\, "Show me Your ways\, so that I may know You." Learning is one of th
 e ways Jews come close to God.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender
 .com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20261128@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261128
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261129
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 34:6
DESCRIPTION:וַיַּעֲבֹר יְהוָה עַל־פָּנָיו וַ
 יִּקְרָא יְהוָה יְהוָה אֵל רַחוּם וְחַ
 נּוּן אֶרֶךְ אַפַּיִם וְרַב־חֶסֶד וֶאֱ
 מֶת\nVaya'avor Adonai al-panav vayikra Adonai Adonai el rachum vechanun
  erekh apayim verav-chesed ve'emet\nAnd the LORD passed by before him\, an
 d proclaimed: ‘The LORD\, the LORD\, God\, merciful and gracious\, long-
 suffering\, and abundant in goodness and truth\;\n\nThese are God's qualit
 ies of mercy\, sung on the High Holy Days: compassionate\, gracious\, slow
  to anger\, full of kindness and truth.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review
 .onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20261129@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261129
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261130
SUMMARY:Torah: Leviticus 19:2
DESCRIPTION:דַּבֵּר אֶל־כָּל־עֲדַת בְּנֵי־יִ
 שְׂרָאֵל וְאָמַרְתָּ אֲלֵהֶם קְדֹשִׁים 
 תִּהְיוּ כִּי קָדוֹשׁ אֲנִי יְהוָה אֱלֹ
 הֵיכֶם׃\nDaber el-kol-adat benei-Yisra'el ve'amarta alehem kedoshim
  tihyu ki kadosh ani Adonai Eloheikhem\nSpeak unto all the congregation of
  the children of Israel\, and say unto them: Ye shall be holy\; for I the 
 LORD your God am holy.\n\n"You shall be holy\, for I am holy." The chapter
  that follows shows what that means: honesty\, kindness and fairness in ev
 eryday life.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20261130@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261130
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261201
SUMMARY:Torah: Leviticus 19:3
DESCRIPTION:אִישׁ אִמּוֹ וְאָבִיו תִּירָאוּ 
 וְאֶת־שַׁבְּתֹתַי תִּשְׁמֹרוּ אֲנִי יְ
 הוָה אֱלֹהֵיכֶם׃\nIsh imo ve'aviv tira'u ve'et-shabetotai t
 ishmoru ani Adonai Eloheikhem\nYe shall fear every man his mother\, and hi
 s father\, and ye shall keep My sabbaths: I am the LORD your God.\n\nRespe
 ct your parents and keep Shabbat. Both are about honouring where we come f
 rom.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20261201@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261201
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261202
SUMMARY:Torah: Leviticus 19:9
DESCRIPTION:וּבְקֻצְרְכֶם אֶת־קְצִיר אַרְצְ
 כֶם לֹא תְכַלֶּה פְּאַת שָׂדְךָ לִקְצֹר 
 וְלֶקֶט קְצִירְךָ לֹא תְלַקֵּט׃\nUvekutzrekhem
  et-ketzir artzekhem lo tekhaleh pe'at sadekha liktzor veleket ketzirekha 
 lo telaket\nAnd when ye reap the harvest of your land\, thou shalt not who
 lly reap the corner of thy field\, neither shalt thou gather the gleaning 
 of thy harvest.\n\nLeave the corners of your field for people in need. Giv
 ing to others is built right into how we earn and spend.\n\nOpen Aleph: ht
 tps://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20261202@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261202
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261203
SUMMARY:Torah: Leviticus 19:14
DESCRIPTION:לֹא־תְקַלֵּל חֵרֵשׁ וְלִפְנֵי עִ
 וֵּר לֹא תִתֵּן מִכְשֹׁל וְיָרֵאתָ מֵּ
 אֱלֹהֶיךָ אֲנִי יְהוָה׃\nLo-tekalel cheresh velifnei 
 iver lo titen mikhshol veyareta me'Elohekha ani Adonai\nThou shalt not cur
 se the deaf\, nor put a stumbling-block before the blind\, but thou shalt 
 fear thy God: I am the LORD.\n\nDo not curse the deaf or put a stumbling b
 lock before the blind. Treat everyone with care\, especially those who can
 not defend themselves.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/m
 orning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20261203@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261203
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261204
SUMMARY:Torah: Leviticus 19:16
DESCRIPTION:לֹא־תֵלֵךְ רָכִיל בְּעַמֶּיךָ לֹא
  תַעֲמֹד עַל־דַּם רֵעֶךָ אֲנִי יְהוָה׃\nL
 o-telekh rakhil be'amekha lo ta'amod al-dam re'ekha ani Adonai\nThou shalt
  not go up and down as a talebearer among thy people\; neither shalt thou 
 stand idly by the blood of thy neighbour: I am the LORD.\n\nDo not spread 
 gossip\, and do not stand by while your neighbour is in danger. Words can 
 hurt\, and silence can too.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.co
 m/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20261204@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261204
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261205
SUMMARY:Torah: Leviticus 19:18
DESCRIPTION:לֹא־תִקֹּם וְלֹא־תִטֹּר אֶת־בְּ
 נֵי עַמֶּךָ וְאָהַבְתָּ לְרֵעֲךָ כָּמוֹ
 ךָ אֲנִי יְהוָה׃\nLo-tikom velo-titor et-benei amekha ve'aha
 vta lere'akha kamokha ani Adonai\nThou shalt not take vengeance\, nor bear
  any grudge against the children of thy people\, but thou shalt love thy n
 eighbour as thyself: I am the LORD.\n\n"Love your neighbour as yourself." 
 Rabbi Akiva called this the great principle of the whole Torah.\n\nOpen Al
 eph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20261205@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261205
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261206
SUMMARY:Torah: Leviticus 19:32
DESCRIPTION:מִפְּנֵי שֵׂיבָה תָּקוּם וְהָדַרְ
 תָּ פְּנֵי זָקֵן וְיָרֵאתָ מֵּאֱלֹהֶיךָ
  אֲנִי יְהוָה׃\nMipenei seivah takum vehadarta penei zaken vey
 areta me'Elohekha ani Adonai\nThou shalt rise up before the hoary head\, a
 nd honour the face of the old man\, and thou shalt fear thy God: I am the 
 LORD.\n\nRise before the elderly and honour them. Age brings wisdom\, and 
 the Torah asks us to show it respect.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.o
 nrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20261206@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261206
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261207
SUMMARY:Torah: Leviticus 25:10
DESCRIPTION:וְקִדַּשְׁתֶּם אֵת שְׁנַת הַחֲמִ
 שִּׁים שָׁנָה וּקְרָאתֶם דְּרוֹר בָּאָ
 רֶץ לְכָל־יֹשְׁבֶיהָ יוֹבֵל הִוא תִּהְ
 יֶה לָכֶם וְשַׁבְתֶּם אִישׁ אֶל־אֲחֻזָּ
 תוֹ וְאִישׁ אֶל־מִשְׁפַּחְתּוֹ תָּשֻׁב
 וּ׃\nVekidashtem et shenat hachamishim shanah ukeratem deror ba'aretz l
 ekhol-yosheveha yovel hiv tihyeh lakhem veshavtem ish el-achuzato ve'ish e
 l-mishpachto tashuvu\nAnd ye shall hallow the fiftieth year\, and proclaim
  liberty throughout the land unto all the inhabitants thereof\; it shall b
 e a jubilee unto you\; and ye shall return every man unto his possession\,
  and ye shall return every man unto his family.\n\n"Proclaim liberty throu
 ghout the land." These words about the Jubilee year are cast on the Libert
 y Bell in Philadelphia.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/
 morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20261207@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261207
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261208
SUMMARY:Torah: Numbers 6:24
DESCRIPTION:יְבָרֶכְךָ יְהוָה וְיִשְׁמְרֶךָ׃\
 nYevarekhkha Adonai veyishmerekha\nThe LORD bless thee\, and keep thee\;\n
 \nThe first line of the Priestly Blessing\, still said in synagogues and b
 y parents to children on Friday night.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.
 onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20261208@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261208
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261209
SUMMARY:Torah: Numbers 6:26
DESCRIPTION:יִשָּׂא יְהוָה פָּנָיו אֵלֶיךָ וְ
 יָשֵׂם לְךָ שָׁלוֹם׃\nYisa Adonai panav elekha veyasem l
 ekha shalom\nThe LORD lift up His countenance upon thee\, and give thee pe
 ace.\n\nThe Priestly Blessing ends with shalom\, peace. In Hebrew\, shalom
  also means wholeness: everything in its right place.\n\nOpen Aleph: https
 ://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20261209@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261209
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261210
SUMMARY:Torah: Numbers 11:29
DESCRIPTION:וַיֹּאמֶר לוֹ מֹשֶׁה הַמְקַנֵּא 
 אַתָּה לִי וּמִי יִתֵּן כָּל־עַם יְהוָה 
 נְבִיאִים כִּי־יִתֵּן יְהוָה אֶת־רוּח
 וֹ עֲלֵיהֶם׃\nVayomer lo Mosheh hamkane atah li umi yiten kol-a
 m Adonai nevi'im ki-yiten Adonai et-rucho aleihem\nAnd Moses said unto him
 : ‘Art thou jealous for my sake? would that all the LORD’S people were
  prophets\, that the LORD would put His spirit upon them! ’\n\nWhen othe
 rs begin to prophesy\, Moses is not jealous. He wishes everyone could shar
 e God's spirit. Great leaders lift others up.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-
 review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20261210@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261210
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261211
SUMMARY:Torah: Numbers 15:39
DESCRIPTION:וְהָיָה לָכֶם לְצִיצִת וּרְאִיתֶם
  אֹתוֹ וּזְכַרְתֶּם אֶת־כָּל־מִצְוֹת יְ
 הוָה וַעֲשִׂיתֶם אֹתָם וְלֹא־תָתֻרוּ אַ
 חֲרֵי לְבַבְכֶם וְאַחֲרֵי עֵינֵיכֶם אֲ
 שֶׁר־אַתֶּם זֹנִים אַחֲרֵיהֶם׃\nVehayah lakhem
  letzitzit ure'item oto uzekhartem et-kol-mitzvot Adonai va'asitem otam ve
 lo-taturu acharei levavkhem ve'acharei eineikhem asher-atem zonim achareih
 em\nAnd it shall be unto you for a fringe\, that ye may look upon it\, and
  remember all the commandments of the LORD\, and do them\; and that ye go 
 not about after your own heart and your own eyes\, after which ye use to g
 o astray\;\n\nThis verse is about the tzitzit\, the fringes on the tallit.
  Seeing them is a reminder of the commandments and of who we want to be.\n
 \nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20261211@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261211
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261212
SUMMARY:Torah: Numbers 24:5
DESCRIPTION:מַה־טֹּבוּ אֹהָלֶיךָ יַעֲקֹב מִ
 שְׁכְּנֹתֶיךָ יִשְׂרָאֵל׃\nMah-tovu ohalekha Ya'ak
 ov mishkenotekha Yisra'el\nHow goodly are thy tents\, O Jacob\, Thy dwelli
 ngs\, O Israel!\n\nMah tovu\, "How good are your tents." Many synagogues o
 pen the morning service with these words.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-revi
 ew.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20261212@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261212
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261213
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 4:9
DESCRIPTION:רַק הִשָּׁמֶר לְךָ וּשְׁמֹר נַפְ
 שְׁךָ מְאֹד פֶּן־תִּשְׁכַּח אֶת־הַדְּ
 בָרִים אֲשֶׁר־רָאוּ עֵינֶיךָ וּפֶן־יָס
 וּרוּ מִלְּבָבְךָ כֹּל יְמֵי חַיֶּיךָ 
 וְהוֹדַעְתָּם לְבָנֶיךָ וְלִבְנֵי בָנֶ
 יךָ׃\nRak hishamer lekha ushemor nafshekha me'od pen-tishkach et-hadev
 arim asher-ra'u einekha ufen-yasuru milevavekha kol yemei chayekha vehodat
 am levanekha velivnei vanekha\nOnly take heed to thyself\, and keep thy so
 ul diligently\, lest thou forget the things which thine eyes saw\, and les
 t they depart from thy heart all the days of thy life\; but make them know
 n unto thy children and thy children’s children\;\n\nDo not forget what 
 you have seen\, and teach it to your children and grandchildren. Memory is
  how a people stays alive.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com
 /#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20261213@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261213
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261214
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 6:4
DESCRIPTION:שְׁמַע יִשְׂרָאֵל יְהוָה אֱלֹהֵינ
 וּ יְהוָה אֶחָד׃\nShema Yisra'el Adonai Eloheinu Adonai echa
 d\nHEAR\, O ISRAEL: THE LORD OUR GOD\, THE LORD IS ONE.\n\nThe Shema\, the
  central line of Jewish prayer: "Hear\, O Israel\, the Lord is our God\, t
 he Lord is One." It is said morning and night.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef
 -review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20261214@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261214
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261215
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 6:5
DESCRIPTION:וְאָהַבְתָּ אֵת יְהוָה אֱלֹהֶיךָ 
 בְּכָל־לְבָבְךָ וּבְכָל־נַפְשְׁךָ וּבְ
 כָל־מְאֹדֶךָ׃\nVe'ahavta et Adonai Elohekha bekhol-levavekha 
 uvekhol-nafshekha uvekhol-me'odekha\nAnd thou shalt love the LORD thy God 
 with all thy heart\, and with all thy soul\, and with all thy might.\n\nV'
 ahavta: love God with all your heart\, all your soul and all your strength
 . Faith in Judaism is about love\, not only belief.\n\nOpen Aleph: https:/
 /alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20261215@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261215
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261216
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 6:7
DESCRIPTION:וְשִׁנַּנְתָּם לְבָנֶיךָ וְדִבַּ
 רְתָּ בָּם בְּשִׁבְתְּךָ בְּבֵיתֶךָ וּ
 בְלֶכְתְּךָ בַדֶּרֶךְ וּבְשָׁכְבְּךָ 
 וּבְקוּמֶךָ׃\nVeshinantam levanekha vedibarta bam beshivtekha 
 beveitekha uvelekhtekha vaderekh uveshakhbekha uvekumekha\nand thou shalt 
 teach them diligently unto thy children\, and shalt talk of them when thou
  sittest in thy house\, and when thou walkest by the way\, and when thou l
 iest down\, and when thou risest up.\n\nTalk about these words at home\, o
 n the road\, when you lie down and when you get up. That is why the Shema 
 is said at bedtime and in the morning.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.
 onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20261216@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261216
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261217
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 8:3
DESCRIPTION:וַיְעַנְּךָ וַיַּרְעִבֶךָ וַיַּ
 אֲכִלְךָ אֶת הַמָּן אֲשֶׁר לֹא־יָדַעְ
 תָּ וְלֹא יָדְעוּן אֲבֹתֶיךָ לְמַעַן ה
 וֹדִעֲךָ כִּי לֹא עַל־הַלֶּחֶם לְבַדּוֹ
  יִחְיֶה הָאָדָם כִּי עַל־כָּל־מוֹצָא 
 פִי־יְהוָה יִחְיֶה הָאָדָם׃\nVay'anekha vayar'ive
 kha vaya'akhilkha et haman asher lo-yadata velo yad'un avotekha lema'an ho
 di'akha ki lo al-halechem levado yichyeh ha'adam ki al-kol-motza fi-Adonai
  yichyeh ha'adam\nAnd He afflicted thee\, and suffered thee to hunger\, an
 d fed thee with manna\, which thou knewest not\, neither did thy fathers k
 now\; that He might make thee know that man doth not live by bread only\, 
 but by every thing that proceedeth out of the mouth of the LORD doth man l
 ive.\n\n"A person does not live by bread alone." We need meaning\, learnin
 g and purpose as much as food.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender
 .com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20261217@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261217
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261218
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 8:10
DESCRIPTION:וְאָכַלְתָּ וְשָׂבָעְתָּ וּבֵרַ
 כְתָּ אֶת־יְהוָה אֱלֹהֶיךָ עַל־הָאָרֶץ 
 הַטֹּבָה אֲשֶׁר נָתַן־לָךְ׃\nVe'akhalta vesava'et
 a uverakhta et-Adonai Elohekha al-ha'aretz hatovah asher natan-lakh\nAnd t
 hou shalt eat and be satisfied\, and bless the LORD thy God for the good l
 and which He hath given thee.\n\nEat\, be satisfied\, and bless. This vers
 e is the source of Birkat Hamazon\, the blessing after meals.\n\nOpen Alep
 h: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20261218@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261218
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261219
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 10:19
DESCRIPTION:וַאֲהַבְתֶּם אֶת־הַגֵּר כִּי־גֵ
 רִים הֱיִיתֶם בְּאֶרֶץ מִצְרָיִם׃\nVa'ahavte
 m et-hager ki-gerim heyitem be'eretz Mitzrayim\nLove ye therefore the stra
 nger\; for ye were strangers in the land of Egypt.\n\nLove the stranger\, 
 because you were strangers in Egypt. The Torah asks for more than not hurt
 ing newcomers\; it asks us to love them.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-revie
 w.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20261219@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261219
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261220
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 16:20
DESCRIPTION:צֶדֶק צֶדֶק תִּרְדֹּף לְמַעַן תִּ
 חְיֶה וְיָרַשְׁתָּ אֶת־הָאָרֶץ אֲשֶׁר־
 יְהוָה אֱלֹהֶיךָ נֹתֵן לָךְ׃\nTzedek tzedek tirdo
 f lema'an tichyeh veyarashta et-ha'aretz asher-Adonai Elohekha noten lakh\
 nJustice\, justice shalt thou follow\, that thou mayest live\, and inherit
  the land which the LORD thy God giveth thee.\n\nTzedek tzedek tirdof: "Ju
 stice\, justice you shall pursue." The word is said twice\, to show how ha
 rd we should work for it.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/
 #/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20261220@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261220
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261221
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 30:14
DESCRIPTION:כִּי־קָרוֹב אֵלֶיךָ הַדָּבָר מְאֹ
 ד בְּפִיךָ וּבִלְבָבְךָ לַעֲשֹׂתוֹ׃\nKi-ka
 rov elekha hadavar me'od befikha uvilvavekha la'asoto\nBut the word is ver
 y nigh unto thee\, in thy mouth\, and in thy heart\, that thou mayest do i
 t.\n\nThe Torah is not far away: it is in your mouth and in your heart. It
  is within reach\, one word at a time.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.
 onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20261221@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261221
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261222
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 30:19
DESCRIPTION:הַעִידֹתִי בָכֶם הַיּוֹם אֶת־הַ
 שָּׁמַיִם וְאֶת־הָאָרֶץ הַחַיִּים וְהַ
 מָּוֶת נָתַתִּי לְפָנֶיךָ הַבְּרָכָה וְ
 הַקְּלָלָה וּבָחַרְתָּ בַּחַיִּים לְמַ
 עַן תִּחְיֶה אַתָּה וְזַרְעֶךָ׃\nHa'idoti vakh
 em hayom et-hashamayim ve'et-ha'aretz hachayim vehamavet natati lefanekha 
 haberakhah vehakelalah uvacharta bachayim lema'an tichyeh atah vezar'ekha\
 nI call heaven and earth to witness against you this day\, that I have set
  before thee life and death\, the blessing and the curse\; therefore choos
 e life\, that thou mayest live\, thou and thy seed\;\n\n"Choose life." Eve
 ry day brings choices\, and the Torah asks us to choose the ones that lead
  to life and blessing.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/m
 orning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20261222@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261222
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261223
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 31:6
DESCRIPTION:חִזְקוּ וְאִמְצוּ אַל־תִּירְאוּ 
 וְאַל־תַּעַרְצוּ מִפְּנֵיהֶם כִּי יְה
 וָה אֱלֹהֶיךָ הוּא הַהֹלֵךְ עִמָּךְ לֹא 
 יַרְפְּךָ וְלֹא יַעַזְבֶךָּ׃\nChizku ve'imtzu al
 -tir'u ve'al-ta'artzu mipeneihem ki Adonai Elohekha hu haholekh imakh lo y
 arpekha velo ya'azveka\nBe strong and of good courage\, fear not\, nor be 
 affrighted at them\; for the LORD thy God\, He it is that doth go with the
 e\; He will not fail thee\, nor forsake thee.’\n\nChazak ve'ematz: "Be s
 trong and of good courage." Moses says this before the people enter the la
 nd without him.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20261223@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261223
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261224
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 6:6
DESCRIPTION:וְהָיוּ הַדְּבָרִים הָאֵלֶּה אֲ
 שֶׁר אָנֹכִי מְצַוְּךָ הַיּוֹם עַל־לְבָ
 בֶךָ׃\nVehayu hadevarim ha'eleh asher anokhi metzavekha hayom al-leva
 vekha\nAnd these words\, which I command thee this day\, shall be upon thy
  heart\;\n\n"These words shall be upon your heart." Learning Torah is mean
 t to go deeper than memory\, into who we are.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-
 review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20261224@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261224
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261225
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 31:16
DESCRIPTION:וְשָׁמְרוּ בְנֵי־יִשְׂרָאֵל אֶת־
 הַשַּׁבָּת לַעֲשׂוֹת אֶת־הַשַּׁבָּת לְ
 דֹרֹתָם בְּרִית עוֹלָם׃\nVeshamru venei-Yisra'el et-h
 ashabat la'asot et-hashabat ledorotam berit olam\nWherefore the children o
 f Israel shall keep the sabbath\, to observe the sabbath throughout their 
 generations\, for a perpetual covenant.\n\nV'shamru: the people of Israel 
 shall keep the Shabbat for all generations. This verse is sung on Friday n
 ight and Shabbat morning.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/
 #/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20261225@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261225
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261226
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 34:10
DESCRIPTION:וְלֹא־קָם נָבִיא עוֹד בְּיִשְׂרָ
 אֵל כְּמֹשֶׁה אֲשֶׁר יְדָעוֹ יְהוָה פָּ
 נִים אֶל־פָּנִים׃\nVelo-kam navi od beyisra'el kemosheh as
 her yeda'o Adonai panim el-panim\nAnd there hath not arisen a prophet sinc
 e in Israel like unto Moses\, whom the LORD knew face to face\;\n\nNear th
 e very end of the Torah: no prophet arose like Moses\, who knew God face t
 o face. Then we roll the scroll back and start again.\n\nOpen Aleph: https
 ://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20261226@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261226
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261227
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 1:1
DESCRIPTION:בְּרֵאשִׁית בָּרָא אֱלֹהִים אֵת 
 הַשָּׁמַיִם וְאֵת הָאָרֶץ׃\nBereshit bara Elohim e
 t hashamayim ve'et ha'aretz\nIn the beginning God created the heaven and t
 he earth.\n\nThe Torah opens with its first word\, Bereshit\, "in the begi
 nning." Everything that follows starts here: the world has a Maker\, and i
 t did not come about by chance.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrende
 r.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20261227@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261227
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261228
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 1:3
DESCRIPTION:וַיֹּאמֶר אֱלֹהִים יְהִי אוֹר וַ
 יְהִי־אוֹר׃\nVayomer Elohim yehi or vayhi-or\nAnd God said: ‘
 Let there be light.’ And there was light.\n\nThe first thing God makes i
 s light\, and He makes it with words. In Judaism speech has real power\, s
 o the words we choose each day matter.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.
 onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20261228@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261228
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261229
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 1:27
DESCRIPTION:וַיִּבְרָא אֱלֹהִים אֶת־הָאָדָם 
 בְּצַלְמוֹ בְּצֶלֶם אֱלֹהִים בָּרָא אֹת
 וֹ זָכָר וּנְקֵבָה בָּרָא אֹתָם׃\nVayivra Eloh
 im et-ha'adam betzalmo betzelem Elohim bara oto zakhar unekevah bara otam\
 nAnd God created man in His own image\, in the image of God created He him
 \; male and female created He them.\n\nEvery person is made in the image o
 f God. That is why each human life has worth\, whoever the person is and w
 herever they come from.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/
 morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20261229@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261229
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261230
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 1:31
DESCRIPTION:וַיַּרְא אֱלֹהִים אֶת־כָּל־אֲשֶׁ
 ר עָשָׂה וְהִנֵּה־טוֹב מְאֹד וַיְהִי־עֶ
 רֶב וַיְהִי־בֹקֶר יוֹם הַשִּׁשִּׁי׃\nVayar
  Elohim et-kol-asher asah vehineh-tov me'od vayhi-erev vayhi-voker yom has
 hishi\nAnd God saw every thing that He had made\, and\, behold\, it was ve
 ry good. And there was evening and there was morning\, the sixth day.\n\nA
 fter each day God saw that it was good. On the sixth day\, with people in 
 the world\, it became "very good." Look for the good in your own day.\n\nO
 pen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20261230@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261230
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261231
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 2:3
DESCRIPTION:וַיְבָרֶךְ אֱלֹהִים אֶת־יוֹם הַ
 שְּׁבִיעִי וַיְקַדֵּשׁ אֹתוֹ כִּי בוֹ 
 שָׁבַת מִכָּל־מְלַאכְתּוֹ אֲשֶׁר־בָּרָ
 א אֱלֹהִים לַעֲשׂוֹת׃\nVayvarekh Elohim et-yom hashevi'
 i vaykadesh oto ki vo shavat mikol-melakhto asher-bara Elohim la'asot\nAnd
  God blessed the seventh day\, and hallowed it\; because that in it He res
 ted from all His work which God in creating had made.\n\nThis is the first
  Shabbat. God rested on the seventh day and made it holy\, and we rest on 
 it too. Shabbat is a gift of time\, not only a rule.\n\nOpen Aleph: https:
 //alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20261231@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261231
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270101
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 2:15
DESCRIPTION:וַיִּקַּח יְהוָה אֱלֹהִים אֶת־הָ
 אָדָם וַיַּנִּחֵהוּ בְגַן־עֵדֶן לְעָבְ
 דָהּ וּלְשָׁמְרָהּ׃\nVayikach Adonai Elohim et-ha'adam v
 ayanichehu vegan-eden le'avedah uleshamerah\nAnd the LORD God took the man
 \, and put him into the garden of Eden to dress it and to keep it.\n\nAdam
  was put in the garden to work it and to guard it. The earth is placed in 
 our care\, and looking after it is part of our job.\n\nOpen Aleph: https:/
 /alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270101@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270101
