UID:aleph-torah-20270108@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270108
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270109
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 12:1
DESCRIPTION:וַיֹּאמֶר יְהוָה אֶל־אַבְרָם לֶךְ
 ־לְךָ מֵאַרְצְךָ וּמִמּוֹלַדְתְּךָ וּ
 מִבֵּית אָבִיךָ אֶל־הָאָרֶץ אֲשֶׁר אַרְ
 אֶךָּ׃\nVayomer Adonai el-Avram lekh-lekha me'artzekha umimoladtekha
  umibeit avikha el-ha'aretz asher ar'eka\nNow the LORD said unto Abram: 
 ‘Get thee out of thy country\, and from thy kindred\, and from thy fathe
 r’s house\, unto the land that I will show thee.\n\nLech lecha: "go for 
 yourself." Abraham leaves everything familiar to follow God. Every new sta
 rt\, including learning Hebrew\, takes a first step like this.\n\nOpen Ale
 ph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270109@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270109
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270110
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 12:2
DESCRIPTION:וְאֶעֶשְׂךָ לְגוֹי גָּדוֹל וַאֲבָ
 רֶכְךָ וַאֲגַדְּלָה שְׁמֶךָ וֶהְיֵה בְּ
 רָכָה׃\nVe'e'eskha legoy gadol va'avarekhkha va'agadelah shemekha ve
 hyeh berakhah\nAnd I will make of thee a great nation\, and I will bless t
 hee\, and make thy name great\; and be thou a blessing.\n\nAbraham is told
  not only that he will be blessed but that he will be a blessing. A good l
 ife is one that brings good to others.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.
 onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270110@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270110
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270111
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 15:5
DESCRIPTION:וַיּוֹצֵא אֹתוֹ הַחוּצָה וַיֹּאמֶ
 ר הַבֶּט־נָא הַשָּׁמַיְמָה וּסְפֹר הַכּ
 וֹכָבִים אִם־תּוּכַל לִסְפֹּר אֹתָם וַ
 יֹּאמֶר לוֹ כֹּה יִהְיֶה זַרְעֶךָ׃\nVayotze 
 oto hachutzah vayomer habet-na hashamaymah usefor hakokhavim im-tukhal lis
 por otam vayomer lo koh yihyeh zar'ekha\nAnd He brought him forth abroad\,
  and said: ‘Look now toward heaven\, and count the stars\, if thou be ab
 le to count them’\; and He said unto him: ‘So shall thy seed be.’\n\
 nGod takes Abraham outside to count the stars. When things feel small or u
 ncertain\, step back and look at the bigger picture.\n\nOpen Aleph: https:
 //alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270111@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270111
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270112
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 18:25
DESCRIPTION:חָלִלָה לְּךָ מֵעֲשֹׂת כַּדָּבָר 
 הַזֶּה לְהָמִית צַדִּיק עִם־רָשָׁע וְהָ
 יָה כַצַדִּיק כָּרָשָׁע חָלִלָה לָּךְ 
 הֲשֹׁפֵט כָּל־הָאָרֶץ לֹא יַעֲשֶׂה מִ
 שְׁפָּט׃\nChalilah lekha me'asot kadavar hazeh lehamit tzadik im-r
 asha vehayah khatzadik karasha chalilah lakh hashofet kol-ha'aretz lo ya'a
 seh mishpat\nThat be far from Thee to do after this manner\, to slay the r
 ighteous with the wicked\, that so the righteous should be as the wicked\;
  that be far from Thee\; shall not the judge of all the earth do justly?
 ’\n\nAbraham argues with God to save the people of Sodom. In Jewish trad
 ition it is right to speak up for justice\, even before the highest author
 ity.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270112@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270112
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270113
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 28:15
DESCRIPTION:וְהִנֵּה אָנֹכִי עִמָּךְ וּשְׁמַ
 רְתִּיךָ בְּכֹל אֲשֶׁר־תֵּלֵךְ וַהֲשִׁ
 בֹתִיךָ אֶל־הָאֲדָמָה הַזֹּאת כִּי לֹא 
 אֶעֱזָבְךָ עַד אֲשֶׁר אִם־עָשִׂיתִי אֵת
  אֲשֶׁר־דִּבַּרְתִּי לָךְ׃\nVehineh anokhi imakh u
 shemartikha bekhol asher-telekh vahashivotikha el-ha'adamah hazot ki lo e'
 ezavekha ad asher im-asiti et asher-dibarti lakh\nAnd\, behold\, I am with
  thee\, and will keep thee whithersoever thou goest\, and will bring thee 
 back into this land\; for I will not leave thee\, until I have done that w
 hich I have spoken to thee of.’\n\nJacob is alone and running away\, and
  God promises: I am with you\, wherever you go. You are never as alone as 
 you feel.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270113@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270113
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270114
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 28:16
DESCRIPTION:וַיִּיקַץ יַעֲקֹב מִשְּׁנָתוֹ וַ
 יֹּאמֶר אָכֵן יֵשׁ יְהוָה בַּמָּקוֹם הַ
 זֶּה וְאָנֹכִי לֹא יָדָעְתִּי׃\nVayikatz Ya'ako
 v mishenato vayomer akhen yesh Adonai bamakom hazeh ve'anokhi lo yada'eti\
 nAnd Jacob awaked out of his sleep\, and he said: ‘Surely the LORD is in
  this place\; and I knew it not.’\n\nJacob wakes from his dream and says
  God was in this place and he did not know it. Holiness can be right where
  you are\, if you notice it.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.c
 om/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270114@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270114
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270115
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 32:11
DESCRIPTION:קָטֹנְתִּי מִכֹּל הַחֲסָדִים וּמִ
 כָּל־הָאֱמֶת אֲשֶׁר עָשִׂיתָ אֶת־עַבְ
 דֶּךָ כִּי בְמַקְלִי עָבַרְתִּי אֶת־הַ
 יַּרְדֵּן הַזֶּה וְעַתָּה הָיִיתִי לִ
 שְׁנֵי מַחֲנוֹת׃\nKatoneti mikol hachasadim umikol-ha'emet 
 asher asita et-avdekha ki vemakli avarti et-hayarden hazeh ve'atah hayiti 
 lishnei machanot\nI am not worthy of all the mercies\, and of all the trut
 h\, which Thou hast shown unto Thy servant\; for with my staff I passed ov
 er this Jordan\; and now I am become two camps.\n\nBefore meeting his brot
 her Esau\, Jacob says he is not worthy of all the kindness he has received
 . Gratitude and humility go together.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.o
 nrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270115@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270115
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270116
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 45:4
DESCRIPTION:וַיֹּאמֶר יוֹסֵף אֶל־אֶחָיו גְּשׁ
 וּ־נָא אֵלַי וַיִּגָּשׁוּ וַיֹּאמֶר אֲ
 נִי יוֹסֵף אֲחִיכֶם אֲשֶׁר־מְכַרְתֶּם 
 אֹתִי מִצְרָיְמָה׃\nVayomer yosef el-echav geshu-na elai 
 vayigashu vayomer ani yosef achikhem asher-mekhartem oti mitzrayemah\nAnd 
 Joseph said unto his brethren: ‘Come near to me\, I pray you.’ And the
 y came near. And he said: ‘I am Joseph your brother\, whom ye sold into 
 Egypt.\n\nJoseph says to the brothers who sold him\, "Come close to me." I
 t is one of the great moments of forgiveness in the Torah.\n\nOpen Aleph: 
 https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270116@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270116
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270117
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 50:20
DESCRIPTION:וְאַתֶּם חֲשַׁבְתֶּם עָלַי רָעָה 
 אֱלֹהִים חֲשָׁבָהּ לְטֹבָה לְמַעַן עֲ
 שֹׂה כַּיּוֹם הַזֶּה לְהַחֲיֹת עַם־רָב׃
 \nVe'atem chashavtem alai ra'ah Elohim chashavah letovah lema'an asoh kayo
 m hazeh lehachayot am-rav\nAnd as for you\, ye meant evil against me\; but
  God meant it for good\, to bring to pass\, as it is this day\, to save mu
 ch people alive.\n\nJoseph tells his brothers that what they meant for har
 m\, God turned to good. Hard chapters of a life can lead somewhere good.\n
 \nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270117@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270117
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270118
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 3:5
DESCRIPTION:וַיֹּאמֶר אַל־תִּקְרַב הֲלֹם שַׁל
 ־נְעָלֶיךָ מֵעַל רַגְלֶיךָ כִּי הַמָּק
 וֹם אֲשֶׁר אַתָּה עוֹמֵד עָלָיו אַדְמַת
 ־קֹדֶשׁ הוּא׃\nVayomer al-tikrav halom shal-ne'alekha me'al ra
 glekha ki hamakom asher atah omed alav admat-kodesh hu\nAnd He said: ‘Dr
 aw not nigh hither\; put off thy shoes from off thy feet\, for the place w
 hereon thou standest is holy ground.’\n\nAt the burning bush Moses is to
 ld to take off his shoes\, because the ground is holy. Some moments call f
 or us to slow down and pay attention.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.o
 nrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270118@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270118
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270119
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 3:14
DESCRIPTION:וַיֹּאמֶר אֱלֹהִים אֶל־מֹשֶׁה אֶ
 הְיֶה אֲשֶׁר אֶהְיֶה וַיֹּאמֶר כֹּה תֹא
 מַר לִבְנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל אֶהְיֶה שְׁלָחַ
 נִי אֲלֵיכֶם׃\nVayomer Elohim el-Mosheh ehyeh asher ehyeh vayo
 mer koh tomar livnei Yisra'el ehyeh shelachani aleikhem\nAnd God said unto
  Moses: ‘I AM THAT I AM’\; and He said: ‘Thus shalt thou say unto th
 e children of Israel: I AM hath sent me unto you.’\n\nEhyeh asher ehyeh:
  "I will be what I will be." God's name here is about being present\, in e
 very time and place.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/mor
 ning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270119@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270119
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270120
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 13:8
DESCRIPTION:וְהִגַּדְתָּ לְבִנְךָ בַּיּוֹם הַ
 הוּא לֵאמֹר בַּעֲבוּר זֶה עָשָׂה יְהוָה 
 לִי בְּצֵאתִי מִמִּצְרָיִם׃\nVehigadta levinkha b
 ayom hahu lemor ba'avur zeh asah Adonai li betzeti mimitzrayim\nAnd thou s
 halt tell thy son in that day\, saying: It is because of that which the LO
 RD did for me when I came forth out of Egypt.\n\nThis verse is why we tell
  the Passover story at the Seder. Each generation tells it as if it happen
 ed to them.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270120@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270120
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270121
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 14:14
DESCRIPTION:יְהוָה יִלָּחֵם לָכֶם וְאַתֶּם 
 תַּחֲרִישׁוּן׃\nAdonai yilachem lakhem ve'atem tacharishun\n
 The LORD will fight for you\, and ye shall hold your peace.’\n\nAt the S
 ea of Reeds\, Moses tells the frightened people that God will fight for th
 em. Sometimes the right move is to stay calm and trust.\n\nOpen Aleph: htt
 ps://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270121@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270121
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270122
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 15:2
DESCRIPTION:עָזִּי וְזִמְרָת יָהּ וַיְהִי־לִי
  לִישׁוּעָה זֶה אֵלִי וְאַנְוֵהוּ אֱלֹ
 הֵי אָבִי וַאֲרֹמְמֶנְהוּ׃\nAzi vezimrat yah vayhi
 -li lishu'ah zeh eli ve'anvehu elohei avi va'aromemenhu\nThe LORD is my st
 rength and song\, And He is become my salvation\; This is my God\, and I w
 ill glorify Him\; My father’s God\, and I will exalt Him.\n\nFrom the So
 ng at the Sea: "The Lord is my strength and my song." These words are sung
  in synagogue every morning.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.c
 om/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270122@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270122
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270123
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 15:11
DESCRIPTION:מִי־כָמֹכָה בָּאֵלִם יְהוָה מִי 
 כָּמֹכָה נֶאְדָּר בַּקֹּדֶשׁ נוֹרָא תְ
 הִלֹּת עֹשֵׂה פֶלֶא׃\nMi-khamokhah ba'elim Adonai mi kam
 okhah nedar bakodesh nora tehilot oseh fele\nWho is like unto Thee\, O LOR
 D\, among the mighty? Who is like unto Thee\, glorious in holiness\, Fearf
 ul in praises\, doing wonders?\n\nMi chamocha\, "Who is like You?" This li
 ne from the Song at the Sea is part of the daily prayers\, just after the 
 Shema.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270123@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270123
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270124
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 19:6
DESCRIPTION:וְאַתֶּם תִּהְיוּ־לִי מַמְלֶכֶת 
 כֹּהֲנִים וְגוֹי קָדוֹשׁ אֵלֶּה הַדְּבָ
 רִים אֲשֶׁר תְּדַבֵּר אֶל־בְּנֵי יִשְׂ
 רָאֵל׃\nVe'atem tihyu-li mamlekhet kohanim vegoy kadosh eleh hadevar
 im asher tedaber el-benei Yisra'el\nand ye shall be unto Me a kingdom of p
 riests\, and a holy nation. These are the words which thou shalt speak unt
 o the children of Israel.’\n\nAt Sinai the whole people is called a king
 dom of priests and a holy nation. Holiness is meant for everyone\, not onl
 y for a few.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270124@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270124
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270125
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 20:2
DESCRIPTION:אָנֹכִי יְהוָה אֱלֹהֶיךָ אֲשֶׁר ה
 וֹצֵאתִיךָ מֵאֶרֶץ מִצְרַיִם מִבֵּית עֲ
 בָדִים׃\nAnokhi Adonai Elohekha asher hotzetikha me'eretz Mitzrayim
  mibeit avadim\nI am the LORD thy God\, who brought thee out of the land o
 f Egypt\, out of the house of bondage.\n\nThe Ten Commandments begin with 
 who God is: the One who brought us out of slavery. Freedom comes first\, a
 nd the commandments follow.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.co
 m/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270125@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270125
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270126
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 20:8
DESCRIPTION:זָכוֹר אֶת־יוֹם הַשַׁבָּת לְקַדְּ
 שׁוֹ\nZakhor et-yom hashabat lekadesho\nRemember the sabbath day\, to 
 keep it holy.\n\nZachor: "Remember the Shabbat day." We remember it with c
 andles\, Kiddush\, rest and time with the people we love.\n\nOpen Aleph: h
 ttps://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270126@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270126
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270127
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 20:12
DESCRIPTION:כַּבֵּד אֶת־אָבִיךָ וְאֶת־אִמֶּ
 ךָ לְמַעַן יַאֲרִכוּן יָמֶיךָ עַל הָאֲ
 דָמָה אֲשֶׁר־יְהוָה אֱלֹהֶיךָ נֹתֵן לָ
 ךְ׃\nKabed et-avikha ve'et-imekha lema'an ya'arikhun yamekha al ha'adam
 ah asher-Adonai Elohekha noten lakh\nHonour thy father and thy mother\, th
 at thy days may be long upon the land which the LORD thy God giveth thee.\
 n\nHonour your father and your mother. It is one of the Ten Commandments\,
  and the first that comes with a promise of long life.\n\nOpen Aleph: http
 s://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270127@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270127
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270128
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 22:20
DESCRIPTION:וְגֵר לֹא־תוֹנֶה וְלֹא תִלְחָצֶנּ
 וּ כִּי־גֵרִים הֱיִיתֶם בְּאֶרֶץ מִצְרָ
 יִם׃\nVeger lo-toneh velo tilchatzenu ki-gerim heyitem be'eretz Mitzra
 yim\nAnd a stranger shalt thou not wrong\, neither shalt thou oppress him\
 ; for ye were strangers in the land of Egypt.\n\nDo not wrong the stranger
 \, because you were strangers in Egypt. This idea comes up again and again
  in the Torah.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270128@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270128
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270129
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 23:2
DESCRIPTION:לֹא־תִהְיֶה אַחֲרֵי־רַבִּים לְרָ
 עֹת וְלֹא־תַעֲנֶה עַל־רִב לִנְטֹת אַחֲ
 רֵי רַבִּים לְהַטֹּת׃\nLo-tihyeh acharei-rabim lera'ot 
 velo-ta'aneh al-riv lintot acharei rabim lehatot\nThou shalt not follow a 
 multitude to do evil\; neither shalt thou bear witness in a cause to turn 
 aside after a multitude to pervert justice\;\n\nDo not follow the crowd to
  do wrong. Doing the right thing sometimes means standing apart.\n\nOpen A
 leph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270129@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270129
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270130
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 23:9
DESCRIPTION:וְגֵר לֹא תִלְחָץ וְאַתֶּם יְדַעְ
 תֶּם אֶת־נֶפֶשׁ הַגֵּר כִּי־גֵרִים הֱיִ
 יתֶם בְּאֶרֶץ מִצְרָיִם׃\nVeger lo tilchatz ve'atem 
 yedatem et-nefesh hager ki-gerim heyitem be'eretz Mitzrayim\nAnd a strange
 r shalt thou not oppress\; for ye know the heart of a stranger\, seeing ye
  were strangers in the land of Egypt.\n\n"You know the heart of the strang
 er." Our own history should make us kind to newcomers.\n\nOpen Aleph: http
 s://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270130@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270130
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270131
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 25:8
DESCRIPTION:וְעָשׂוּ לִי מִקְדָּשׁ וְשָׁכַנְ
 תִּי בְּתוֹכָם׃\nVe'asu li mikdash veshakhanti betokham\nAnd
  let them make Me a sanctuary\, that I may dwell among them.\n\n"Make Me a
  sanctuary\, and I will dwell among them." Not "in it\," but among them: G
 od lives among people\, in the places they make holy.\n\nOpen Aleph: https
 ://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270131@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270131
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270201
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 33:13
DESCRIPTION:וְעַתָּה אִם־נָא מָצָאתִי חֵן בְּ
 עֵינֶיךָ הוֹדִעֵנִי נָא אֶת־דְּרָכֶךָ 
 וְאֵדָעֲךָ לְמַעַן אֶמְצָא־חֵן בְּעֵי
 נֶיךָ וּרְאֵה כִּי עַמְּךָ הַגּוֹי הַ
 זֶּה׃\nVe'atah im-na matzati chen be'einekha hodi'eni na et-derakhekh
 a ve'eda'akha lema'an emtza-chen be'einekha ure'eh ki amekha hagoy hazeh\n
 Now therefore\, I pray Thee\, if I have found grace in Thy sight\, show me
  now Thy ways\, that I may know Thee\, to the end that I may find grace in
  Thy sight\; and consider that this nation is Thy people.’\n\nMoses asks
  God\, "Show me Your ways\, so that I may know You." Learning is one of th
 e ways Jews come close to God.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender
 .com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270201@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270201
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270202
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 34:6
DESCRIPTION:וַיַּעֲבֹר יְהוָה עַל־פָּנָיו וַ
 יִּקְרָא יְהוָה יְהוָה אֵל רַחוּם וְחַ
 נּוּן אֶרֶךְ אַפַּיִם וְרַב־חֶסֶד וֶאֱ
 מֶת\nVaya'avor Adonai al-panav vayikra Adonai Adonai el rachum vechanun
  erekh apayim verav-chesed ve'emet\nAnd the LORD passed by before him\, an
 d proclaimed: ‘The LORD\, the LORD\, God\, merciful and gracious\, long-
 suffering\, and abundant in goodness and truth\;\n\nThese are God's qualit
 ies of mercy\, sung on the High Holy Days: compassionate\, gracious\, slow
  to anger\, full of kindness and truth.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review
 .onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270202@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270202
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270203
SUMMARY:Torah: Leviticus 19:2
DESCRIPTION:דַּבֵּר אֶל־כָּל־עֲדַת בְּנֵי־יִ
 שְׂרָאֵל וְאָמַרְתָּ אֲלֵהֶם קְדֹשִׁים 
 תִּהְיוּ כִּי קָדוֹשׁ אֲנִי יְהוָה אֱלֹ
 הֵיכֶם׃\nDaber el-kol-adat benei-Yisra'el ve'amarta alehem kedoshim
  tihyu ki kadosh ani Adonai Eloheikhem\nSpeak unto all the congregation of
  the children of Israel\, and say unto them: Ye shall be holy\; for I the 
 LORD your God am holy.\n\n"You shall be holy\, for I am holy." The chapter
  that follows shows what that means: honesty\, kindness and fairness in ev
 eryday life.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270203@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270203
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270204
SUMMARY:Torah: Leviticus 19:3
DESCRIPTION:אִישׁ אִמּוֹ וְאָבִיו תִּירָאוּ 
 וְאֶת־שַׁבְּתֹתַי תִּשְׁמֹרוּ אֲנִי יְ
 הוָה אֱלֹהֵיכֶם׃\nIsh imo ve'aviv tira'u ve'et-shabetotai t
 ishmoru ani Adonai Eloheikhem\nYe shall fear every man his mother\, and hi
 s father\, and ye shall keep My sabbaths: I am the LORD your God.\n\nRespe
 ct your parents and keep Shabbat. Both are about honouring where we come f
 rom.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270204@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270204
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270205
SUMMARY:Torah: Leviticus 19:9
DESCRIPTION:וּבְקֻצְרְכֶם אֶת־קְצִיר אַרְצְ
 כֶם לֹא תְכַלֶּה פְּאַת שָׂדְךָ לִקְצֹר 
 וְלֶקֶט קְצִירְךָ לֹא תְלַקֵּט׃\nUvekutzrekhem
  et-ketzir artzekhem lo tekhaleh pe'at sadekha liktzor veleket ketzirekha 
 lo telaket\nAnd when ye reap the harvest of your land\, thou shalt not who
 lly reap the corner of thy field\, neither shalt thou gather the gleaning 
 of thy harvest.\n\nLeave the corners of your field for people in need. Giv
 ing to others is built right into how we earn and spend.\n\nOpen Aleph: ht
 tps://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270205@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270205
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270206
SUMMARY:Torah: Leviticus 19:14
DESCRIPTION:לֹא־תְקַלֵּל חֵרֵשׁ וְלִפְנֵי עִ
 וֵּר לֹא תִתֵּן מִכְשֹׁל וְיָרֵאתָ מֵּ
 אֱלֹהֶיךָ אֲנִי יְהוָה׃\nLo-tekalel cheresh velifnei 
 iver lo titen mikhshol veyareta me'Elohekha ani Adonai\nThou shalt not cur
 se the deaf\, nor put a stumbling-block before the blind\, but thou shalt 
 fear thy God: I am the LORD.\n\nDo not curse the deaf or put a stumbling b
 lock before the blind. Treat everyone with care\, especially those who can
 not defend themselves.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/m
 orning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270206@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270206
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270207
SUMMARY:Torah: Leviticus 19:16
DESCRIPTION:לֹא־תֵלֵךְ רָכִיל בְּעַמֶּיךָ לֹא
  תַעֲמֹד עַל־דַּם רֵעֶךָ אֲנִי יְהוָה׃\nL
 o-telekh rakhil be'amekha lo ta'amod al-dam re'ekha ani Adonai\nThou shalt
  not go up and down as a talebearer among thy people\; neither shalt thou 
 stand idly by the blood of thy neighbour: I am the LORD.\n\nDo not spread 
 gossip\, and do not stand by while your neighbour is in danger. Words can 
 hurt\, and silence can too.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.co
 m/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270207@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270207
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270208
SUMMARY:Torah: Leviticus 19:18
DESCRIPTION:לֹא־תִקֹּם וְלֹא־תִטֹּר אֶת־בְּ
 נֵי עַמֶּךָ וְאָהַבְתָּ לְרֵעֲךָ כָּמוֹ
 ךָ אֲנִי יְהוָה׃\nLo-tikom velo-titor et-benei amekha ve'aha
 vta lere'akha kamokha ani Adonai\nThou shalt not take vengeance\, nor bear
  any grudge against the children of thy people\, but thou shalt love thy n
 eighbour as thyself: I am the LORD.\n\n"Love your neighbour as yourself." 
 Rabbi Akiva called this the great principle of the whole Torah.\n\nOpen Al
 eph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270208@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270208
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270209
SUMMARY:Torah: Leviticus 19:32
DESCRIPTION:מִפְּנֵי שֵׂיבָה תָּקוּם וְהָדַרְ
 תָּ פְּנֵי זָקֵן וְיָרֵאתָ מֵּאֱלֹהֶיךָ
  אֲנִי יְהוָה׃\nMipenei seivah takum vehadarta penei zaken vey
 areta me'Elohekha ani Adonai\nThou shalt rise up before the hoary head\, a
 nd honour the face of the old man\, and thou shalt fear thy God: I am the 
 LORD.\n\nRise before the elderly and honour them. Age brings wisdom\, and 
 the Torah asks us to show it respect.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.o
 nrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270209@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270209
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270210
SUMMARY:Torah: Leviticus 25:10
DESCRIPTION:וְקִדַּשְׁתֶּם אֵת שְׁנַת הַחֲמִ
 שִּׁים שָׁנָה וּקְרָאתֶם דְּרוֹר בָּאָ
 רֶץ לְכָל־יֹשְׁבֶיהָ יוֹבֵל הִוא תִּהְ
 יֶה לָכֶם וְשַׁבְתֶּם אִישׁ אֶל־אֲחֻזָּ
 תוֹ וְאִישׁ אֶל־מִשְׁפַּחְתּוֹ תָּשֻׁב
 וּ׃\nVekidashtem et shenat hachamishim shanah ukeratem deror ba'aretz l
 ekhol-yosheveha yovel hiv tihyeh lakhem veshavtem ish el-achuzato ve'ish e
 l-mishpachto tashuvu\nAnd ye shall hallow the fiftieth year\, and proclaim
  liberty throughout the land unto all the inhabitants thereof\; it shall b
 e a jubilee unto you\; and ye shall return every man unto his possession\,
  and ye shall return every man unto his family.\n\n"Proclaim liberty throu
 ghout the land." These words about the Jubilee year are cast on the Libert
 y Bell in Philadelphia.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/
 morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270210@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270210
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270211
SUMMARY:Torah: Numbers 6:24
DESCRIPTION:יְבָרֶכְךָ יְהוָה וְיִשְׁמְרֶךָ׃\
 nYevarekhkha Adonai veyishmerekha\nThe LORD bless thee\, and keep thee\;\n
 \nThe first line of the Priestly Blessing\, still said in synagogues and b
 y parents to children on Friday night.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.
 onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270211@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270211
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270212
SUMMARY:Torah: Numbers 6:26
DESCRIPTION:יִשָּׂא יְהוָה פָּנָיו אֵלֶיךָ וְ
 יָשֵׂם לְךָ שָׁלוֹם׃\nYisa Adonai panav elekha veyasem l
 ekha shalom\nThe LORD lift up His countenance upon thee\, and give thee pe
 ace.\n\nThe Priestly Blessing ends with shalom\, peace. In Hebrew\, shalom
  also means wholeness: everything in its right place.\n\nOpen Aleph: https
 ://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270212@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270212
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270213
SUMMARY:Torah: Numbers 11:29
DESCRIPTION:וַיֹּאמֶר לוֹ מֹשֶׁה הַמְקַנֵּא 
 אַתָּה לִי וּמִי יִתֵּן כָּל־עַם יְהוָה 
 נְבִיאִים כִּי־יִתֵּן יְהוָה אֶת־רוּח
 וֹ עֲלֵיהֶם׃\nVayomer lo Mosheh hamkane atah li umi yiten kol-a
 m Adonai nevi'im ki-yiten Adonai et-rucho aleihem\nAnd Moses said unto him
 : ‘Art thou jealous for my sake? would that all the LORD’S people were
  prophets\, that the LORD would put His spirit upon them! ’\n\nWhen othe
 rs begin to prophesy\, Moses is not jealous. He wishes everyone could shar
 e God's spirit. Great leaders lift others up.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-
 review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270213@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270213
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270214
SUMMARY:Torah: Numbers 15:39
DESCRIPTION:וְהָיָה לָכֶם לְצִיצִת וּרְאִיתֶם
  אֹתוֹ וּזְכַרְתֶּם אֶת־כָּל־מִצְוֹת יְ
 הוָה וַעֲשִׂיתֶם אֹתָם וְלֹא־תָתֻרוּ אַ
 חֲרֵי לְבַבְכֶם וְאַחֲרֵי עֵינֵיכֶם אֲ
 שֶׁר־אַתֶּם זֹנִים אַחֲרֵיהֶם׃\nVehayah lakhem
  letzitzit ure'item oto uzekhartem et-kol-mitzvot Adonai va'asitem otam ve
 lo-taturu acharei levavkhem ve'acharei eineikhem asher-atem zonim achareih
 em\nAnd it shall be unto you for a fringe\, that ye may look upon it\, and
  remember all the commandments of the LORD\, and do them\; and that ye go 
 not about after your own heart and your own eyes\, after which ye use to g
 o astray\;\n\nThis verse is about the tzitzit\, the fringes on the tallit.
  Seeing them is a reminder of the commandments and of who we want to be.\n
 \nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270214@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270214
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270215
SUMMARY:Torah: Numbers 24:5
DESCRIPTION:מַה־טֹּבוּ אֹהָלֶיךָ יַעֲקֹב מִ
 שְׁכְּנֹתֶיךָ יִשְׂרָאֵל׃\nMah-tovu ohalekha Ya'ak
 ov mishkenotekha Yisra'el\nHow goodly are thy tents\, O Jacob\, Thy dwelli
 ngs\, O Israel!\n\nMah tovu\, "How good are your tents." Many synagogues o
 pen the morning service with these words.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-revi
 ew.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270215@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270215
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270216
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 4:9
DESCRIPTION:רַק הִשָּׁמֶר לְךָ וּשְׁמֹר נַפְ
 שְׁךָ מְאֹד פֶּן־תִּשְׁכַּח אֶת־הַדְּ
 בָרִים אֲשֶׁר־רָאוּ עֵינֶיךָ וּפֶן־יָס
 וּרוּ מִלְּבָבְךָ כֹּל יְמֵי חַיֶּיךָ 
 וְהוֹדַעְתָּם לְבָנֶיךָ וְלִבְנֵי בָנֶ
 יךָ׃\nRak hishamer lekha ushemor nafshekha me'od pen-tishkach et-hadev
 arim asher-ra'u einekha ufen-yasuru milevavekha kol yemei chayekha vehodat
 am levanekha velivnei vanekha\nOnly take heed to thyself\, and keep thy so
 ul diligently\, lest thou forget the things which thine eyes saw\, and les
 t they depart from thy heart all the days of thy life\; but make them know
 n unto thy children and thy children’s children\;\n\nDo not forget what 
 you have seen\, and teach it to your children and grandchildren. Memory is
  how a people stays alive.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com
 /#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270216@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270216
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270217
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 6:4
DESCRIPTION:שְׁמַע יִשְׂרָאֵל יְהוָה אֱלֹהֵינ
 וּ יְהוָה אֶחָד׃\nShema Yisra'el Adonai Eloheinu Adonai echa
 d\nHEAR\, O ISRAEL: THE LORD OUR GOD\, THE LORD IS ONE.\n\nThe Shema\, the
  central line of Jewish prayer: "Hear\, O Israel\, the Lord is our God\, t
 he Lord is One." It is said morning and night.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef
 -review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270217@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270217
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270218
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 6:5
DESCRIPTION:וְאָהַבְתָּ אֵת יְהוָה אֱלֹהֶיךָ 
 בְּכָל־לְבָבְךָ וּבְכָל־נַפְשְׁךָ וּבְ
 כָל־מְאֹדֶךָ׃\nVe'ahavta et Adonai Elohekha bekhol-levavekha 
 uvekhol-nafshekha uvekhol-me'odekha\nAnd thou shalt love the LORD thy God 
 with all thy heart\, and with all thy soul\, and with all thy might.\n\nV'
 ahavta: love God with all your heart\, all your soul and all your strength
 . Faith in Judaism is about love\, not only belief.\n\nOpen Aleph: https:/
 /alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270218@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270218
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270219
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 6:7
DESCRIPTION:וְשִׁנַּנְתָּם לְבָנֶיךָ וְדִבַּ
 רְתָּ בָּם בְּשִׁבְתְּךָ בְּבֵיתֶךָ וּ
 בְלֶכְתְּךָ בַדֶּרֶךְ וּבְשָׁכְבְּךָ 
 וּבְקוּמֶךָ׃\nVeshinantam levanekha vedibarta bam beshivtekha 
 beveitekha uvelekhtekha vaderekh uveshakhbekha uvekumekha\nand thou shalt 
 teach them diligently unto thy children\, and shalt talk of them when thou
  sittest in thy house\, and when thou walkest by the way\, and when thou l
 iest down\, and when thou risest up.\n\nTalk about these words at home\, o
 n the road\, when you lie down and when you get up. That is why the Shema 
 is said at bedtime and in the morning.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.
 onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270219@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270219
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270220
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 8:3
DESCRIPTION:וַיְעַנְּךָ וַיַּרְעִבֶךָ וַיַּ
 אֲכִלְךָ אֶת הַמָּן אֲשֶׁר לֹא־יָדַעְ
 תָּ וְלֹא יָדְעוּן אֲבֹתֶיךָ לְמַעַן ה
 וֹדִעֲךָ כִּי לֹא עַל־הַלֶּחֶם לְבַדּוֹ
  יִחְיֶה הָאָדָם כִּי עַל־כָּל־מוֹצָא 
 פִי־יְהוָה יִחְיֶה הָאָדָם׃\nVay'anekha vayar'ive
 kha vaya'akhilkha et haman asher lo-yadata velo yad'un avotekha lema'an ho
 di'akha ki lo al-halechem levado yichyeh ha'adam ki al-kol-motza fi-Adonai
  yichyeh ha'adam\nAnd He afflicted thee\, and suffered thee to hunger\, an
 d fed thee with manna\, which thou knewest not\, neither did thy fathers k
 now\; that He might make thee know that man doth not live by bread only\, 
 but by every thing that proceedeth out of the mouth of the LORD doth man l
 ive.\n\n"A person does not live by bread alone." We need meaning\, learnin
 g and purpose as much as food.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender
 .com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270220@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270220
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270221
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 8:10
DESCRIPTION:וְאָכַלְתָּ וְשָׂבָעְתָּ וּבֵרַ
 כְתָּ אֶת־יְהוָה אֱלֹהֶיךָ עַל־הָאָרֶץ 
 הַטֹּבָה אֲשֶׁר נָתַן־לָךְ׃\nVe'akhalta vesava'et
 a uverakhta et-Adonai Elohekha al-ha'aretz hatovah asher natan-lakh\nAnd t
 hou shalt eat and be satisfied\, and bless the LORD thy God for the good l
 and which He hath given thee.\n\nEat\, be satisfied\, and bless. This vers
 e is the source of Birkat Hamazon\, the blessing after meals.\n\nOpen Alep
 h: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270221@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270221
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270222
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 10:19
DESCRIPTION:וַאֲהַבְתֶּם אֶת־הַגֵּר כִּי־גֵ
 רִים הֱיִיתֶם בְּאֶרֶץ מִצְרָיִם׃\nVa'ahavte
 m et-hager ki-gerim heyitem be'eretz Mitzrayim\nLove ye therefore the stra
 nger\; for ye were strangers in the land of Egypt.\n\nLove the stranger\, 
 because you were strangers in Egypt. The Torah asks for more than not hurt
 ing newcomers\; it asks us to love them.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-revie
 w.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270222@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270222
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270223
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 16:20
DESCRIPTION:צֶדֶק צֶדֶק תִּרְדֹּף לְמַעַן תִּ
 חְיֶה וְיָרַשְׁתָּ אֶת־הָאָרֶץ אֲשֶׁר־
 יְהוָה אֱלֹהֶיךָ נֹתֵן לָךְ׃\nTzedek tzedek tirdo
 f lema'an tichyeh veyarashta et-ha'aretz asher-Adonai Elohekha noten lakh\
 nJustice\, justice shalt thou follow\, that thou mayest live\, and inherit
  the land which the LORD thy God giveth thee.\n\nTzedek tzedek tirdof: "Ju
 stice\, justice you shall pursue." The word is said twice\, to show how ha
 rd we should work for it.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/
 #/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270223@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270223
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270224
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 30:14
DESCRIPTION:כִּי־קָרוֹב אֵלֶיךָ הַדָּבָר מְאֹ
 ד בְּפִיךָ וּבִלְבָבְךָ לַעֲשֹׂתוֹ׃\nKi-ka
 rov elekha hadavar me'od befikha uvilvavekha la'asoto\nBut the word is ver
 y nigh unto thee\, in thy mouth\, and in thy heart\, that thou mayest do i
 t.\n\nThe Torah is not far away: it is in your mouth and in your heart. It
  is within reach\, one word at a time.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.
 onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270224@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270224
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270225
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 30:19
DESCRIPTION:הַעִידֹתִי בָכֶם הַיּוֹם אֶת־הַ
 שָּׁמַיִם וְאֶת־הָאָרֶץ הַחַיִּים וְהַ
 מָּוֶת נָתַתִּי לְפָנֶיךָ הַבְּרָכָה וְ
 הַקְּלָלָה וּבָחַרְתָּ בַּחַיִּים לְמַ
 עַן תִּחְיֶה אַתָּה וְזַרְעֶךָ׃\nHa'idoti vakh
 em hayom et-hashamayim ve'et-ha'aretz hachayim vehamavet natati lefanekha 
 haberakhah vehakelalah uvacharta bachayim lema'an tichyeh atah vezar'ekha\
 nI call heaven and earth to witness against you this day\, that I have set
  before thee life and death\, the blessing and the curse\; therefore choos
 e life\, that thou mayest live\, thou and thy seed\;\n\n"Choose life." Eve
 ry day brings choices\, and the Torah asks us to choose the ones that lead
  to life and blessing.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/m
 orning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270225@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270225
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270226
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 31:6
DESCRIPTION:חִזְקוּ וְאִמְצוּ אַל־תִּירְאוּ 
 וְאַל־תַּעַרְצוּ מִפְּנֵיהֶם כִּי יְה
 וָה אֱלֹהֶיךָ הוּא הַהֹלֵךְ עִמָּךְ לֹא 
 יַרְפְּךָ וְלֹא יַעַזְבֶךָּ׃\nChizku ve'imtzu al
 -tir'u ve'al-ta'artzu mipeneihem ki Adonai Elohekha hu haholekh imakh lo y
 arpekha velo ya'azveka\nBe strong and of good courage\, fear not\, nor be 
 affrighted at them\; for the LORD thy God\, He it is that doth go with the
 e\; He will not fail thee\, nor forsake thee.’\n\nChazak ve'ematz: "Be s
 trong and of good courage." Moses says this before the people enter the la
 nd without him.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270226@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270226
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270227
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 6:6
DESCRIPTION:וְהָיוּ הַדְּבָרִים הָאֵלֶּה אֲ
 שֶׁר אָנֹכִי מְצַוְּךָ הַיּוֹם עַל־לְבָ
 בֶךָ׃\nVehayu hadevarim ha'eleh asher anokhi metzavekha hayom al-leva
 vekha\nAnd these words\, which I command thee this day\, shall be upon thy
  heart\;\n\n"These words shall be upon your heart." Learning Torah is mean
 t to go deeper than memory\, into who we are.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-
 review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270227@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270227
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270228
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 31:16
DESCRIPTION:וְשָׁמְרוּ בְנֵי־יִשְׂרָאֵל אֶת־
 הַשַּׁבָּת לַעֲשׂוֹת אֶת־הַשַּׁבָּת לְ
 דֹרֹתָם בְּרִית עוֹלָם׃\nVeshamru venei-Yisra'el et-h
 ashabat la'asot et-hashabat ledorotam berit olam\nWherefore the children o
 f Israel shall keep the sabbath\, to observe the sabbath throughout their 
 generations\, for a perpetual covenant.\n\nV'shamru: the people of Israel 
 shall keep the Shabbat for all generations. This verse is sung on Friday n
 ight and Shabbat morning.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/
 #/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270228@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270228
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270301
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 34:10
DESCRIPTION:וְלֹא־קָם נָבִיא עוֹד בְּיִשְׂרָ
 אֵל כְּמֹשֶׁה אֲשֶׁר יְדָעוֹ יְהוָה פָּ
 נִים אֶל־פָּנִים׃\nVelo-kam navi od beyisra'el kemosheh as
 her yeda'o Adonai panim el-panim\nAnd there hath not arisen a prophet sinc
 e in Israel like unto Moses\, whom the LORD knew face to face\;\n\nNear th
 e very end of the Torah: no prophet arose like Moses\, who knew God face t
 o face. Then we roll the scroll back and start again.\n\nOpen Aleph: https
 ://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270301@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270301
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270302
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 1:1
DESCRIPTION:בְּרֵאשִׁית בָּרָא אֱלֹהִים אֵת 
 הַשָּׁמַיִם וְאֵת הָאָרֶץ׃\nBereshit bara Elohim e
 t hashamayim ve'et ha'aretz\nIn the beginning God created the heaven and t
 he earth.\n\nThe Torah opens with its first word\, Bereshit\, "in the begi
 nning." Everything that follows starts here: the world has a Maker\, and i
 t did not come about by chance.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrende
 r.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270302@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270302
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270303
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 1:3
DESCRIPTION:וַיֹּאמֶר אֱלֹהִים יְהִי אוֹר וַ
 יְהִי־אוֹר׃\nVayomer Elohim yehi or vayhi-or\nAnd God said: ‘
 Let there be light.’ And there was light.\n\nThe first thing God makes i
 s light\, and He makes it with words. In Judaism speech has real power\, s
 o the words we choose each day matter.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.
 onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270303@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270303
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270304
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 1:27
DESCRIPTION:וַיִּבְרָא אֱלֹהִים אֶת־הָאָדָם 
 בְּצַלְמוֹ בְּצֶלֶם אֱלֹהִים בָּרָא אֹת
 וֹ זָכָר וּנְקֵבָה בָּרָא אֹתָם׃\nVayivra Eloh
 im et-ha'adam betzalmo betzelem Elohim bara oto zakhar unekevah bara otam\
 nAnd God created man in His own image\, in the image of God created He him
 \; male and female created He them.\n\nEvery person is made in the image o
 f God. That is why each human life has worth\, whoever the person is and w
 herever they come from.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/
 morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270304@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270304
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270305
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 1:31
DESCRIPTION:וַיַּרְא אֱלֹהִים אֶת־כָּל־אֲשֶׁ
 ר עָשָׂה וְהִנֵּה־טוֹב מְאֹד וַיְהִי־עֶ
 רֶב וַיְהִי־בֹקֶר יוֹם הַשִּׁשִּׁי׃\nVayar
  Elohim et-kol-asher asah vehineh-tov me'od vayhi-erev vayhi-voker yom has
 hishi\nAnd God saw every thing that He had made\, and\, behold\, it was ve
 ry good. And there was evening and there was morning\, the sixth day.\n\nA
 fter each day God saw that it was good. On the sixth day\, with people in 
 the world\, it became "very good." Look for the good in your own day.\n\nO
 pen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270305@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270305
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270306
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 2:3
DESCRIPTION:וַיְבָרֶךְ אֱלֹהִים אֶת־יוֹם הַ
 שְּׁבִיעִי וַיְקַדֵּשׁ אֹתוֹ כִּי בוֹ 
 שָׁבַת מִכָּל־מְלַאכְתּוֹ אֲשֶׁר־בָּרָ
 א אֱלֹהִים לַעֲשׂוֹת׃\nVayvarekh Elohim et-yom hashevi'
 i vaykadesh oto ki vo shavat mikol-melakhto asher-bara Elohim la'asot\nAnd
  God blessed the seventh day\, and hallowed it\; because that in it He res
 ted from all His work which God in creating had made.\n\nThis is the first
  Shabbat. God rested on the seventh day and made it holy\, and we rest on 
 it too. Shabbat is a gift of time\, not only a rule.\n\nOpen Aleph: https:
 //alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270306@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270306
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270307
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 2:15
DESCRIPTION:וַיִּקַּח יְהוָה אֱלֹהִים אֶת־הָ
 אָדָם וַיַּנִּחֵהוּ בְגַן־עֵדֶן לְעָבְ
 דָהּ וּלְשָׁמְרָהּ׃\nVayikach Adonai Elohim et-ha'adam v
 ayanichehu vegan-eden le'avedah uleshamerah\nAnd the LORD God took the man
 \, and put him into the garden of Eden to dress it and to keep it.\n\nAdam
  was put in the garden to work it and to guard it. The earth is placed in 
 our care\, and looking after it is part of our job.\n\nOpen Aleph: https:/
 /alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270307@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270307
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270308
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 2:18
DESCRIPTION:וַיֹּאמֶר יְהוָה אֱלֹהִים לֹא־טוֹ
 ב הֱיוֹת הָאָדָם לְבַדּוֹ אֶעֱשֶׂהּ־לּ
 וֹ עֵזֶר כְּנֶגְדּוֹ׃\nVayomer Adonai Elohim lo-tov hey
 ot ha'adam levado e'eseh-lo ezer kenegdo\nAnd the LORD God said: ‘It is 
 not good that the man should be alone\; I will make him a help meet for hi
 m.’\n\n"It is not good to be alone." People need each other. Community\,
  friendship and family are part of how we were made.\n\nOpen Aleph: https:
 //alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270308@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270308
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270309
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 4:9
DESCRIPTION:וַיֹּאמֶר יְהוָה אֶל־קַיִן אֵי הֶ
 בֶל אָחִיךָ וַיֹּאמֶר לֹא יָדַעְתִּי הֲ
 שֹׁמֵר אָחִי אָנֹכִי׃\nVayomer Adonai el-kayin ei hevel
  achikha vayomer lo yadati hashomer achi anokhi\nAnd the LORD said unto Ca
 in: ‘Where is Abel thy brother?’ And he said: ‘I know not\; am I my 
 brother’s keeper?’\n\nCain asks\, "Am I my brother's keeper?" The rest
  of the Torah answers yes. We are responsible for one another.\n\nOpen Ale
 ph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270309@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270309
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270310
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 12:1
DESCRIPTION:וַיֹּאמֶר יְהוָה אֶל־אַבְרָם לֶךְ
 ־לְךָ מֵאַרְצְךָ וּמִמּוֹלַדְתְּךָ וּ
 מִבֵּית אָבִיךָ אֶל־הָאָרֶץ אֲשֶׁר אַרְ
 אֶךָּ׃\nVayomer Adonai el-Avram lekh-lekha me'artzekha umimoladtekha
  umibeit avikha el-ha'aretz asher ar'eka\nNow the LORD said unto Abram: 
 ‘Get thee out of thy country\, and from thy kindred\, and from thy fathe
 r’s house\, unto the land that I will show thee.\n\nLech lecha: "go for 
 yourself." Abraham leaves everything familiar to follow God. Every new sta
 rt\, including learning Hebrew\, takes a first step like this.\n\nOpen Ale
 ph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270310@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270310
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270311
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 12:2
DESCRIPTION:וְאֶעֶשְׂךָ לְגוֹי גָּדוֹל וַאֲבָ
 רֶכְךָ וַאֲגַדְּלָה שְׁמֶךָ וֶהְיֵה בְּ
 רָכָה׃\nVe'e'eskha legoy gadol va'avarekhkha va'agadelah shemekha ve
 hyeh berakhah\nAnd I will make of thee a great nation\, and I will bless t
 hee\, and make thy name great\; and be thou a blessing.\n\nAbraham is told
  not only that he will be blessed but that he will be a blessing. A good l
 ife is one that brings good to others.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.
 onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270311@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270311
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270312
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 15:5
DESCRIPTION:וַיּוֹצֵא אֹתוֹ הַחוּצָה וַיֹּאמֶ
 ר הַבֶּט־נָא הַשָּׁמַיְמָה וּסְפֹר הַכּ
 וֹכָבִים אִם־תּוּכַל לִסְפֹּר אֹתָם וַ
 יֹּאמֶר לוֹ כֹּה יִהְיֶה זַרְעֶךָ׃\nVayotze 
 oto hachutzah vayomer habet-na hashamaymah usefor hakokhavim im-tukhal lis
 por otam vayomer lo koh yihyeh zar'ekha\nAnd He brought him forth abroad\,
  and said: ‘Look now toward heaven\, and count the stars\, if thou be ab
 le to count them’\; and He said unto him: ‘So shall thy seed be.’\n\
 nGod takes Abraham outside to count the stars. When things feel small or u
 ncertain\, step back and look at the bigger picture.\n\nOpen Aleph: https:
 //alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270312@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270312
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270313
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 18:25
DESCRIPTION:חָלִלָה לְּךָ מֵעֲשֹׂת כַּדָּבָר 
 הַזֶּה לְהָמִית צַדִּיק עִם־רָשָׁע וְהָ
 יָה כַצַדִּיק כָּרָשָׁע חָלִלָה לָּךְ 
 הֲשֹׁפֵט כָּל־הָאָרֶץ לֹא יַעֲשֶׂה מִ
 שְׁפָּט׃\nChalilah lekha me'asot kadavar hazeh lehamit tzadik im-r
 asha vehayah khatzadik karasha chalilah lakh hashofet kol-ha'aretz lo ya'a
 seh mishpat\nThat be far from Thee to do after this manner\, to slay the r
 ighteous with the wicked\, that so the righteous should be as the wicked\;
  that be far from Thee\; shall not the judge of all the earth do justly?
 ’\n\nAbraham argues with God to save the people of Sodom. In Jewish trad
 ition it is right to speak up for justice\, even before the highest author
 ity.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270313@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270313
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270314
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 28:15
DESCRIPTION:וְהִנֵּה אָנֹכִי עִמָּךְ וּשְׁמַ
 רְתִּיךָ בְּכֹל אֲשֶׁר־תֵּלֵךְ וַהֲשִׁ
 בֹתִיךָ אֶל־הָאֲדָמָה הַזֹּאת כִּי לֹא 
 אֶעֱזָבְךָ עַד אֲשֶׁר אִם־עָשִׂיתִי אֵת
  אֲשֶׁר־דִּבַּרְתִּי לָךְ׃\nVehineh anokhi imakh u
 shemartikha bekhol asher-telekh vahashivotikha el-ha'adamah hazot ki lo e'
 ezavekha ad asher im-asiti et asher-dibarti lakh\nAnd\, behold\, I am with
  thee\, and will keep thee whithersoever thou goest\, and will bring thee 
 back into this land\; for I will not leave thee\, until I have done that w
 hich I have spoken to thee of.’\n\nJacob is alone and running away\, and
  God promises: I am with you\, wherever you go. You are never as alone as 
 you feel.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270314@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270314
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270315
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 28:16
DESCRIPTION:וַיִּיקַץ יַעֲקֹב מִשְּׁנָתוֹ וַ
 יֹּאמֶר אָכֵן יֵשׁ יְהוָה בַּמָּקוֹם הַ
 זֶּה וְאָנֹכִי לֹא יָדָעְתִּי׃\nVayikatz Ya'ako
 v mishenato vayomer akhen yesh Adonai bamakom hazeh ve'anokhi lo yada'eti\
 nAnd Jacob awaked out of his sleep\, and he said: ‘Surely the LORD is in
  this place\; and I knew it not.’\n\nJacob wakes from his dream and says
  God was in this place and he did not know it. Holiness can be right where
  you are\, if you notice it.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.c
 om/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270315@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270315
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270316
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 32:11
DESCRIPTION:קָטֹנְתִּי מִכֹּל הַחֲסָדִים וּמִ
 כָּל־הָאֱמֶת אֲשֶׁר עָשִׂיתָ אֶת־עַבְ
 דֶּךָ כִּי בְמַקְלִי עָבַרְתִּי אֶת־הַ
 יַּרְדֵּן הַזֶּה וְעַתָּה הָיִיתִי לִ
 שְׁנֵי מַחֲנוֹת׃\nKatoneti mikol hachasadim umikol-ha'emet 
 asher asita et-avdekha ki vemakli avarti et-hayarden hazeh ve'atah hayiti 
 lishnei machanot\nI am not worthy of all the mercies\, and of all the trut
 h\, which Thou hast shown unto Thy servant\; for with my staff I passed ov
 er this Jordan\; and now I am become two camps.\n\nBefore meeting his brot
 her Esau\, Jacob says he is not worthy of all the kindness he has received
 . Gratitude and humility go together.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.o
 nrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270316@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270316
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270317
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 45:4
DESCRIPTION:וַיֹּאמֶר יוֹסֵף אֶל־אֶחָיו גְּשׁ
 וּ־נָא אֵלַי וַיִּגָּשׁוּ וַיֹּאמֶר אֲ
 נִי יוֹסֵף אֲחִיכֶם אֲשֶׁר־מְכַרְתֶּם 
 אֹתִי מִצְרָיְמָה׃\nVayomer yosef el-echav geshu-na elai 
 vayigashu vayomer ani yosef achikhem asher-mekhartem oti mitzrayemah\nAnd 
 Joseph said unto his brethren: ‘Come near to me\, I pray you.’ And the
 y came near. And he said: ‘I am Joseph your brother\, whom ye sold into 
 Egypt.\n\nJoseph says to the brothers who sold him\, "Come close to me." I
 t is one of the great moments of forgiveness in the Torah.\n\nOpen Aleph: 
 https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270317@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270317
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270318
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 50:20
DESCRIPTION:וְאַתֶּם חֲשַׁבְתֶּם עָלַי רָעָה 
 אֱלֹהִים חֲשָׁבָהּ לְטֹבָה לְמַעַן עֲ
 שֹׂה כַּיּוֹם הַזֶּה לְהַחֲיֹת עַם־רָב׃
 \nVe'atem chashavtem alai ra'ah Elohim chashavah letovah lema'an asoh kayo
 m hazeh lehachayot am-rav\nAnd as for you\, ye meant evil against me\; but
  God meant it for good\, to bring to pass\, as it is this day\, to save mu
 ch people alive.\n\nJoseph tells his brothers that what they meant for har
 m\, God turned to good. Hard chapters of a life can lead somewhere good.\n
 \nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270318@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270318
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270319
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 3:5
DESCRIPTION:וַיֹּאמֶר אַל־תִּקְרַב הֲלֹם שַׁל
 ־נְעָלֶיךָ מֵעַל רַגְלֶיךָ כִּי הַמָּק
 וֹם אֲשֶׁר אַתָּה עוֹמֵד עָלָיו אַדְמַת
 ־קֹדֶשׁ הוּא׃\nVayomer al-tikrav halom shal-ne'alekha me'al ra
 glekha ki hamakom asher atah omed alav admat-kodesh hu\nAnd He said: ‘Dr
 aw not nigh hither\; put off thy shoes from off thy feet\, for the place w
 hereon thou standest is holy ground.’\n\nAt the burning bush Moses is to
 ld to take off his shoes\, because the ground is holy. Some moments call f
 or us to slow down and pay attention.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.o
 nrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270319@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270319
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270320
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 3:14
DESCRIPTION:וַיֹּאמֶר אֱלֹהִים אֶל־מֹשֶׁה אֶ
 הְיֶה אֲשֶׁר אֶהְיֶה וַיֹּאמֶר כֹּה תֹא
 מַר לִבְנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל אֶהְיֶה שְׁלָחַ
 נִי אֲלֵיכֶם׃\nVayomer Elohim el-Mosheh ehyeh asher ehyeh vayo
 mer koh tomar livnei Yisra'el ehyeh shelachani aleikhem\nAnd God said unto
  Moses: ‘I AM THAT I AM’\; and He said: ‘Thus shalt thou say unto th
 e children of Israel: I AM hath sent me unto you.’\n\nEhyeh asher ehyeh:
  "I will be what I will be." God's name here is about being present\, in e
 very time and place.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/mor
 ning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270320@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270320
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270321
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 13:8
DESCRIPTION:וְהִגַּדְתָּ לְבִנְךָ בַּיּוֹם הַ
 הוּא לֵאמֹר בַּעֲבוּר זֶה עָשָׂה יְהוָה 
 לִי בְּצֵאתִי מִמִּצְרָיִם׃\nVehigadta levinkha b
 ayom hahu lemor ba'avur zeh asah Adonai li betzeti mimitzrayim\nAnd thou s
 halt tell thy son in that day\, saying: It is because of that which the LO
 RD did for me when I came forth out of Egypt.\n\nThis verse is why we tell
  the Passover story at the Seder. Each generation tells it as if it happen
 ed to them.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270321@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270321
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270322
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 14:14
DESCRIPTION:יְהוָה יִלָּחֵם לָכֶם וְאַתֶּם 
 תַּחֲרִישׁוּן׃\nAdonai yilachem lakhem ve'atem tacharishun\n
 The LORD will fight for you\, and ye shall hold your peace.’\n\nAt the S
 ea of Reeds\, Moses tells the frightened people that God will fight for th
 em. Sometimes the right move is to stay calm and trust.\n\nOpen Aleph: htt
 ps://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270322@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270322
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270323
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 15:2
DESCRIPTION:עָזִּי וְזִמְרָת יָהּ וַיְהִי־לִי
  לִישׁוּעָה זֶה אֵלִי וְאַנְוֵהוּ אֱלֹ
 הֵי אָבִי וַאֲרֹמְמֶנְהוּ׃\nAzi vezimrat yah vayhi
 -li lishu'ah zeh eli ve'anvehu elohei avi va'aromemenhu\nThe LORD is my st
 rength and song\, And He is become my salvation\; This is my God\, and I w
 ill glorify Him\; My father’s God\, and I will exalt Him.\n\nFrom the So
 ng at the Sea: "The Lord is my strength and my song." These words are sung
  in synagogue every morning.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.c
 om/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270323@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270323
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270324
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 15:11
DESCRIPTION:מִי־כָמֹכָה בָּאֵלִם יְהוָה מִי 
 כָּמֹכָה נֶאְדָּר בַּקֹּדֶשׁ נוֹרָא תְ
 הִלֹּת עֹשֵׂה פֶלֶא׃\nMi-khamokhah ba'elim Adonai mi kam
 okhah nedar bakodesh nora tehilot oseh fele\nWho is like unto Thee\, O LOR
 D\, among the mighty? Who is like unto Thee\, glorious in holiness\, Fearf
 ul in praises\, doing wonders?\n\nMi chamocha\, "Who is like You?" This li
 ne from the Song at the Sea is part of the daily prayers\, just after the 
 Shema.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270324@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270324
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270325
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 19:6
DESCRIPTION:וְאַתֶּם תִּהְיוּ־לִי מַמְלֶכֶת 
 כֹּהֲנִים וְגוֹי קָדוֹשׁ אֵלֶּה הַדְּבָ
 רִים אֲשֶׁר תְּדַבֵּר אֶל־בְּנֵי יִשְׂ
 רָאֵל׃\nVe'atem tihyu-li mamlekhet kohanim vegoy kadosh eleh hadevar
 im asher tedaber el-benei Yisra'el\nand ye shall be unto Me a kingdom of p
 riests\, and a holy nation. These are the words which thou shalt speak unt
 o the children of Israel.’\n\nAt Sinai the whole people is called a king
 dom of priests and a holy nation. Holiness is meant for everyone\, not onl
 y for a few.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270325@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270325
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270326
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 20:2
DESCRIPTION:אָנֹכִי יְהוָה אֱלֹהֶיךָ אֲשֶׁר ה
 וֹצֵאתִיךָ מֵאֶרֶץ מִצְרַיִם מִבֵּית עֲ
 בָדִים׃\nAnokhi Adonai Elohekha asher hotzetikha me'eretz Mitzrayim
  mibeit avadim\nI am the LORD thy God\, who brought thee out of the land o
 f Egypt\, out of the house of bondage.\n\nThe Ten Commandments begin with 
 who God is: the One who brought us out of slavery. Freedom comes first\, a
 nd the commandments follow.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.co
 m/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270326@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270326
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270327
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 20:8
DESCRIPTION:זָכוֹר אֶת־יוֹם הַשַׁבָּת לְקַדְּ
 שׁוֹ\nZakhor et-yom hashabat lekadesho\nRemember the sabbath day\, to 
 keep it holy.\n\nZachor: "Remember the Shabbat day." We remember it with c
 andles\, Kiddush\, rest and time with the people we love.\n\nOpen Aleph: h
 ttps://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270327@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270327
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270328
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 20:12
DESCRIPTION:כַּבֵּד אֶת־אָבִיךָ וְאֶת־אִמֶּ
 ךָ לְמַעַן יַאֲרִכוּן יָמֶיךָ עַל הָאֲ
 דָמָה אֲשֶׁר־יְהוָה אֱלֹהֶיךָ נֹתֵן לָ
 ךְ׃\nKabed et-avikha ve'et-imekha lema'an ya'arikhun yamekha al ha'adam
 ah asher-Adonai Elohekha noten lakh\nHonour thy father and thy mother\, th
 at thy days may be long upon the land which the LORD thy God giveth thee.\
 n\nHonour your father and your mother. It is one of the Ten Commandments\,
  and the first that comes with a promise of long life.\n\nOpen Aleph: http
 s://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270328@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270328
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270329
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 22:20
DESCRIPTION:וְגֵר לֹא־תוֹנֶה וְלֹא תִלְחָצֶנּ
 וּ כִּי־גֵרִים הֱיִיתֶם בְּאֶרֶץ מִצְרָ
 יִם׃\nVeger lo-toneh velo tilchatzenu ki-gerim heyitem be'eretz Mitzra
 yim\nAnd a stranger shalt thou not wrong\, neither shalt thou oppress him\
 ; for ye were strangers in the land of Egypt.\n\nDo not wrong the stranger
 \, because you were strangers in Egypt. This idea comes up again and again
  in the Torah.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270329@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270329
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270330
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 23:2
DESCRIPTION:לֹא־תִהְיֶה אַחֲרֵי־רַבִּים לְרָ
 עֹת וְלֹא־תַעֲנֶה עַל־רִב לִנְטֹת אַחֲ
 רֵי רַבִּים לְהַטֹּת׃\nLo-tihyeh acharei-rabim lera'ot 
 velo-ta'aneh al-riv lintot acharei rabim lehatot\nThou shalt not follow a 
 multitude to do evil\; neither shalt thou bear witness in a cause to turn 
 aside after a multitude to pervert justice\;\n\nDo not follow the crowd to
  do wrong. Doing the right thing sometimes means standing apart.\n\nOpen A
 leph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270330@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270330
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270331
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 23:9
DESCRIPTION:וְגֵר לֹא תִלְחָץ וְאַתֶּם יְדַעְ
 תֶּם אֶת־נֶפֶשׁ הַגֵּר כִּי־גֵרִים הֱיִ
 יתֶם בְּאֶרֶץ מִצְרָיִם׃\nVeger lo tilchatz ve'atem 
 yedatem et-nefesh hager ki-gerim heyitem be'eretz Mitzrayim\nAnd a strange
 r shalt thou not oppress\; for ye know the heart of a stranger\, seeing ye
  were strangers in the land of Egypt.\n\n"You know the heart of the strang
 er." Our own history should make us kind to newcomers.\n\nOpen Aleph: http
 s://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270331@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270331
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270401
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 25:8
DESCRIPTION:וְעָשׂוּ לִי מִקְדָּשׁ וְשָׁכַנְ
 תִּי בְּתוֹכָם׃\nVe'asu li mikdash veshakhanti betokham\nAnd
  let them make Me a sanctuary\, that I may dwell among them.\n\n"Make Me a
  sanctuary\, and I will dwell among them." Not "in it\," but among them: G
 od lives among people\, in the places they make holy.\n\nOpen Aleph: https
 ://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270401@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270401
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270402
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 33:13
DESCRIPTION:וְעַתָּה אִם־נָא מָצָאתִי חֵן בְּ
 עֵינֶיךָ הוֹדִעֵנִי נָא אֶת־דְּרָכֶךָ 
 וְאֵדָעֲךָ לְמַעַן אֶמְצָא־חֵן בְּעֵי
 נֶיךָ וּרְאֵה כִּי עַמְּךָ הַגּוֹי הַ
 זֶּה׃\nVe'atah im-na matzati chen be'einekha hodi'eni na et-derakhekh
 a ve'eda'akha lema'an emtza-chen be'einekha ure'eh ki amekha hagoy hazeh\n
 Now therefore\, I pray Thee\, if I have found grace in Thy sight\, show me
  now Thy ways\, that I may know Thee\, to the end that I may find grace in
  Thy sight\; and consider that this nation is Thy people.’\n\nMoses asks
  God\, "Show me Your ways\, so that I may know You." Learning is one of th
 e ways Jews come close to God.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender
 .com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270402@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270402
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270403
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 34:6
DESCRIPTION:וַיַּעֲבֹר יְהוָה עַל־פָּנָיו וַ
 יִּקְרָא יְהוָה יְהוָה אֵל רַחוּם וְחַ
 נּוּן אֶרֶךְ אַפַּיִם וְרַב־חֶסֶד וֶאֱ
 מֶת\nVaya'avor Adonai al-panav vayikra Adonai Adonai el rachum vechanun
  erekh apayim verav-chesed ve'emet\nAnd the LORD passed by before him\, an
 d proclaimed: ‘The LORD\, the LORD\, God\, merciful and gracious\, long-
 suffering\, and abundant in goodness and truth\;\n\nThese are God's qualit
 ies of mercy\, sung on the High Holy Days: compassionate\, gracious\, slow
  to anger\, full of kindness and truth.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review
 .onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270403@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270403
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270404
SUMMARY:Torah: Leviticus 19:2
DESCRIPTION:דַּבֵּר אֶל־כָּל־עֲדַת בְּנֵי־יִ
 שְׂרָאֵל וְאָמַרְתָּ אֲלֵהֶם קְדֹשִׁים 
 תִּהְיוּ כִּי קָדוֹשׁ אֲנִי יְהוָה אֱלֹ
 הֵיכֶם׃\nDaber el-kol-adat benei-Yisra'el ve'amarta alehem kedoshim
  tihyu ki kadosh ani Adonai Eloheikhem\nSpeak unto all the congregation of
  the children of Israel\, and say unto them: Ye shall be holy\; for I the 
 LORD your God am holy.\n\n"You shall be holy\, for I am holy." The chapter
  that follows shows what that means: honesty\, kindness and fairness in ev
 eryday life.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270404@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270404
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270405
SUMMARY:Torah: Leviticus 19:3
DESCRIPTION:אִישׁ אִמּוֹ וְאָבִיו תִּירָאוּ 
 וְאֶת־שַׁבְּתֹתַי תִּשְׁמֹרוּ אֲנִי יְ
 הוָה אֱלֹהֵיכֶם׃\nIsh imo ve'aviv tira'u ve'et-shabetotai t
 ishmoru ani Adonai Eloheikhem\nYe shall fear every man his mother\, and hi
 s father\, and ye shall keep My sabbaths: I am the LORD your God.\n\nRespe
 ct your parents and keep Shabbat. Both are about honouring where we come f
 rom.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270405@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270405
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270406
SUMMARY:Torah: Leviticus 19:9
DESCRIPTION:וּבְקֻצְרְכֶם אֶת־קְצִיר אַרְצְ
 כֶם לֹא תְכַלֶּה פְּאַת שָׂדְךָ לִקְצֹר 
 וְלֶקֶט קְצִירְךָ לֹא תְלַקֵּט׃\nUvekutzrekhem
  et-ketzir artzekhem lo tekhaleh pe'at sadekha liktzor veleket ketzirekha 
 lo telaket\nAnd when ye reap the harvest of your land\, thou shalt not who
 lly reap the corner of thy field\, neither shalt thou gather the gleaning 
 of thy harvest.\n\nLeave the corners of your field for people in need. Giv
 ing to others is built right into how we earn and spend.\n\nOpen Aleph: ht
 tps://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270406@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270406
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270407
SUMMARY:Torah: Leviticus 19:14
DESCRIPTION:לֹא־תְקַלֵּל חֵרֵשׁ וְלִפְנֵי עִ
 וֵּר לֹא תִתֵּן מִכְשֹׁל וְיָרֵאתָ מֵּ
 אֱלֹהֶיךָ אֲנִי יְהוָה׃\nLo-tekalel cheresh velifnei 
 iver lo titen mikhshol veyareta me'Elohekha ani Adonai\nThou shalt not cur
 se the deaf\, nor put a stumbling-block before the blind\, but thou shalt 
 fear thy God: I am the LORD.\n\nDo not curse the deaf or put a stumbling b
 lock before the blind. Treat everyone with care\, especially those who can
 not defend themselves.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/m
 orning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270407@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270407
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270408
SUMMARY:Torah: Leviticus 19:16
DESCRIPTION:לֹא־תֵלֵךְ רָכִיל בְּעַמֶּיךָ לֹא
  תַעֲמֹד עַל־דַּם רֵעֶךָ אֲנִי יְהוָה׃\nL
 o-telekh rakhil be'amekha lo ta'amod al-dam re'ekha ani Adonai\nThou shalt
  not go up and down as a talebearer among thy people\; neither shalt thou 
 stand idly by the blood of thy neighbour: I am the LORD.\n\nDo not spread 
 gossip\, and do not stand by while your neighbour is in danger. Words can 
 hurt\, and silence can too.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.co
 m/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270408@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270408
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270409
SUMMARY:Torah: Leviticus 19:18
DESCRIPTION:לֹא־תִקֹּם וְלֹא־תִטֹּר אֶת־בְּ
 נֵי עַמֶּךָ וְאָהַבְתָּ לְרֵעֲךָ כָּמוֹ
 ךָ אֲנִי יְהוָה׃\nLo-tikom velo-titor et-benei amekha ve'aha
 vta lere'akha kamokha ani Adonai\nThou shalt not take vengeance\, nor bear
  any grudge against the children of thy people\, but thou shalt love thy n
 eighbour as thyself: I am the LORD.\n\n"Love your neighbour as yourself." 
 Rabbi Akiva called this the great principle of the whole Torah.\n\nOpen Al
 eph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270409@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270409
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270410
SUMMARY:Torah: Leviticus 19:32
DESCRIPTION:מִפְּנֵי שֵׂיבָה תָּקוּם וְהָדַרְ
 תָּ פְּנֵי זָקֵן וְיָרֵאתָ מֵּאֱלֹהֶיךָ
  אֲנִי יְהוָה׃\nMipenei seivah takum vehadarta penei zaken vey
 areta me'Elohekha ani Adonai\nThou shalt rise up before the hoary head\, a
 nd honour the face of the old man\, and thou shalt fear thy God: I am the 
 LORD.\n\nRise before the elderly and honour them. Age brings wisdom\, and 
 the Torah asks us to show it respect.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.o
 nrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270410@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270410
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270411
SUMMARY:Torah: Leviticus 25:10
DESCRIPTION:וְקִדַּשְׁתֶּם אֵת שְׁנַת הַחֲמִ
 שִּׁים שָׁנָה וּקְרָאתֶם דְּרוֹר בָּאָ
 רֶץ לְכָל־יֹשְׁבֶיהָ יוֹבֵל הִוא תִּהְ
 יֶה לָכֶם וְשַׁבְתֶּם אִישׁ אֶל־אֲחֻזָּ
 תוֹ וְאִישׁ אֶל־מִשְׁפַּחְתּוֹ תָּשֻׁב
 וּ׃\nVekidashtem et shenat hachamishim shanah ukeratem deror ba'aretz l
 ekhol-yosheveha yovel hiv tihyeh lakhem veshavtem ish el-achuzato ve'ish e
 l-mishpachto tashuvu\nAnd ye shall hallow the fiftieth year\, and proclaim
  liberty throughout the land unto all the inhabitants thereof\; it shall b
 e a jubilee unto you\; and ye shall return every man unto his possession\,
  and ye shall return every man unto his family.\n\n"Proclaim liberty throu
 ghout the land." These words about the Jubilee year are cast on the Libert
 y Bell in Philadelphia.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/
 morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270411@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270411
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270412
SUMMARY:Torah: Numbers 6:24
DESCRIPTION:יְבָרֶכְךָ יְהוָה וְיִשְׁמְרֶךָ׃\
 nYevarekhkha Adonai veyishmerekha\nThe LORD bless thee\, and keep thee\;\n
 \nThe first line of the Priestly Blessing\, still said in synagogues and b
 y parents to children on Friday night.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.
 onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270412@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270412
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270413
SUMMARY:Torah: Numbers 6:26
DESCRIPTION:יִשָּׂא יְהוָה פָּנָיו אֵלֶיךָ וְ
 יָשֵׂם לְךָ שָׁלוֹם׃\nYisa Adonai panav elekha veyasem l
 ekha shalom\nThe LORD lift up His countenance upon thee\, and give thee pe
 ace.\n\nThe Priestly Blessing ends with shalom\, peace. In Hebrew\, shalom
  also means wholeness: everything in its right place.\n\nOpen Aleph: https
 ://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270413@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270413
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270414
SUMMARY:Torah: Numbers 11:29
DESCRIPTION:וַיֹּאמֶר לוֹ מֹשֶׁה הַמְקַנֵּא 
 אַתָּה לִי וּמִי יִתֵּן כָּל־עַם יְהוָה 
 נְבִיאִים כִּי־יִתֵּן יְהוָה אֶת־רוּח
 וֹ עֲלֵיהֶם׃\nVayomer lo Mosheh hamkane atah li umi yiten kol-a
 m Adonai nevi'im ki-yiten Adonai et-rucho aleihem\nAnd Moses said unto him
 : ‘Art thou jealous for my sake? would that all the LORD’S people were
  prophets\, that the LORD would put His spirit upon them! ’\n\nWhen othe
 rs begin to prophesy\, Moses is not jealous. He wishes everyone could shar
 e God's spirit. Great leaders lift others up.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-
 review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270414@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270414
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270415
SUMMARY:Torah: Numbers 15:39
DESCRIPTION:וְהָיָה לָכֶם לְצִיצִת וּרְאִיתֶם
  אֹתוֹ וּזְכַרְתֶּם אֶת־כָּל־מִצְוֹת יְ
 הוָה וַעֲשִׂיתֶם אֹתָם וְלֹא־תָתֻרוּ אַ
 חֲרֵי לְבַבְכֶם וְאַחֲרֵי עֵינֵיכֶם אֲ
 שֶׁר־אַתֶּם זֹנִים אַחֲרֵיהֶם׃\nVehayah lakhem
  letzitzit ure'item oto uzekhartem et-kol-mitzvot Adonai va'asitem otam ve
 lo-taturu acharei levavkhem ve'acharei eineikhem asher-atem zonim achareih
 em\nAnd it shall be unto you for a fringe\, that ye may look upon it\, and
  remember all the commandments of the LORD\, and do them\; and that ye go 
 not about after your own heart and your own eyes\, after which ye use to g
 o astray\;\n\nThis verse is about the tzitzit\, the fringes on the tallit.
  Seeing them is a reminder of the commandments and of who we want to be.\n
 \nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270415@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270415
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270416
SUMMARY:Torah: Numbers 24:5
DESCRIPTION:מַה־טֹּבוּ אֹהָלֶיךָ יַעֲקֹב מִ
 שְׁכְּנֹתֶיךָ יִשְׂרָאֵל׃\nMah-tovu ohalekha Ya'ak
 ov mishkenotekha Yisra'el\nHow goodly are thy tents\, O Jacob\, Thy dwelli
 ngs\, O Israel!\n\nMah tovu\, "How good are your tents." Many synagogues o
 pen the morning service with these words.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-revi
 ew.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270416@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270416
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270417
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 4:9
DESCRIPTION:רַק הִשָּׁמֶר לְךָ וּשְׁמֹר נַפְ
 שְׁךָ מְאֹד פֶּן־תִּשְׁכַּח אֶת־הַדְּ
 בָרִים אֲשֶׁר־רָאוּ עֵינֶיךָ וּפֶן־יָס
 וּרוּ מִלְּבָבְךָ כֹּל יְמֵי חַיֶּיךָ 
 וְהוֹדַעְתָּם לְבָנֶיךָ וְלִבְנֵי בָנֶ
 יךָ׃\nRak hishamer lekha ushemor nafshekha me'od pen-tishkach et-hadev
 arim asher-ra'u einekha ufen-yasuru milevavekha kol yemei chayekha vehodat
 am levanekha velivnei vanekha\nOnly take heed to thyself\, and keep thy so
 ul diligently\, lest thou forget the things which thine eyes saw\, and les
 t they depart from thy heart all the days of thy life\; but make them know
 n unto thy children and thy children’s children\;\n\nDo not forget what 
 you have seen\, and teach it to your children and grandchildren. Memory is
  how a people stays alive.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com
 /#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270417@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270417
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270418
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 6:4
DESCRIPTION:שְׁמַע יִשְׂרָאֵל יְהוָה אֱלֹהֵינ
 וּ יְהוָה אֶחָד׃\nShema Yisra'el Adonai Eloheinu Adonai echa
 d\nHEAR\, O ISRAEL: THE LORD OUR GOD\, THE LORD IS ONE.\n\nThe Shema\, the
  central line of Jewish prayer: "Hear\, O Israel\, the Lord is our God\, t
 he Lord is One." It is said morning and night.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef
 -review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270418@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270418
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270419
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 6:5
DESCRIPTION:וְאָהַבְתָּ אֵת יְהוָה אֱלֹהֶיךָ 
 בְּכָל־לְבָבְךָ וּבְכָל־נַפְשְׁךָ וּבְ
 כָל־מְאֹדֶךָ׃\nVe'ahavta et Adonai Elohekha bekhol-levavekha 
 uvekhol-nafshekha uvekhol-me'odekha\nAnd thou shalt love the LORD thy God 
 with all thy heart\, and with all thy soul\, and with all thy might.\n\nV'
 ahavta: love God with all your heart\, all your soul and all your strength
 . Faith in Judaism is about love\, not only belief.\n\nOpen Aleph: https:/
 /alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270419@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270419
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270420
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 6:7
DESCRIPTION:וְשִׁנַּנְתָּם לְבָנֶיךָ וְדִבַּ
 רְתָּ בָּם בְּשִׁבְתְּךָ בְּבֵיתֶךָ וּ
 בְלֶכְתְּךָ בַדֶּרֶךְ וּבְשָׁכְבְּךָ 
 וּבְקוּמֶךָ׃\nVeshinantam levanekha vedibarta bam beshivtekha 
 beveitekha uvelekhtekha vaderekh uveshakhbekha uvekumekha\nand thou shalt 
 teach them diligently unto thy children\, and shalt talk of them when thou
  sittest in thy house\, and when thou walkest by the way\, and when thou l
 iest down\, and when thou risest up.\n\nTalk about these words at home\, o
 n the road\, when you lie down and when you get up. That is why the Shema 
 is said at bedtime and in the morning.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.
 onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270420@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270420
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270421
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 8:3
DESCRIPTION:וַיְעַנְּךָ וַיַּרְעִבֶךָ וַיַּ
 אֲכִלְךָ אֶת הַמָּן אֲשֶׁר לֹא־יָדַעְ
 תָּ וְלֹא יָדְעוּן אֲבֹתֶיךָ לְמַעַן ה
 וֹדִעֲךָ כִּי לֹא עַל־הַלֶּחֶם לְבַדּוֹ
  יִחְיֶה הָאָדָם כִּי עַל־כָּל־מוֹצָא 
 פִי־יְהוָה יִחְיֶה הָאָדָם׃\nVay'anekha vayar'ive
 kha vaya'akhilkha et haman asher lo-yadata velo yad'un avotekha lema'an ho
 di'akha ki lo al-halechem levado yichyeh ha'adam ki al-kol-motza fi-Adonai
  yichyeh ha'adam\nAnd He afflicted thee\, and suffered thee to hunger\, an
 d fed thee with manna\, which thou knewest not\, neither did thy fathers k
 now\; that He might make thee know that man doth not live by bread only\, 
 but by every thing that proceedeth out of the mouth of the LORD doth man l
 ive.\n\n"A person does not live by bread alone." We need meaning\, learnin
 g and purpose as much as food.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender
 .com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270421@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270421
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270422
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 8:10
DESCRIPTION:וְאָכַלְתָּ וְשָׂבָעְתָּ וּבֵרַ
 כְתָּ אֶת־יְהוָה אֱלֹהֶיךָ עַל־הָאָרֶץ 
 הַטֹּבָה אֲשֶׁר נָתַן־לָךְ׃\nVe'akhalta vesava'et
 a uverakhta et-Adonai Elohekha al-ha'aretz hatovah asher natan-lakh\nAnd t
 hou shalt eat and be satisfied\, and bless the LORD thy God for the good l
 and which He hath given thee.\n\nEat\, be satisfied\, and bless. This vers
 e is the source of Birkat Hamazon\, the blessing after meals.\n\nOpen Alep
 h: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270422@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270422
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270423
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 10:19
DESCRIPTION:וַאֲהַבְתֶּם אֶת־הַגֵּר כִּי־גֵ
 רִים הֱיִיתֶם בְּאֶרֶץ מִצְרָיִם׃\nVa'ahavte
 m et-hager ki-gerim heyitem be'eretz Mitzrayim\nLove ye therefore the stra
 nger\; for ye were strangers in the land of Egypt.\n\nLove the stranger\, 
 because you were strangers in Egypt. The Torah asks for more than not hurt
 ing newcomers\; it asks us to love them.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-revie
 w.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270423@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270423
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270424
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 16:20
DESCRIPTION:צֶדֶק צֶדֶק תִּרְדֹּף לְמַעַן תִּ
 חְיֶה וְיָרַשְׁתָּ אֶת־הָאָרֶץ אֲשֶׁר־
 יְהוָה אֱלֹהֶיךָ נֹתֵן לָךְ׃\nTzedek tzedek tirdo
 f lema'an tichyeh veyarashta et-ha'aretz asher-Adonai Elohekha noten lakh\
 nJustice\, justice shalt thou follow\, that thou mayest live\, and inherit
  the land which the LORD thy God giveth thee.\n\nTzedek tzedek tirdof: "Ju
 stice\, justice you shall pursue." The word is said twice\, to show how ha
 rd we should work for it.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/
 #/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270424@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270424
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270425
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 30:14
DESCRIPTION:כִּי־קָרוֹב אֵלֶיךָ הַדָּבָר מְאֹ
 ד בְּפִיךָ וּבִלְבָבְךָ לַעֲשֹׂתוֹ׃\nKi-ka
 rov elekha hadavar me'od befikha uvilvavekha la'asoto\nBut the word is ver
 y nigh unto thee\, in thy mouth\, and in thy heart\, that thou mayest do i
 t.\n\nThe Torah is not far away: it is in your mouth and in your heart. It
  is within reach\, one word at a time.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.
 onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270425@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270425
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270426
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 30:19
DESCRIPTION:הַעִידֹתִי בָכֶם הַיּוֹם אֶת־הַ
 שָּׁמַיִם וְאֶת־הָאָרֶץ הַחַיִּים וְהַ
 מָּוֶת נָתַתִּי לְפָנֶיךָ הַבְּרָכָה וְ
 הַקְּלָלָה וּבָחַרְתָּ בַּחַיִּים לְמַ
 עַן תִּחְיֶה אַתָּה וְזַרְעֶךָ׃\nHa'idoti vakh
 em hayom et-hashamayim ve'et-ha'aretz hachayim vehamavet natati lefanekha 
 haberakhah vehakelalah uvacharta bachayim lema'an tichyeh atah vezar'ekha\
 nI call heaven and earth to witness against you this day\, that I have set
  before thee life and death\, the blessing and the curse\; therefore choos
 e life\, that thou mayest live\, thou and thy seed\;\n\n"Choose life." Eve
 ry day brings choices\, and the Torah asks us to choose the ones that lead
  to life and blessing.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/m
 orning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270426@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270426
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270427
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 31:6
DESCRIPTION:חִזְקוּ וְאִמְצוּ אַל־תִּירְאוּ 
 וְאַל־תַּעַרְצוּ מִפְּנֵיהֶם כִּי יְה
 וָה אֱלֹהֶיךָ הוּא הַהֹלֵךְ עִמָּךְ לֹא 
 יַרְפְּךָ וְלֹא יַעַזְבֶךָּ׃\nChizku ve'imtzu al
 -tir'u ve'al-ta'artzu mipeneihem ki Adonai Elohekha hu haholekh imakh lo y
 arpekha velo ya'azveka\nBe strong and of good courage\, fear not\, nor be 
 affrighted at them\; for the LORD thy God\, He it is that doth go with the
 e\; He will not fail thee\, nor forsake thee.’\n\nChazak ve'ematz: "Be s
 trong and of good courage." Moses says this before the people enter the la
 nd without him.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270427@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270427
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270428
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 6:6
DESCRIPTION:וְהָיוּ הַדְּבָרִים הָאֵלֶּה אֲ
 שֶׁר אָנֹכִי מְצַוְּךָ הַיּוֹם עַל־לְבָ
 בֶךָ׃\nVehayu hadevarim ha'eleh asher anokhi metzavekha hayom al-leva
 vekha\nAnd these words\, which I command thee this day\, shall be upon thy
  heart\;\n\n"These words shall be upon your heart." Learning Torah is mean
 t to go deeper than memory\, into who we are.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-
 review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270428@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270428
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270429
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 31:16
DESCRIPTION:וְשָׁמְרוּ בְנֵי־יִשְׂרָאֵל אֶת־
 הַשַּׁבָּת לַעֲשׂוֹת אֶת־הַשַּׁבָּת לְ
 דֹרֹתָם בְּרִית עוֹלָם׃\nVeshamru venei-Yisra'el et-h
 ashabat la'asot et-hashabat ledorotam berit olam\nWherefore the children o
 f Israel shall keep the sabbath\, to observe the sabbath throughout their 
 generations\, for a perpetual covenant.\n\nV'shamru: the people of Israel 
 shall keep the Shabbat for all generations. This verse is sung on Friday n
 ight and Shabbat morning.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/
 #/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270429@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270429
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270430
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 34:10
DESCRIPTION:וְלֹא־קָם נָבִיא עוֹד בְּיִשְׂרָ
 אֵל כְּמֹשֶׁה אֲשֶׁר יְדָעוֹ יְהוָה פָּ
 נִים אֶל־פָּנִים׃\nVelo-kam navi od beyisra'el kemosheh as
 her yeda'o Adonai panim el-panim\nAnd there hath not arisen a prophet sinc
 e in Israel like unto Moses\, whom the LORD knew face to face\;\n\nNear th
 e very end of the Torah: no prophet arose like Moses\, who knew God face t
 o face. Then we roll the scroll back and start again.\n\nOpen Aleph: https
 ://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270430@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270430
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270501
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 1:1
DESCRIPTION:בְּרֵאשִׁית בָּרָא אֱלֹהִים אֵת 
 הַשָּׁמַיִם וְאֵת הָאָרֶץ׃\nBereshit bara Elohim e
 t hashamayim ve'et ha'aretz\nIn the beginning God created the heaven and t
 he earth.\n\nThe Torah opens with its first word\, Bereshit\, "in the begi
 nning." Everything that follows starts here: the world has a Maker\, and i
 t did not come about by chance.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrende
 r.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270501@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270501
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270502
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 1:3
DESCRIPTION:וַיֹּאמֶר אֱלֹהִים יְהִי אוֹר וַ
 יְהִי־אוֹר׃\nVayomer Elohim yehi or vayhi-or\nAnd God said: ‘
 Let there be light.’ And there was light.\n\nThe first thing God makes i
 s light\, and He makes it with words. In Judaism speech has real power\, s
 o the words we choose each day matter.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.
 onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270502@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270502
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270503
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 1:27
DESCRIPTION:וַיִּבְרָא אֱלֹהִים אֶת־הָאָדָם 
 בְּצַלְמוֹ בְּצֶלֶם אֱלֹהִים בָּרָא אֹת
 וֹ זָכָר וּנְקֵבָה בָּרָא אֹתָם׃\nVayivra Eloh
 im et-ha'adam betzalmo betzelem Elohim bara oto zakhar unekevah bara otam\
 nAnd God created man in His own image\, in the image of God created He him
 \; male and female created He them.\n\nEvery person is made in the image o
 f God. That is why each human life has worth\, whoever the person is and w
 herever they come from.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/
 morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270503@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270503
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270504
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 1:31
DESCRIPTION:וַיַּרְא אֱלֹהִים אֶת־כָּל־אֲשֶׁ
 ר עָשָׂה וְהִנֵּה־טוֹב מְאֹד וַיְהִי־עֶ
 רֶב וַיְהִי־בֹקֶר יוֹם הַשִּׁשִּׁי׃\nVayar
  Elohim et-kol-asher asah vehineh-tov me'od vayhi-erev vayhi-voker yom has
 hishi\nAnd God saw every thing that He had made\, and\, behold\, it was ve
 ry good. And there was evening and there was morning\, the sixth day.\n\nA
 fter each day God saw that it was good. On the sixth day\, with people in 
 the world\, it became "very good." Look for the good in your own day.\n\nO
 pen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270504@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270504
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270505
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 2:3
DESCRIPTION:וַיְבָרֶךְ אֱלֹהִים אֶת־יוֹם הַ
 שְּׁבִיעִי וַיְקַדֵּשׁ אֹתוֹ כִּי בוֹ 
 שָׁבַת מִכָּל־מְלַאכְתּוֹ אֲשֶׁר־בָּרָ
 א אֱלֹהִים לַעֲשׂוֹת׃\nVayvarekh Elohim et-yom hashevi'
 i vaykadesh oto ki vo shavat mikol-melakhto asher-bara Elohim la'asot\nAnd
  God blessed the seventh day\, and hallowed it\; because that in it He res
 ted from all His work which God in creating had made.\n\nThis is the first
  Shabbat. God rested on the seventh day and made it holy\, and we rest on 
 it too. Shabbat is a gift of time\, not only a rule.\n\nOpen Aleph: https:
 //alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270505@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270505
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270506
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 2:15
DESCRIPTION:וַיִּקַּח יְהוָה אֱלֹהִים אֶת־הָ
 אָדָם וַיַּנִּחֵהוּ בְגַן־עֵדֶן לְעָבְ
 דָהּ וּלְשָׁמְרָהּ׃\nVayikach Adonai Elohim et-ha'adam v
 ayanichehu vegan-eden le'avedah uleshamerah\nAnd the LORD God took the man
 \, and put him into the garden of Eden to dress it and to keep it.\n\nAdam
  was put in the garden to work it and to guard it. The earth is placed in 
 our care\, and looking after it is part of our job.\n\nOpen Aleph: https:/
 /alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270506@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270506
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270507
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 2:18
DESCRIPTION:וַיֹּאמֶר יְהוָה אֱלֹהִים לֹא־טוֹ
 ב הֱיוֹת הָאָדָם לְבַדּוֹ אֶעֱשֶׂהּ־לּ
 וֹ עֵזֶר כְּנֶגְדּוֹ׃\nVayomer Adonai Elohim lo-tov hey
 ot ha'adam levado e'eseh-lo ezer kenegdo\nAnd the LORD God said: ‘It is 
 not good that the man should be alone\; I will make him a help meet for hi
 m.’\n\n"It is not good to be alone." People need each other. Community\,
  friendship and family are part of how we were made.\n\nOpen Aleph: https:
 //alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270507@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270507
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270508
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 4:9
DESCRIPTION:וַיֹּאמֶר יְהוָה אֶל־קַיִן אֵי הֶ
 בֶל אָחִיךָ וַיֹּאמֶר לֹא יָדַעְתִּי הֲ
 שֹׁמֵר אָחִי אָנֹכִי׃\nVayomer Adonai el-kayin ei hevel
  achikha vayomer lo yadati hashomer achi anokhi\nAnd the LORD said unto Ca
 in: ‘Where is Abel thy brother?’ And he said: ‘I know not\; am I my 
 brother’s keeper?’\n\nCain asks\, "Am I my brother's keeper?" The rest
  of the Torah answers yes. We are responsible for one another.\n\nOpen Ale
 ph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270508@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270508
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270509
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 12:1
DESCRIPTION:וַיֹּאמֶר יְהוָה אֶל־אַבְרָם לֶךְ
 ־לְךָ מֵאַרְצְךָ וּמִמּוֹלַדְתְּךָ וּ
 מִבֵּית אָבִיךָ אֶל־הָאָרֶץ אֲשֶׁר אַרְ
 אֶךָּ׃\nVayomer Adonai el-Avram lekh-lekha me'artzekha umimoladtekha
  umibeit avikha el-ha'aretz asher ar'eka\nNow the LORD said unto Abram: 
 ‘Get thee out of thy country\, and from thy kindred\, and from thy fathe
 r’s house\, unto the land that I will show thee.\n\nLech lecha: "go for 
 yourself." Abraham leaves everything familiar to follow God. Every new sta
 rt\, including learning Hebrew\, takes a first step like this.\n\nOpen Ale
 ph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270509@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270509
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270510
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 12:2
DESCRIPTION:וְאֶעֶשְׂךָ לְגוֹי גָּדוֹל וַאֲבָ
 רֶכְךָ וַאֲגַדְּלָה שְׁמֶךָ וֶהְיֵה בְּ
 רָכָה׃\nVe'e'eskha legoy gadol va'avarekhkha va'agadelah shemekha ve
 hyeh berakhah\nAnd I will make of thee a great nation\, and I will bless t
 hee\, and make thy name great\; and be thou a blessing.\n\nAbraham is told
  not only that he will be blessed but that he will be a blessing. A good l
 ife is one that brings good to others.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.
 onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270510@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270510
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270511
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 15:5
DESCRIPTION:וַיּוֹצֵא אֹתוֹ הַחוּצָה וַיֹּאמֶ
 ר הַבֶּט־נָא הַשָּׁמַיְמָה וּסְפֹר הַכּ
 וֹכָבִים אִם־תּוּכַל לִסְפֹּר אֹתָם וַ
 יֹּאמֶר לוֹ כֹּה יִהְיֶה זַרְעֶךָ׃\nVayotze 
 oto hachutzah vayomer habet-na hashamaymah usefor hakokhavim im-tukhal lis
 por otam vayomer lo koh yihyeh zar'ekha\nAnd He brought him forth abroad\,
  and said: ‘Look now toward heaven\, and count the stars\, if thou be ab
 le to count them’\; and He said unto him: ‘So shall thy seed be.’\n\
 nGod takes Abraham outside to count the stars. When things feel small or u
 ncertain\, step back and look at the bigger picture.\n\nOpen Aleph: https:
 //alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270511@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270511
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270512
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 18:25
DESCRIPTION:חָלִלָה לְּךָ מֵעֲשֹׂת כַּדָּבָר 
 הַזֶּה לְהָמִית צַדִּיק עִם־רָשָׁע וְהָ
 יָה כַצַדִּיק כָּרָשָׁע חָלִלָה לָּךְ 
 הֲשֹׁפֵט כָּל־הָאָרֶץ לֹא יַעֲשֶׂה מִ
 שְׁפָּט׃\nChalilah lekha me'asot kadavar hazeh lehamit tzadik im-r
 asha vehayah khatzadik karasha chalilah lakh hashofet kol-ha'aretz lo ya'a
 seh mishpat\nThat be far from Thee to do after this manner\, to slay the r
 ighteous with the wicked\, that so the righteous should be as the wicked\;
  that be far from Thee\; shall not the judge of all the earth do justly?
 ’\n\nAbraham argues with God to save the people of Sodom. In Jewish trad
 ition it is right to speak up for justice\, even before the highest author
 ity.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270512@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270512
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270513
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 28:15
DESCRIPTION:וְהִנֵּה אָנֹכִי עִמָּךְ וּשְׁמַ
 רְתִּיךָ בְּכֹל אֲשֶׁר־תֵּלֵךְ וַהֲשִׁ
 בֹתִיךָ אֶל־הָאֲדָמָה הַזֹּאת כִּי לֹא 
 אֶעֱזָבְךָ עַד אֲשֶׁר אִם־עָשִׂיתִי אֵת
  אֲשֶׁר־דִּבַּרְתִּי לָךְ׃\nVehineh anokhi imakh u
 shemartikha bekhol asher-telekh vahashivotikha el-ha'adamah hazot ki lo e'
 ezavekha ad asher im-asiti et asher-dibarti lakh\nAnd\, behold\, I am with
  thee\, and will keep thee whithersoever thou goest\, and will bring thee 
 back into this land\; for I will not leave thee\, until I have done that w
 hich I have spoken to thee of.’\n\nJacob is alone and running away\, and
  God promises: I am with you\, wherever you go. You are never as alone as 
 you feel.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270513@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270513
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270514
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 28:16
DESCRIPTION:וַיִּיקַץ יַעֲקֹב מִשְּׁנָתוֹ וַ
 יֹּאמֶר אָכֵן יֵשׁ יְהוָה בַּמָּקוֹם הַ
 זֶּה וְאָנֹכִי לֹא יָדָעְתִּי׃\nVayikatz Ya'ako
 v mishenato vayomer akhen yesh Adonai bamakom hazeh ve'anokhi lo yada'eti\
 nAnd Jacob awaked out of his sleep\, and he said: ‘Surely the LORD is in
  this place\; and I knew it not.’\n\nJacob wakes from his dream and says
  God was in this place and he did not know it. Holiness can be right where
  you are\, if you notice it.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.c
 om/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270514@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270514
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270515
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 32:11
DESCRIPTION:קָטֹנְתִּי מִכֹּל הַחֲסָדִים וּמִ
 כָּל־הָאֱמֶת אֲשֶׁר עָשִׂיתָ אֶת־עַבְ
 דֶּךָ כִּי בְמַקְלִי עָבַרְתִּי אֶת־הַ
 יַּרְדֵּן הַזֶּה וְעַתָּה הָיִיתִי לִ
 שְׁנֵי מַחֲנוֹת׃\nKatoneti mikol hachasadim umikol-ha'emet 
 asher asita et-avdekha ki vemakli avarti et-hayarden hazeh ve'atah hayiti 
 lishnei machanot\nI am not worthy of all the mercies\, and of all the trut
 h\, which Thou hast shown unto Thy servant\; for with my staff I passed ov
 er this Jordan\; and now I am become two camps.\n\nBefore meeting his brot
 her Esau\, Jacob says he is not worthy of all the kindness he has received
 . Gratitude and humility go together.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.o
 nrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270515@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270515
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270516
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 45:4
DESCRIPTION:וַיֹּאמֶר יוֹסֵף אֶל־אֶחָיו גְּשׁ
 וּ־נָא אֵלַי וַיִּגָּשׁוּ וַיֹּאמֶר אֲ
 נִי יוֹסֵף אֲחִיכֶם אֲשֶׁר־מְכַרְתֶּם 
 אֹתִי מִצְרָיְמָה׃\nVayomer yosef el-echav geshu-na elai 
 vayigashu vayomer ani yosef achikhem asher-mekhartem oti mitzrayemah\nAnd 
 Joseph said unto his brethren: ‘Come near to me\, I pray you.’ And the
 y came near. And he said: ‘I am Joseph your brother\, whom ye sold into 
 Egypt.\n\nJoseph says to the brothers who sold him\, "Come close to me." I
 t is one of the great moments of forgiveness in the Torah.\n\nOpen Aleph: 
 https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270516@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270516
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270517
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 50:20
DESCRIPTION:וְאַתֶּם חֲשַׁבְתֶּם עָלַי רָעָה 
 אֱלֹהִים חֲשָׁבָהּ לְטֹבָה לְמַעַן עֲ
 שֹׂה כַּיּוֹם הַזֶּה לְהַחֲיֹת עַם־רָב׃
 \nVe'atem chashavtem alai ra'ah Elohim chashavah letovah lema'an asoh kayo
 m hazeh lehachayot am-rav\nAnd as for you\, ye meant evil against me\; but
  God meant it for good\, to bring to pass\, as it is this day\, to save mu
 ch people alive.\n\nJoseph tells his brothers that what they meant for har
 m\, God turned to good. Hard chapters of a life can lead somewhere good.\n
 \nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270517@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270517
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270518
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 3:5
DESCRIPTION:וַיֹּאמֶר אַל־תִּקְרַב הֲלֹם שַׁל
 ־נְעָלֶיךָ מֵעַל רַגְלֶיךָ כִּי הַמָּק
 וֹם אֲשֶׁר אַתָּה עוֹמֵד עָלָיו אַדְמַת
 ־קֹדֶשׁ הוּא׃\nVayomer al-tikrav halom shal-ne'alekha me'al ra
 glekha ki hamakom asher atah omed alav admat-kodesh hu\nAnd He said: ‘Dr
 aw not nigh hither\; put off thy shoes from off thy feet\, for the place w
 hereon thou standest is holy ground.’\n\nAt the burning bush Moses is to
 ld to take off his shoes\, because the ground is holy. Some moments call f
 or us to slow down and pay attention.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.o
 nrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270518@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270518
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270519
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 3:14
DESCRIPTION:וַיֹּאמֶר אֱלֹהִים אֶל־מֹשֶׁה אֶ
 הְיֶה אֲשֶׁר אֶהְיֶה וַיֹּאמֶר כֹּה תֹא
 מַר לִבְנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל אֶהְיֶה שְׁלָחַ
 נִי אֲלֵיכֶם׃\nVayomer Elohim el-Mosheh ehyeh asher ehyeh vayo
 mer koh tomar livnei Yisra'el ehyeh shelachani aleikhem\nAnd God said unto
  Moses: ‘I AM THAT I AM’\; and He said: ‘Thus shalt thou say unto th
 e children of Israel: I AM hath sent me unto you.’\n\nEhyeh asher ehyeh:
  "I will be what I will be." God's name here is about being present\, in e
 very time and place.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/mor
 ning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270519@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270519
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270520
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 13:8
DESCRIPTION:וְהִגַּדְתָּ לְבִנְךָ בַּיּוֹם הַ
 הוּא לֵאמֹר בַּעֲבוּר זֶה עָשָׂה יְהוָה 
 לִי בְּצֵאתִי מִמִּצְרָיִם׃\nVehigadta levinkha b
 ayom hahu lemor ba'avur zeh asah Adonai li betzeti mimitzrayim\nAnd thou s
 halt tell thy son in that day\, saying: It is because of that which the LO
 RD did for me when I came forth out of Egypt.\n\nThis verse is why we tell
  the Passover story at the Seder. Each generation tells it as if it happen
 ed to them.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270520@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270520
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270521
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 14:14
DESCRIPTION:יְהוָה יִלָּחֵם לָכֶם וְאַתֶּם 
 תַּחֲרִישׁוּן׃\nAdonai yilachem lakhem ve'atem tacharishun\n
 The LORD will fight for you\, and ye shall hold your peace.’\n\nAt the S
 ea of Reeds\, Moses tells the frightened people that God will fight for th
 em. Sometimes the right move is to stay calm and trust.\n\nOpen Aleph: htt
 ps://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270521@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270521
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270522
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 15:2
DESCRIPTION:עָזִּי וְזִמְרָת יָהּ וַיְהִי־לִי
  לִישׁוּעָה זֶה אֵלִי וְאַנְוֵהוּ אֱלֹ
 הֵי אָבִי וַאֲרֹמְמֶנְהוּ׃\nAzi vezimrat yah vayhi
 -li lishu'ah zeh eli ve'anvehu elohei avi va'aromemenhu\nThe LORD is my st
 rength and song\, And He is become my salvation\; This is my God\, and I w
 ill glorify Him\; My father’s God\, and I will exalt Him.\n\nFrom the So
 ng at the Sea: "The Lord is my strength and my song." These words are sung
  in synagogue every morning.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.c
 om/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270522@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270522
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270523
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 15:11
DESCRIPTION:מִי־כָמֹכָה בָּאֵלִם יְהוָה מִי 
 כָּמֹכָה נֶאְדָּר בַּקֹּדֶשׁ נוֹרָא תְ
 הִלֹּת עֹשֵׂה פֶלֶא׃\nMi-khamokhah ba'elim Adonai mi kam
 okhah nedar bakodesh nora tehilot oseh fele\nWho is like unto Thee\, O LOR
 D\, among the mighty? Who is like unto Thee\, glorious in holiness\, Fearf
 ul in praises\, doing wonders?\n\nMi chamocha\, "Who is like You?" This li
 ne from the Song at the Sea is part of the daily prayers\, just after the 
 Shema.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270523@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270523
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270524
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 19:6
DESCRIPTION:וְאַתֶּם תִּהְיוּ־לִי מַמְלֶכֶת 
 כֹּהֲנִים וְגוֹי קָדוֹשׁ אֵלֶּה הַדְּבָ
 רִים אֲשֶׁר תְּדַבֵּר אֶל־בְּנֵי יִשְׂ
 רָאֵל׃\nVe'atem tihyu-li mamlekhet kohanim vegoy kadosh eleh hadevar
 im asher tedaber el-benei Yisra'el\nand ye shall be unto Me a kingdom of p
 riests\, and a holy nation. These are the words which thou shalt speak unt
 o the children of Israel.’\n\nAt Sinai the whole people is called a king
 dom of priests and a holy nation. Holiness is meant for everyone\, not onl
 y for a few.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270524@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270524
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270525
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 20:2
DESCRIPTION:אָנֹכִי יְהוָה אֱלֹהֶיךָ אֲשֶׁר ה
 וֹצֵאתִיךָ מֵאֶרֶץ מִצְרַיִם מִבֵּית עֲ
 בָדִים׃\nAnokhi Adonai Elohekha asher hotzetikha me'eretz Mitzrayim
  mibeit avadim\nI am the LORD thy God\, who brought thee out of the land o
 f Egypt\, out of the house of bondage.\n\nThe Ten Commandments begin with 
 who God is: the One who brought us out of slavery. Freedom comes first\, a
 nd the commandments follow.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.co
 m/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270525@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270525
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270526
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 20:8
DESCRIPTION:זָכוֹר אֶת־יוֹם הַשַׁבָּת לְקַדְּ
 שׁוֹ\nZakhor et-yom hashabat lekadesho\nRemember the sabbath day\, to 
 keep it holy.\n\nZachor: "Remember the Shabbat day." We remember it with c
 andles\, Kiddush\, rest and time with the people we love.\n\nOpen Aleph: h
 ttps://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270526@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270526
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270527
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 20:12
DESCRIPTION:כַּבֵּד אֶת־אָבִיךָ וְאֶת־אִמֶּ
 ךָ לְמַעַן יַאֲרִכוּן יָמֶיךָ עַל הָאֲ
 דָמָה אֲשֶׁר־יְהוָה אֱלֹהֶיךָ נֹתֵן לָ
 ךְ׃\nKabed et-avikha ve'et-imekha lema'an ya'arikhun yamekha al ha'adam
 ah asher-Adonai Elohekha noten lakh\nHonour thy father and thy mother\, th
 at thy days may be long upon the land which the LORD thy God giveth thee.\
 n\nHonour your father and your mother. It is one of the Ten Commandments\,
  and the first that comes with a promise of long life.\n\nOpen Aleph: http
 s://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270527@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270527
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270528
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 22:20
DESCRIPTION:וְגֵר לֹא־תוֹנֶה וְלֹא תִלְחָצֶנּ
 וּ כִּי־גֵרִים הֱיִיתֶם בְּאֶרֶץ מִצְרָ
 יִם׃\nVeger lo-toneh velo tilchatzenu ki-gerim heyitem be'eretz Mitzra
 yim\nAnd a stranger shalt thou not wrong\, neither shalt thou oppress him\
 ; for ye were strangers in the land of Egypt.\n\nDo not wrong the stranger
 \, because you were strangers in Egypt. This idea comes up again and again
  in the Torah.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270528@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270528
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270529
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 23:2
DESCRIPTION:לֹא־תִהְיֶה אַחֲרֵי־רַבִּים לְרָ
 עֹת וְלֹא־תַעֲנֶה עַל־רִב לִנְטֹת אַחֲ
 רֵי רַבִּים לְהַטֹּת׃\nLo-tihyeh acharei-rabim lera'ot 
 velo-ta'aneh al-riv lintot acharei rabim lehatot\nThou shalt not follow a 
 multitude to do evil\; neither shalt thou bear witness in a cause to turn 
 aside after a multitude to pervert justice\;\n\nDo not follow the crowd to
  do wrong. Doing the right thing sometimes means standing apart.\n\nOpen A
 leph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270529@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270529
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270530
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 23:9
DESCRIPTION:וְגֵר לֹא תִלְחָץ וְאַתֶּם יְדַעְ
 תֶּם אֶת־נֶפֶשׁ הַגֵּר כִּי־גֵרִים הֱיִ
 יתֶם בְּאֶרֶץ מִצְרָיִם׃\nVeger lo tilchatz ve'atem 
 yedatem et-nefesh hager ki-gerim heyitem be'eretz Mitzrayim\nAnd a strange
 r shalt thou not oppress\; for ye know the heart of a stranger\, seeing ye
  were strangers in the land of Egypt.\n\n"You know the heart of the strang
 er." Our own history should make us kind to newcomers.\n\nOpen Aleph: http
 s://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270530@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270530
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270531
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 25:8
DESCRIPTION:וְעָשׂוּ לִי מִקְדָּשׁ וְשָׁכַנְ
 תִּי בְּתוֹכָם׃\nVe'asu li mikdash veshakhanti betokham\nAnd
  let them make Me a sanctuary\, that I may dwell among them.\n\n"Make Me a
  sanctuary\, and I will dwell among them." Not "in it\," but among them: G
 od lives among people\, in the places they make holy.\n\nOpen Aleph: https
 ://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270531@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270531
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270601
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 33:13
DESCRIPTION:וְעַתָּה אִם־נָא מָצָאתִי חֵן בְּ
 עֵינֶיךָ הוֹדִעֵנִי נָא אֶת־דְּרָכֶךָ 
 וְאֵדָעֲךָ לְמַעַן אֶמְצָא־חֵן בְּעֵי
 נֶיךָ וּרְאֵה כִּי עַמְּךָ הַגּוֹי הַ
 זֶּה׃\nVe'atah im-na matzati chen be'einekha hodi'eni na et-derakhekh
 a ve'eda'akha lema'an emtza-chen be'einekha ure'eh ki amekha hagoy hazeh\n
 Now therefore\, I pray Thee\, if I have found grace in Thy sight\, show me
  now Thy ways\, that I may know Thee\, to the end that I may find grace in
  Thy sight\; and consider that this nation is Thy people.’\n\nMoses asks
  God\, "Show me Your ways\, so that I may know You." Learning is one of th
 e ways Jews come close to God.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender
 .com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270601@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270601
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270602
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 34:6
DESCRIPTION:וַיַּעֲבֹר יְהוָה עַל־פָּנָיו וַ
 יִּקְרָא יְהוָה יְהוָה אֵל רַחוּם וְחַ
 נּוּן אֶרֶךְ אַפַּיִם וְרַב־חֶסֶד וֶאֱ
 מֶת\nVaya'avor Adonai al-panav vayikra Adonai Adonai el rachum vechanun
  erekh apayim verav-chesed ve'emet\nAnd the LORD passed by before him\, an
 d proclaimed: ‘The LORD\, the LORD\, God\, merciful and gracious\, long-
 suffering\, and abundant in goodness and truth\;\n\nThese are God's qualit
 ies of mercy\, sung on the High Holy Days: compassionate\, gracious\, slow
  to anger\, full of kindness and truth.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review
 .onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270602@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270602
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270603
SUMMARY:Torah: Leviticus 19:2
DESCRIPTION:דַּבֵּר אֶל־כָּל־עֲדַת בְּנֵי־יִ
 שְׂרָאֵל וְאָמַרְתָּ אֲלֵהֶם קְדֹשִׁים 
 תִּהְיוּ כִּי קָדוֹשׁ אֲנִי יְהוָה אֱלֹ
 הֵיכֶם׃\nDaber el-kol-adat benei-Yisra'el ve'amarta alehem kedoshim
  tihyu ki kadosh ani Adonai Eloheikhem\nSpeak unto all the congregation of
  the children of Israel\, and say unto them: Ye shall be holy\; for I the 
 LORD your God am holy.\n\n"You shall be holy\, for I am holy." The chapter
  that follows shows what that means: honesty\, kindness and fairness in ev
 eryday life.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270603@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270603
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270604
SUMMARY:Torah: Leviticus 19:3
DESCRIPTION:אִישׁ אִמּוֹ וְאָבִיו תִּירָאוּ 
 וְאֶת־שַׁבְּתֹתַי תִּשְׁמֹרוּ אֲנִי יְ
 הוָה אֱלֹהֵיכֶם׃\nIsh imo ve'aviv tira'u ve'et-shabetotai t
 ishmoru ani Adonai Eloheikhem\nYe shall fear every man his mother\, and hi
 s father\, and ye shall keep My sabbaths: I am the LORD your God.\n\nRespe
 ct your parents and keep Shabbat. Both are about honouring where we come f
 rom.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270604@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270604
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270605
SUMMARY:Torah: Leviticus 19:9
DESCRIPTION:וּבְקֻצְרְכֶם אֶת־קְצִיר אַרְצְ
 כֶם לֹא תְכַלֶּה פְּאַת שָׂדְךָ לִקְצֹר 
 וְלֶקֶט קְצִירְךָ לֹא תְלַקֵּט׃\nUvekutzrekhem
  et-ketzir artzekhem lo tekhaleh pe'at sadekha liktzor veleket ketzirekha 
 lo telaket\nAnd when ye reap the harvest of your land\, thou shalt not who
 lly reap the corner of thy field\, neither shalt thou gather the gleaning 
 of thy harvest.\n\nLeave the corners of your field for people in need. Giv
 ing to others is built right into how we earn and spend.\n\nOpen Aleph: ht
 tps://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270605@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270605
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270606
SUMMARY:Torah: Leviticus 19:14
DESCRIPTION:לֹא־תְקַלֵּל חֵרֵשׁ וְלִפְנֵי עִ
 וֵּר לֹא תִתֵּן מִכְשֹׁל וְיָרֵאתָ מֵּ
 אֱלֹהֶיךָ אֲנִי יְהוָה׃\nLo-tekalel cheresh velifnei 
 iver lo titen mikhshol veyareta me'Elohekha ani Adonai\nThou shalt not cur
 se the deaf\, nor put a stumbling-block before the blind\, but thou shalt 
 fear thy God: I am the LORD.\n\nDo not curse the deaf or put a stumbling b
 lock before the blind. Treat everyone with care\, especially those who can
 not defend themselves.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/m
 orning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270606@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270606
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270607
SUMMARY:Torah: Leviticus 19:16
DESCRIPTION:לֹא־תֵלֵךְ רָכִיל בְּעַמֶּיךָ לֹא
  תַעֲמֹד עַל־דַּם רֵעֶךָ אֲנִי יְהוָה׃\nL
 o-telekh rakhil be'amekha lo ta'amod al-dam re'ekha ani Adonai\nThou shalt
  not go up and down as a talebearer among thy people\; neither shalt thou 
 stand idly by the blood of thy neighbour: I am the LORD.\n\nDo not spread 
 gossip\, and do not stand by while your neighbour is in danger. Words can 
 hurt\, and silence can too.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.co
 m/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270607@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270607
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270608
SUMMARY:Torah: Leviticus 19:18
DESCRIPTION:לֹא־תִקֹּם וְלֹא־תִטֹּר אֶת־בְּ
 נֵי עַמֶּךָ וְאָהַבְתָּ לְרֵעֲךָ כָּמוֹ
 ךָ אֲנִי יְהוָה׃\nLo-tikom velo-titor et-benei amekha ve'aha
 vta lere'akha kamokha ani Adonai\nThou shalt not take vengeance\, nor bear
  any grudge against the children of thy people\, but thou shalt love thy n
 eighbour as thyself: I am the LORD.\n\n"Love your neighbour as yourself." 
 Rabbi Akiva called this the great principle of the whole Torah.\n\nOpen Al
 eph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270608@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270608
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270609
SUMMARY:Torah: Leviticus 19:32
DESCRIPTION:מִפְּנֵי שֵׂיבָה תָּקוּם וְהָדַרְ
 תָּ פְּנֵי זָקֵן וְיָרֵאתָ מֵּאֱלֹהֶיךָ
  אֲנִי יְהוָה׃\nMipenei seivah takum vehadarta penei zaken vey
 areta me'Elohekha ani Adonai\nThou shalt rise up before the hoary head\, a
 nd honour the face of the old man\, and thou shalt fear thy God: I am the 
 LORD.\n\nRise before the elderly and honour them. Age brings wisdom\, and 
 the Torah asks us to show it respect.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.o
 nrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270609@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270609
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270610
SUMMARY:Torah: Leviticus 25:10
DESCRIPTION:וְקִדַּשְׁתֶּם אֵת שְׁנַת הַחֲמִ
 שִּׁים שָׁנָה וּקְרָאתֶם דְּרוֹר בָּאָ
 רֶץ לְכָל־יֹשְׁבֶיהָ יוֹבֵל הִוא תִּהְ
 יֶה לָכֶם וְשַׁבְתֶּם אִישׁ אֶל־אֲחֻזָּ
 תוֹ וְאִישׁ אֶל־מִשְׁפַּחְתּוֹ תָּשֻׁב
 וּ׃\nVekidashtem et shenat hachamishim shanah ukeratem deror ba'aretz l
 ekhol-yosheveha yovel hiv tihyeh lakhem veshavtem ish el-achuzato ve'ish e
 l-mishpachto tashuvu\nAnd ye shall hallow the fiftieth year\, and proclaim
  liberty throughout the land unto all the inhabitants thereof\; it shall b
 e a jubilee unto you\; and ye shall return every man unto his possession\,
  and ye shall return every man unto his family.\n\n"Proclaim liberty throu
 ghout the land." These words about the Jubilee year are cast on the Libert
 y Bell in Philadelphia.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/
 morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270610@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270610
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270611
SUMMARY:Torah: Numbers 6:24
DESCRIPTION:יְבָרֶכְךָ יְהוָה וְיִשְׁמְרֶךָ׃\
 nYevarekhkha Adonai veyishmerekha\nThe LORD bless thee\, and keep thee\;\n
 \nThe first line of the Priestly Blessing\, still said in synagogues and b
 y parents to children on Friday night.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.
 onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270611@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270611
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270612
SUMMARY:Torah: Numbers 6:26
DESCRIPTION:יִשָּׂא יְהוָה פָּנָיו אֵלֶיךָ וְ
 יָשֵׂם לְךָ שָׁלוֹם׃\nYisa Adonai panav elekha veyasem l
 ekha shalom\nThe LORD lift up His countenance upon thee\, and give thee pe
 ace.\n\nThe Priestly Blessing ends with shalom\, peace. In Hebrew\, shalom
  also means wholeness: everything in its right place.\n\nOpen Aleph: https
 ://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270612@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270612
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270613
SUMMARY:Torah: Numbers 11:29
DESCRIPTION:וַיֹּאמֶר לוֹ מֹשֶׁה הַמְקַנֵּא 
 אַתָּה לִי וּמִי יִתֵּן כָּל־עַם יְהוָה 
 נְבִיאִים כִּי־יִתֵּן יְהוָה אֶת־רוּח
 וֹ עֲלֵיהֶם׃\nVayomer lo Mosheh hamkane atah li umi yiten kol-a
 m Adonai nevi'im ki-yiten Adonai et-rucho aleihem\nAnd Moses said unto him
 : ‘Art thou jealous for my sake? would that all the LORD’S people were
  prophets\, that the LORD would put His spirit upon them! ’\n\nWhen othe
 rs begin to prophesy\, Moses is not jealous. He wishes everyone could shar
 e God's spirit. Great leaders lift others up.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-
 review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270613@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270613
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270614
SUMMARY:Torah: Numbers 15:39
DESCRIPTION:וְהָיָה לָכֶם לְצִיצִת וּרְאִיתֶם
  אֹתוֹ וּזְכַרְתֶּם אֶת־כָּל־מִצְוֹת יְ
 הוָה וַעֲשִׂיתֶם אֹתָם וְלֹא־תָתֻרוּ אַ
 חֲרֵי לְבַבְכֶם וְאַחֲרֵי עֵינֵיכֶם אֲ
 שֶׁר־אַתֶּם זֹנִים אַחֲרֵיהֶם׃\nVehayah lakhem
  letzitzit ure'item oto uzekhartem et-kol-mitzvot Adonai va'asitem otam ve
 lo-taturu acharei levavkhem ve'acharei eineikhem asher-atem zonim achareih
 em\nAnd it shall be unto you for a fringe\, that ye may look upon it\, and
  remember all the commandments of the LORD\, and do them\; and that ye go 
 not about after your own heart and your own eyes\, after which ye use to g
 o astray\;\n\nThis verse is about the tzitzit\, the fringes on the tallit.
  Seeing them is a reminder of the commandments and of who we want to be.\n
 \nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270614@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270614
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270615
SUMMARY:Torah: Numbers 24:5
DESCRIPTION:מַה־טֹּבוּ אֹהָלֶיךָ יַעֲקֹב מִ
 שְׁכְּנֹתֶיךָ יִשְׂרָאֵל׃\nMah-tovu ohalekha Ya'ak
 ov mishkenotekha Yisra'el\nHow goodly are thy tents\, O Jacob\, Thy dwelli
 ngs\, O Israel!\n\nMah tovu\, "How good are your tents." Many synagogues o
 pen the morning service with these words.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-revi
 ew.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270615@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270615
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270616
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 4:9
DESCRIPTION:רַק הִשָּׁמֶר לְךָ וּשְׁמֹר נַפְ
 שְׁךָ מְאֹד פֶּן־תִּשְׁכַּח אֶת־הַדְּ
 בָרִים אֲשֶׁר־רָאוּ עֵינֶיךָ וּפֶן־יָס
 וּרוּ מִלְּבָבְךָ כֹּל יְמֵי חַיֶּיךָ 
 וְהוֹדַעְתָּם לְבָנֶיךָ וְלִבְנֵי בָנֶ
 יךָ׃\nRak hishamer lekha ushemor nafshekha me'od pen-tishkach et-hadev
 arim asher-ra'u einekha ufen-yasuru milevavekha kol yemei chayekha vehodat
 am levanekha velivnei vanekha\nOnly take heed to thyself\, and keep thy so
 ul diligently\, lest thou forget the things which thine eyes saw\, and les
 t they depart from thy heart all the days of thy life\; but make them know
 n unto thy children and thy children’s children\;\n\nDo not forget what 
 you have seen\, and teach it to your children and grandchildren. Memory is
  how a people stays alive.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com
 /#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270616@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270616
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270617
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 6:4
DESCRIPTION:שְׁמַע יִשְׂרָאֵל יְהוָה אֱלֹהֵינ
 וּ יְהוָה אֶחָד׃\nShema Yisra'el Adonai Eloheinu Adonai echa
 d\nHEAR\, O ISRAEL: THE LORD OUR GOD\, THE LORD IS ONE.\n\nThe Shema\, the
  central line of Jewish prayer: "Hear\, O Israel\, the Lord is our God\, t
 he Lord is One." It is said morning and night.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef
 -review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270617@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270617
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270618
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 6:5
DESCRIPTION:וְאָהַבְתָּ אֵת יְהוָה אֱלֹהֶיךָ 
 בְּכָל־לְבָבְךָ וּבְכָל־נַפְשְׁךָ וּבְ
 כָל־מְאֹדֶךָ׃\nVe'ahavta et Adonai Elohekha bekhol-levavekha 
 uvekhol-nafshekha uvekhol-me'odekha\nAnd thou shalt love the LORD thy God 
 with all thy heart\, and with all thy soul\, and with all thy might.\n\nV'
 ahavta: love God with all your heart\, all your soul and all your strength
 . Faith in Judaism is about love\, not only belief.\n\nOpen Aleph: https:/
 /alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270618@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270618
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270619
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 6:7
DESCRIPTION:וְשִׁנַּנְתָּם לְבָנֶיךָ וְדִבַּ
 רְתָּ בָּם בְּשִׁבְתְּךָ בְּבֵיתֶךָ וּ
 בְלֶכְתְּךָ בַדֶּרֶךְ וּבְשָׁכְבְּךָ 
 וּבְקוּמֶךָ׃\nVeshinantam levanekha vedibarta bam beshivtekha 
 beveitekha uvelekhtekha vaderekh uveshakhbekha uvekumekha\nand thou shalt 
 teach them diligently unto thy children\, and shalt talk of them when thou
  sittest in thy house\, and when thou walkest by the way\, and when thou l
 iest down\, and when thou risest up.\n\nTalk about these words at home\, o
 n the road\, when you lie down and when you get up. That is why the Shema 
 is said at bedtime and in the morning.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.
 onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270619@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270619
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270620
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 8:3
DESCRIPTION:וַיְעַנְּךָ וַיַּרְעִבֶךָ וַיַּ
 אֲכִלְךָ אֶת הַמָּן אֲשֶׁר לֹא־יָדַעְ
 תָּ וְלֹא יָדְעוּן אֲבֹתֶיךָ לְמַעַן ה
 וֹדִעֲךָ כִּי לֹא עַל־הַלֶּחֶם לְבַדּוֹ
  יִחְיֶה הָאָדָם כִּי עַל־כָּל־מוֹצָא 
 פִי־יְהוָה יִחְיֶה הָאָדָם׃\nVay'anekha vayar'ive
 kha vaya'akhilkha et haman asher lo-yadata velo yad'un avotekha lema'an ho
 di'akha ki lo al-halechem levado yichyeh ha'adam ki al-kol-motza fi-Adonai
  yichyeh ha'adam\nAnd He afflicted thee\, and suffered thee to hunger\, an
 d fed thee with manna\, which thou knewest not\, neither did thy fathers k
 now\; that He might make thee know that man doth not live by bread only\, 
 but by every thing that proceedeth out of the mouth of the LORD doth man l
 ive.\n\n"A person does not live by bread alone." We need meaning\, learnin
 g and purpose as much as food.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender
 .com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270620@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270620
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270621
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 8:10
DESCRIPTION:וְאָכַלְתָּ וְשָׂבָעְתָּ וּבֵרַ
 כְתָּ אֶת־יְהוָה אֱלֹהֶיךָ עַל־הָאָרֶץ 
 הַטֹּבָה אֲשֶׁר נָתַן־לָךְ׃\nVe'akhalta vesava'et
 a uverakhta et-Adonai Elohekha al-ha'aretz hatovah asher natan-lakh\nAnd t
 hou shalt eat and be satisfied\, and bless the LORD thy God for the good l
 and which He hath given thee.\n\nEat\, be satisfied\, and bless. This vers
 e is the source of Birkat Hamazon\, the blessing after meals.\n\nOpen Alep
 h: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270621@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270621
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270622
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 10:19
DESCRIPTION:וַאֲהַבְתֶּם אֶת־הַגֵּר כִּי־גֵ
 רִים הֱיִיתֶם בְּאֶרֶץ מִצְרָיִם׃\nVa'ahavte
 m et-hager ki-gerim heyitem be'eretz Mitzrayim\nLove ye therefore the stra
 nger\; for ye were strangers in the land of Egypt.\n\nLove the stranger\, 
 because you were strangers in Egypt. The Torah asks for more than not hurt
 ing newcomers\; it asks us to love them.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-revie
 w.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270622@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270622
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270623
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 16:20
DESCRIPTION:צֶדֶק צֶדֶק תִּרְדֹּף לְמַעַן תִּ
 חְיֶה וְיָרַשְׁתָּ אֶת־הָאָרֶץ אֲשֶׁר־
 יְהוָה אֱלֹהֶיךָ נֹתֵן לָךְ׃\nTzedek tzedek tirdo
 f lema'an tichyeh veyarashta et-ha'aretz asher-Adonai Elohekha noten lakh\
 nJustice\, justice shalt thou follow\, that thou mayest live\, and inherit
  the land which the LORD thy God giveth thee.\n\nTzedek tzedek tirdof: "Ju
 stice\, justice you shall pursue." The word is said twice\, to show how ha
 rd we should work for it.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/
 #/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270623@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270623
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270624
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 30:14
DESCRIPTION:כִּי־קָרוֹב אֵלֶיךָ הַדָּבָר מְאֹ
 ד בְּפִיךָ וּבִלְבָבְךָ לַעֲשֹׂתוֹ׃\nKi-ka
 rov elekha hadavar me'od befikha uvilvavekha la'asoto\nBut the word is ver
 y nigh unto thee\, in thy mouth\, and in thy heart\, that thou mayest do i
 t.\n\nThe Torah is not far away: it is in your mouth and in your heart. It
  is within reach\, one word at a time.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.
 onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270624@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270624
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270625
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 30:19
DESCRIPTION:הַעִידֹתִי בָכֶם הַיּוֹם אֶת־הַ
 שָּׁמַיִם וְאֶת־הָאָרֶץ הַחַיִּים וְהַ
 מָּוֶת נָתַתִּי לְפָנֶיךָ הַבְּרָכָה וְ
 הַקְּלָלָה וּבָחַרְתָּ בַּחַיִּים לְמַ
 עַן תִּחְיֶה אַתָּה וְזַרְעֶךָ׃\nHa'idoti vakh
 em hayom et-hashamayim ve'et-ha'aretz hachayim vehamavet natati lefanekha 
 haberakhah vehakelalah uvacharta bachayim lema'an tichyeh atah vezar'ekha\
 nI call heaven and earth to witness against you this day\, that I have set
  before thee life and death\, the blessing and the curse\; therefore choos
 e life\, that thou mayest live\, thou and thy seed\;\n\n"Choose life." Eve
 ry day brings choices\, and the Torah asks us to choose the ones that lead
  to life and blessing.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/m
 orning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270625@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270625
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270626
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 31:6
DESCRIPTION:חִזְקוּ וְאִמְצוּ אַל־תִּירְאוּ 
 וְאַל־תַּעַרְצוּ מִפְּנֵיהֶם כִּי יְה
 וָה אֱלֹהֶיךָ הוּא הַהֹלֵךְ עִמָּךְ לֹא 
 יַרְפְּךָ וְלֹא יַעַזְבֶךָּ׃\nChizku ve'imtzu al
 -tir'u ve'al-ta'artzu mipeneihem ki Adonai Elohekha hu haholekh imakh lo y
 arpekha velo ya'azveka\nBe strong and of good courage\, fear not\, nor be 
 affrighted at them\; for the LORD thy God\, He it is that doth go with the
 e\; He will not fail thee\, nor forsake thee.’\n\nChazak ve'ematz: "Be s
 trong and of good courage." Moses says this before the people enter the la
 nd without him.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270626@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270626
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270627
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 6:6
DESCRIPTION:וְהָיוּ הַדְּבָרִים הָאֵלֶּה אֲ
 שֶׁר אָנֹכִי מְצַוְּךָ הַיּוֹם עַל־לְבָ
 בֶךָ׃\nVehayu hadevarim ha'eleh asher anokhi metzavekha hayom al-leva
 vekha\nAnd these words\, which I command thee this day\, shall be upon thy
  heart\;\n\n"These words shall be upon your heart." Learning Torah is mean
 t to go deeper than memory\, into who we are.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-
 review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270627@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270627
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270628
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 31:16
DESCRIPTION:וְשָׁמְרוּ בְנֵי־יִשְׂרָאֵל אֶת־
 הַשַּׁבָּת לַעֲשׂוֹת אֶת־הַשַּׁבָּת לְ
 דֹרֹתָם בְּרִית עוֹלָם׃\nVeshamru venei-Yisra'el et-h
 ashabat la'asot et-hashabat ledorotam berit olam\nWherefore the children o
 f Israel shall keep the sabbath\, to observe the sabbath throughout their 
 generations\, for a perpetual covenant.\n\nV'shamru: the people of Israel 
 shall keep the Shabbat for all generations. This verse is sung on Friday n
 ight and Shabbat morning.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/
 #/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270628@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270628
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270629
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 34:10
DESCRIPTION:וְלֹא־קָם נָבִיא עוֹד בְּיִשְׂרָ
 אֵל כְּמֹשֶׁה אֲשֶׁר יְדָעוֹ יְהוָה פָּ
 נִים אֶל־פָּנִים׃\nVelo-kam navi od beyisra'el kemosheh as
 her yeda'o Adonai panim el-panim\nAnd there hath not arisen a prophet sinc
 e in Israel like unto Moses\, whom the LORD knew face to face\;\n\nNear th
 e very end of the Torah: no prophet arose like Moses\, who knew God face t
 o face. Then we roll the scroll back and start again.\n\nOpen Aleph: https
 ://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270629@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270629
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270630
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 1:1
DESCRIPTION:בְּרֵאשִׁית בָּרָא אֱלֹהִים אֵת 
 הַשָּׁמַיִם וְאֵת הָאָרֶץ׃\nBereshit bara Elohim e
 t hashamayim ve'et ha'aretz\nIn the beginning God created the heaven and t
 he earth.\n\nThe Torah opens with its first word\, Bereshit\, "in the begi
 nning." Everything that follows starts here: the world has a Maker\, and i
 t did not come about by chance.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrende
 r.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270630@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270630
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270701
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 1:3
DESCRIPTION:וַיֹּאמֶר אֱלֹהִים יְהִי אוֹר וַ
 יְהִי־אוֹר׃\nVayomer Elohim yehi or vayhi-or\nAnd God said: ‘
 Let there be light.’ And there was light.\n\nThe first thing God makes i
 s light\, and He makes it with words. In Judaism speech has real power\, s
 o the words we choose each day matter.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.
 onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270701@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270701
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270702
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 1:27
DESCRIPTION:וַיִּבְרָא אֱלֹהִים אֶת־הָאָדָם 
 בְּצַלְמוֹ בְּצֶלֶם אֱלֹהִים בָּרָא אֹת
 וֹ זָכָר וּנְקֵבָה בָּרָא אֹתָם׃\nVayivra Eloh
 im et-ha'adam betzalmo betzelem Elohim bara oto zakhar unekevah bara otam\
 nAnd God created man in His own image\, in the image of God created He him
 \; male and female created He them.\n\nEvery person is made in the image o
 f God. That is why each human life has worth\, whoever the person is and w
 herever they come from.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/
 morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270702@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270702
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270703
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 1:31
DESCRIPTION:וַיַּרְא אֱלֹהִים אֶת־כָּל־אֲשֶׁ
 ר עָשָׂה וְהִנֵּה־טוֹב מְאֹד וַיְהִי־עֶ
 רֶב וַיְהִי־בֹקֶר יוֹם הַשִּׁשִּׁי׃\nVayar
  Elohim et-kol-asher asah vehineh-tov me'od vayhi-erev vayhi-voker yom has
 hishi\nAnd God saw every thing that He had made\, and\, behold\, it was ve
 ry good. And there was evening and there was morning\, the sixth day.\n\nA
 fter each day God saw that it was good. On the sixth day\, with people in 
 the world\, it became "very good." Look for the good in your own day.\n\nO
 pen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270703@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270703
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270704
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 2:3
DESCRIPTION:וַיְבָרֶךְ אֱלֹהִים אֶת־יוֹם הַ
 שְּׁבִיעִי וַיְקַדֵּשׁ אֹתוֹ כִּי בוֹ 
 שָׁבַת מִכָּל־מְלַאכְתּוֹ אֲשֶׁר־בָּרָ
 א אֱלֹהִים לַעֲשׂוֹת׃\nVayvarekh Elohim et-yom hashevi'
 i vaykadesh oto ki vo shavat mikol-melakhto asher-bara Elohim la'asot\nAnd
  God blessed the seventh day\, and hallowed it\; because that in it He res
 ted from all His work which God in creating had made.\n\nThis is the first
  Shabbat. God rested on the seventh day and made it holy\, and we rest on 
 it too. Shabbat is a gift of time\, not only a rule.\n\nOpen Aleph: https:
 //alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270704@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270704
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270705
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 2:15
DESCRIPTION:וַיִּקַּח יְהוָה אֱלֹהִים אֶת־הָ
 אָדָם וַיַּנִּחֵהוּ בְגַן־עֵדֶן לְעָבְ
 דָהּ וּלְשָׁמְרָהּ׃\nVayikach Adonai Elohim et-ha'adam v
 ayanichehu vegan-eden le'avedah uleshamerah\nAnd the LORD God took the man
 \, and put him into the garden of Eden to dress it and to keep it.\n\nAdam
  was put in the garden to work it and to guard it. The earth is placed in 
 our care\, and looking after it is part of our job.\n\nOpen Aleph: https:/
 /alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270705@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270705
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270706
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 2:18
DESCRIPTION:וַיֹּאמֶר יְהוָה אֱלֹהִים לֹא־טוֹ
 ב הֱיוֹת הָאָדָם לְבַדּוֹ אֶעֱשֶׂהּ־לּ
 וֹ עֵזֶר כְּנֶגְדּוֹ׃\nVayomer Adonai Elohim lo-tov hey
 ot ha'adam levado e'eseh-lo ezer kenegdo\nAnd the LORD God said: ‘It is 
 not good that the man should be alone\; I will make him a help meet for hi
 m.’\n\n"It is not good to be alone." People need each other. Community\,
  friendship and family are part of how we were made.\n\nOpen Aleph: https:
 //alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270706@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270706
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270707
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 4:9
DESCRIPTION:וַיֹּאמֶר יְהוָה אֶל־קַיִן אֵי הֶ
 בֶל אָחִיךָ וַיֹּאמֶר לֹא יָדַעְתִּי הֲ
 שֹׁמֵר אָחִי אָנֹכִי׃\nVayomer Adonai el-kayin ei hevel
  achikha vayomer lo yadati hashomer achi anokhi\nAnd the LORD said unto Ca
 in: ‘Where is Abel thy brother?’ And he said: ‘I know not\; am I my 
 brother’s keeper?’\n\nCain asks\, "Am I my brother's keeper?" The rest
  of the Torah answers yes. We are responsible for one another.\n\nOpen Ale
 ph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270707@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270707
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270708
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 12:1
DESCRIPTION:וַיֹּאמֶר יְהוָה אֶל־אַבְרָם לֶךְ
 ־לְךָ מֵאַרְצְךָ וּמִמּוֹלַדְתְּךָ וּ
 מִבֵּית אָבִיךָ אֶל־הָאָרֶץ אֲשֶׁר אַרְ
 אֶךָּ׃\nVayomer Adonai el-Avram lekh-lekha me'artzekha umimoladtekha
  umibeit avikha el-ha'aretz asher ar'eka\nNow the LORD said unto Abram: 
 ‘Get thee out of thy country\, and from thy kindred\, and from thy fathe
 r’s house\, unto the land that I will show thee.\n\nLech lecha: "go for 
 yourself." Abraham leaves everything familiar to follow God. Every new sta
 rt\, including learning Hebrew\, takes a first step like this.\n\nOpen Ale
 ph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270708@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270708
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270709
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 12:2
DESCRIPTION:וְאֶעֶשְׂךָ לְגוֹי גָּדוֹל וַאֲבָ
 רֶכְךָ וַאֲגַדְּלָה שְׁמֶךָ וֶהְיֵה בְּ
 רָכָה׃\nVe'e'eskha legoy gadol va'avarekhkha va'agadelah shemekha ve
 hyeh berakhah\nAnd I will make of thee a great nation\, and I will bless t
 hee\, and make thy name great\; and be thou a blessing.\n\nAbraham is told
  not only that he will be blessed but that he will be a blessing. A good l
 ife is one that brings good to others.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.
 onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270709@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270709
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270710
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 15:5
DESCRIPTION:וַיּוֹצֵא אֹתוֹ הַחוּצָה וַיֹּאמֶ
 ר הַבֶּט־נָא הַשָּׁמַיְמָה וּסְפֹר הַכּ
 וֹכָבִים אִם־תּוּכַל לִסְפֹּר אֹתָם וַ
 יֹּאמֶר לוֹ כֹּה יִהְיֶה זַרְעֶךָ׃\nVayotze 
 oto hachutzah vayomer habet-na hashamaymah usefor hakokhavim im-tukhal lis
 por otam vayomer lo koh yihyeh zar'ekha\nAnd He brought him forth abroad\,
  and said: ‘Look now toward heaven\, and count the stars\, if thou be ab
 le to count them’\; and He said unto him: ‘So shall thy seed be.’\n\
 nGod takes Abraham outside to count the stars. When things feel small or u
 ncertain\, step back and look at the bigger picture.\n\nOpen Aleph: https:
 //alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270710@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270710
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270711
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 18:25
DESCRIPTION:חָלִלָה לְּךָ מֵעֲשֹׂת כַּדָּבָר 
 הַזֶּה לְהָמִית צַדִּיק עִם־רָשָׁע וְהָ
 יָה כַצַדִּיק כָּרָשָׁע חָלִלָה לָּךְ 
 הֲשֹׁפֵט כָּל־הָאָרֶץ לֹא יַעֲשֶׂה מִ
 שְׁפָּט׃\nChalilah lekha me'asot kadavar hazeh lehamit tzadik im-r
 asha vehayah khatzadik karasha chalilah lakh hashofet kol-ha'aretz lo ya'a
 seh mishpat\nThat be far from Thee to do after this manner\, to slay the r
 ighteous with the wicked\, that so the righteous should be as the wicked\;
  that be far from Thee\; shall not the judge of all the earth do justly?
 ’\n\nAbraham argues with God to save the people of Sodom. In Jewish trad
 ition it is right to speak up for justice\, even before the highest author
 ity.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270711@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270711
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270712
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 28:15
DESCRIPTION:וְהִנֵּה אָנֹכִי עִמָּךְ וּשְׁמַ
 רְתִּיךָ בְּכֹל אֲשֶׁר־תֵּלֵךְ וַהֲשִׁ
 בֹתִיךָ אֶל־הָאֲדָמָה הַזֹּאת כִּי לֹא 
 אֶעֱזָבְךָ עַד אֲשֶׁר אִם־עָשִׂיתִי אֵת
  אֲשֶׁר־דִּבַּרְתִּי לָךְ׃\nVehineh anokhi imakh u
 shemartikha bekhol asher-telekh vahashivotikha el-ha'adamah hazot ki lo e'
 ezavekha ad asher im-asiti et asher-dibarti lakh\nAnd\, behold\, I am with
  thee\, and will keep thee whithersoever thou goest\, and will bring thee 
 back into this land\; for I will not leave thee\, until I have done that w
 hich I have spoken to thee of.’\n\nJacob is alone and running away\, and
  God promises: I am with you\, wherever you go. You are never as alone as 
 you feel.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270712@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270712
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270713
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 28:16
DESCRIPTION:וַיִּיקַץ יַעֲקֹב מִשְּׁנָתוֹ וַ
 יֹּאמֶר אָכֵן יֵשׁ יְהוָה בַּמָּקוֹם הַ
 זֶּה וְאָנֹכִי לֹא יָדָעְתִּי׃\nVayikatz Ya'ako
 v mishenato vayomer akhen yesh Adonai bamakom hazeh ve'anokhi lo yada'eti\
 nAnd Jacob awaked out of his sleep\, and he said: ‘Surely the LORD is in
  this place\; and I knew it not.’\n\nJacob wakes from his dream and says
  God was in this place and he did not know it. Holiness can be right where
  you are\, if you notice it.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.c
 om/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270713@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270713
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270714
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 32:11
DESCRIPTION:קָטֹנְתִּי מִכֹּל הַחֲסָדִים וּמִ
 כָּל־הָאֱמֶת אֲשֶׁר עָשִׂיתָ אֶת־עַבְ
 דֶּךָ כִּי בְמַקְלִי עָבַרְתִּי אֶת־הַ
 יַּרְדֵּן הַזֶּה וְעַתָּה הָיִיתִי לִ
 שְׁנֵי מַחֲנוֹת׃\nKatoneti mikol hachasadim umikol-ha'emet 
 asher asita et-avdekha ki vemakli avarti et-hayarden hazeh ve'atah hayiti 
 lishnei machanot\nI am not worthy of all the mercies\, and of all the trut
 h\, which Thou hast shown unto Thy servant\; for with my staff I passed ov
 er this Jordan\; and now I am become two camps.\n\nBefore meeting his brot
 her Esau\, Jacob says he is not worthy of all the kindness he has received
 . Gratitude and humility go together.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.o
 nrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270714@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270714
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270715
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 45:4
DESCRIPTION:וַיֹּאמֶר יוֹסֵף אֶל־אֶחָיו גְּשׁ
 וּ־נָא אֵלַי וַיִּגָּשׁוּ וַיֹּאמֶר אֲ
 נִי יוֹסֵף אֲחִיכֶם אֲשֶׁר־מְכַרְתֶּם 
 אֹתִי מִצְרָיְמָה׃\nVayomer yosef el-echav geshu-na elai 
 vayigashu vayomer ani yosef achikhem asher-mekhartem oti mitzrayemah\nAnd 
 Joseph said unto his brethren: ‘Come near to me\, I pray you.’ And the
 y came near. And he said: ‘I am Joseph your brother\, whom ye sold into 
 Egypt.\n\nJoseph says to the brothers who sold him\, "Come close to me." I
 t is one of the great moments of forgiveness in the Torah.\n\nOpen Aleph: 
 https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270715@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270715
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270716
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 50:20
DESCRIPTION:וְאַתֶּם חֲשַׁבְתֶּם עָלַי רָעָה 
 אֱלֹהִים חֲשָׁבָהּ לְטֹבָה לְמַעַן עֲ
 שֹׂה כַּיּוֹם הַזֶּה לְהַחֲיֹת עַם־רָב׃
 \nVe'atem chashavtem alai ra'ah Elohim chashavah letovah lema'an asoh kayo
 m hazeh lehachayot am-rav\nAnd as for you\, ye meant evil against me\; but
  God meant it for good\, to bring to pass\, as it is this day\, to save mu
 ch people alive.\n\nJoseph tells his brothers that what they meant for har
 m\, God turned to good. Hard chapters of a life can lead somewhere good.\n
 \nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270716@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270716
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270717
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 3:5
DESCRIPTION:וַיֹּאמֶר אַל־תִּקְרַב הֲלֹם שַׁל
 ־נְעָלֶיךָ מֵעַל רַגְלֶיךָ כִּי הַמָּק
 וֹם אֲשֶׁר אַתָּה עוֹמֵד עָלָיו אַדְמַת
 ־קֹדֶשׁ הוּא׃\nVayomer al-tikrav halom shal-ne'alekha me'al ra
 glekha ki hamakom asher atah omed alav admat-kodesh hu\nAnd He said: ‘Dr
 aw not nigh hither\; put off thy shoes from off thy feet\, for the place w
 hereon thou standest is holy ground.’\n\nAt the burning bush Moses is to
 ld to take off his shoes\, because the ground is holy. Some moments call f
 or us to slow down and pay attention.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.o
 nrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270717@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270717
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270718
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 3:14
DESCRIPTION:וַיֹּאמֶר אֱלֹהִים אֶל־מֹשֶׁה אֶ
 הְיֶה אֲשֶׁר אֶהְיֶה וַיֹּאמֶר כֹּה תֹא
 מַר לִבְנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל אֶהְיֶה שְׁלָחַ
 נִי אֲלֵיכֶם׃\nVayomer Elohim el-Mosheh ehyeh asher ehyeh vayo
 mer koh tomar livnei Yisra'el ehyeh shelachani aleikhem\nAnd God said unto
  Moses: ‘I AM THAT I AM’\; and He said: ‘Thus shalt thou say unto th
 e children of Israel: I AM hath sent me unto you.’\n\nEhyeh asher ehyeh:
  "I will be what I will be." God's name here is about being present\, in e
 very time and place.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/mor
 ning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270718@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270718
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270719
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 13:8
DESCRIPTION:וְהִגַּדְתָּ לְבִנְךָ בַּיּוֹם הַ
 הוּא לֵאמֹר בַּעֲבוּר זֶה עָשָׂה יְהוָה 
 לִי בְּצֵאתִי מִמִּצְרָיִם׃\nVehigadta levinkha b
 ayom hahu lemor ba'avur zeh asah Adonai li betzeti mimitzrayim\nAnd thou s
 halt tell thy son in that day\, saying: It is because of that which the LO
 RD did for me when I came forth out of Egypt.\n\nThis verse is why we tell
  the Passover story at the Seder. Each generation tells it as if it happen
 ed to them.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270719@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270719
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270720
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 14:14
DESCRIPTION:יְהוָה יִלָּחֵם לָכֶם וְאַתֶּם 
 תַּחֲרִישׁוּן׃\nAdonai yilachem lakhem ve'atem tacharishun\n
 The LORD will fight for you\, and ye shall hold your peace.’\n\nAt the S
 ea of Reeds\, Moses tells the frightened people that God will fight for th
 em. Sometimes the right move is to stay calm and trust.\n\nOpen Aleph: htt
 ps://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270720@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270720
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270721
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 15:2
DESCRIPTION:עָזִּי וְזִמְרָת יָהּ וַיְהִי־לִי
  לִישׁוּעָה זֶה אֵלִי וְאַנְוֵהוּ אֱלֹ
 הֵי אָבִי וַאֲרֹמְמֶנְהוּ׃\nAzi vezimrat yah vayhi
 -li lishu'ah zeh eli ve'anvehu elohei avi va'aromemenhu\nThe LORD is my st
 rength and song\, And He is become my salvation\; This is my God\, and I w
 ill glorify Him\; My father’s God\, and I will exalt Him.\n\nFrom the So
 ng at the Sea: "The Lord is my strength and my song." These words are sung
  in synagogue every morning.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.c
 om/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270721@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270721
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270722
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 15:11
DESCRIPTION:מִי־כָמֹכָה בָּאֵלִם יְהוָה מִי 
 כָּמֹכָה נֶאְדָּר בַּקֹּדֶשׁ נוֹרָא תְ
 הִלֹּת עֹשֵׂה פֶלֶא׃\nMi-khamokhah ba'elim Adonai mi kam
 okhah nedar bakodesh nora tehilot oseh fele\nWho is like unto Thee\, O LOR
 D\, among the mighty? Who is like unto Thee\, glorious in holiness\, Fearf
 ul in praises\, doing wonders?\n\nMi chamocha\, "Who is like You?" This li
 ne from the Song at the Sea is part of the daily prayers\, just after the 
 Shema.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270722@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270722
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270723
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 19:6
DESCRIPTION:וְאַתֶּם תִּהְיוּ־לִי מַמְלֶכֶת 
 כֹּהֲנִים וְגוֹי קָדוֹשׁ אֵלֶּה הַדְּבָ
 רִים אֲשֶׁר תְּדַבֵּר אֶל־בְּנֵי יִשְׂ
 רָאֵל׃\nVe'atem tihyu-li mamlekhet kohanim vegoy kadosh eleh hadevar
 im asher tedaber el-benei Yisra'el\nand ye shall be unto Me a kingdom of p
 riests\, and a holy nation. These are the words which thou shalt speak unt
 o the children of Israel.’\n\nAt Sinai the whole people is called a king
 dom of priests and a holy nation. Holiness is meant for everyone\, not onl
 y for a few.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270723@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270723
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270724
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 20:2
DESCRIPTION:אָנֹכִי יְהוָה אֱלֹהֶיךָ אֲשֶׁר ה
 וֹצֵאתִיךָ מֵאֶרֶץ מִצְרַיִם מִבֵּית עֲ
 בָדִים׃\nAnokhi Adonai Elohekha asher hotzetikha me'eretz Mitzrayim
  mibeit avadim\nI am the LORD thy God\, who brought thee out of the land o
 f Egypt\, out of the house of bondage.\n\nThe Ten Commandments begin with 
 who God is: the One who brought us out of slavery. Freedom comes first\, a
 nd the commandments follow.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.co
 m/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270724@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270724
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270725
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 20:8
DESCRIPTION:זָכוֹר אֶת־יוֹם הַשַׁבָּת לְקַדְּ
 שׁוֹ\nZakhor et-yom hashabat lekadesho\nRemember the sabbath day\, to 
 keep it holy.\n\nZachor: "Remember the Shabbat day." We remember it with c
 andles\, Kiddush\, rest and time with the people we love.\n\nOpen Aleph: h
 ttps://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270725@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270725
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270726
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 20:12
DESCRIPTION:כַּבֵּד אֶת־אָבִיךָ וְאֶת־אִמֶּ
 ךָ לְמַעַן יַאֲרִכוּן יָמֶיךָ עַל הָאֲ
 דָמָה אֲשֶׁר־יְהוָה אֱלֹהֶיךָ נֹתֵן לָ
 ךְ׃\nKabed et-avikha ve'et-imekha lema'an ya'arikhun yamekha al ha'adam
 ah asher-Adonai Elohekha noten lakh\nHonour thy father and thy mother\, th
 at thy days may be long upon the land which the LORD thy God giveth thee.\
 n\nHonour your father and your mother. It is one of the Ten Commandments\,
  and the first that comes with a promise of long life.\n\nOpen Aleph: http
 s://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270726@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270726
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270727
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 22:20
DESCRIPTION:וְגֵר לֹא־תוֹנֶה וְלֹא תִלְחָצֶנּ
 וּ כִּי־גֵרִים הֱיִיתֶם בְּאֶרֶץ מִצְרָ
 יִם׃\nVeger lo-toneh velo tilchatzenu ki-gerim heyitem be'eretz Mitzra
 yim\nAnd a stranger shalt thou not wrong\, neither shalt thou oppress him\
 ; for ye were strangers in the land of Egypt.\n\nDo not wrong the stranger
 \, because you were strangers in Egypt. This idea comes up again and again
  in the Torah.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270727@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270727
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270728
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 23:2
DESCRIPTION:לֹא־תִהְיֶה אַחֲרֵי־רַבִּים לְרָ
 עֹת וְלֹא־תַעֲנֶה עַל־רִב לִנְטֹת אַחֲ
 רֵי רַבִּים לְהַטֹּת׃\nLo-tihyeh acharei-rabim lera'ot 
 velo-ta'aneh al-riv lintot acharei rabim lehatot\nThou shalt not follow a 
 multitude to do evil\; neither shalt thou bear witness in a cause to turn 
 aside after a multitude to pervert justice\;\n\nDo not follow the crowd to
  do wrong. Doing the right thing sometimes means standing apart.\n\nOpen A
 leph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270728@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270728
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270729
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 23:9
DESCRIPTION:וְגֵר לֹא תִלְחָץ וְאַתֶּם יְדַעְ
 תֶּם אֶת־נֶפֶשׁ הַגֵּר כִּי־גֵרִים הֱיִ
 יתֶם בְּאֶרֶץ מִצְרָיִם׃\nVeger lo tilchatz ve'atem 
 yedatem et-nefesh hager ki-gerim heyitem be'eretz Mitzrayim\nAnd a strange
 r shalt thou not oppress\; for ye know the heart of a stranger\, seeing ye
  were strangers in the land of Egypt.\n\n"You know the heart of the strang
 er." Our own history should make us kind to newcomers.\n\nOpen Aleph: http
 s://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270729@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270729
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270730
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 25:8
DESCRIPTION:וְעָשׂוּ לִי מִקְדָּשׁ וְשָׁכַנְ
 תִּי בְּתוֹכָם׃\nVe'asu li mikdash veshakhanti betokham\nAnd
  let them make Me a sanctuary\, that I may dwell among them.\n\n"Make Me a
  sanctuary\, and I will dwell among them." Not "in it\," but among them: G
 od lives among people\, in the places they make holy.\n\nOpen Aleph: https
 ://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270730@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270730
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270731
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 33:13
DESCRIPTION:וְעַתָּה אִם־נָא מָצָאתִי חֵן בְּ
 עֵינֶיךָ הוֹדִעֵנִי נָא אֶת־דְּרָכֶךָ 
 וְאֵדָעֲךָ לְמַעַן אֶמְצָא־חֵן בְּעֵי
 נֶיךָ וּרְאֵה כִּי עַמְּךָ הַגּוֹי הַ
 זֶּה׃\nVe'atah im-na matzati chen be'einekha hodi'eni na et-derakhekh
 a ve'eda'akha lema'an emtza-chen be'einekha ure'eh ki amekha hagoy hazeh\n
 Now therefore\, I pray Thee\, if I have found grace in Thy sight\, show me
  now Thy ways\, that I may know Thee\, to the end that I may find grace in
  Thy sight\; and consider that this nation is Thy people.’\n\nMoses asks
  God\, "Show me Your ways\, so that I may know You." Learning is one of th
 e ways Jews come close to God.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender
 .com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270731@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270731
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270801
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 34:6
DESCRIPTION:וַיַּעֲבֹר יְהוָה עַל־פָּנָיו וַ
 יִּקְרָא יְהוָה יְהוָה אֵל רַחוּם וְחַ
 נּוּן אֶרֶךְ אַפַּיִם וְרַב־חֶסֶד וֶאֱ
 מֶת\nVaya'avor Adonai al-panav vayikra Adonai Adonai el rachum vechanun
  erekh apayim verav-chesed ve'emet\nAnd the LORD passed by before him\, an
 d proclaimed: ‘The LORD\, the LORD\, God\, merciful and gracious\, long-
 suffering\, and abundant in goodness and truth\;\n\nThese are God's qualit
 ies of mercy\, sung on the High Holy Days: compassionate\, gracious\, slow
  to anger\, full of kindness and truth.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review
 .onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270801@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270801
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270802
SUMMARY:Torah: Leviticus 19:2
DESCRIPTION:דַּבֵּר אֶל־כָּל־עֲדַת בְּנֵי־יִ
 שְׂרָאֵל וְאָמַרְתָּ אֲלֵהֶם קְדֹשִׁים 
 תִּהְיוּ כִּי קָדוֹשׁ אֲנִי יְהוָה אֱלֹ
 הֵיכֶם׃\nDaber el-kol-adat benei-Yisra'el ve'amarta alehem kedoshim
  tihyu ki kadosh ani Adonai Eloheikhem\nSpeak unto all the congregation of
  the children of Israel\, and say unto them: Ye shall be holy\; for I the 
 LORD your God am holy.\n\n"You shall be holy\, for I am holy." The chapter
  that follows shows what that means: honesty\, kindness and fairness in ev
 eryday life.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270802@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270802
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270803
SUMMARY:Torah: Leviticus 19:3
DESCRIPTION:אִישׁ אִמּוֹ וְאָבִיו תִּירָאוּ 
 וְאֶת־שַׁבְּתֹתַי תִּשְׁמֹרוּ אֲנִי יְ
 הוָה אֱלֹהֵיכֶם׃\nIsh imo ve'aviv tira'u ve'et-shabetotai t
 ishmoru ani Adonai Eloheikhem\nYe shall fear every man his mother\, and hi
 s father\, and ye shall keep My sabbaths: I am the LORD your God.\n\nRespe
 ct your parents and keep Shabbat. Both are about honouring where we come f
 rom.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270803@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270803
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270804
SUMMARY:Torah: Leviticus 19:9
DESCRIPTION:וּבְקֻצְרְכֶם אֶת־קְצִיר אַרְצְ
 כֶם לֹא תְכַלֶּה פְּאַת שָׂדְךָ לִקְצֹר 
 וְלֶקֶט קְצִירְךָ לֹא תְלַקֵּט׃\nUvekutzrekhem
  et-ketzir artzekhem lo tekhaleh pe'at sadekha liktzor veleket ketzirekha 
 lo telaket\nAnd when ye reap the harvest of your land\, thou shalt not who
 lly reap the corner of thy field\, neither shalt thou gather the gleaning 
 of thy harvest.\n\nLeave the corners of your field for people in need. Giv
 ing to others is built right into how we earn and spend.\n\nOpen Aleph: ht
 tps://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270804@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270804
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270805
SUMMARY:Torah: Leviticus 19:14
DESCRIPTION:לֹא־תְקַלֵּל חֵרֵשׁ וְלִפְנֵי עִ
 וֵּר לֹא תִתֵּן מִכְשֹׁל וְיָרֵאתָ מֵּ
 אֱלֹהֶיךָ אֲנִי יְהוָה׃\nLo-tekalel cheresh velifnei 
 iver lo titen mikhshol veyareta me'Elohekha ani Adonai\nThou shalt not cur
 se the deaf\, nor put a stumbling-block before the blind\, but thou shalt 
 fear thy God: I am the LORD.\n\nDo not curse the deaf or put a stumbling b
 lock before the blind. Treat everyone with care\, especially those who can
 not defend themselves.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/m
 orning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270805@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270805
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270806
SUMMARY:Torah: Leviticus 19:16
DESCRIPTION:לֹא־תֵלֵךְ רָכִיל בְּעַמֶּיךָ לֹא
  תַעֲמֹד עַל־דַּם רֵעֶךָ אֲנִי יְהוָה׃\nL
 o-telekh rakhil be'amekha lo ta'amod al-dam re'ekha ani Adonai\nThou shalt
  not go up and down as a talebearer among thy people\; neither shalt thou 
 stand idly by the blood of thy neighbour: I am the LORD.\n\nDo not spread 
 gossip\, and do not stand by while your neighbour is in danger. Words can 
 hurt\, and silence can too.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.co
 m/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270806@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270806
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270807
SUMMARY:Torah: Leviticus 19:18
DESCRIPTION:לֹא־תִקֹּם וְלֹא־תִטֹּר אֶת־בְּ
 נֵי עַמֶּךָ וְאָהַבְתָּ לְרֵעֲךָ כָּמוֹ
 ךָ אֲנִי יְהוָה׃\nLo-tikom velo-titor et-benei amekha ve'aha
 vta lere'akha kamokha ani Adonai\nThou shalt not take vengeance\, nor bear
  any grudge against the children of thy people\, but thou shalt love thy n
 eighbour as thyself: I am the LORD.\n\n"Love your neighbour as yourself." 
 Rabbi Akiva called this the great principle of the whole Torah.\n\nOpen Al
 eph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270807@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270807
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270808
SUMMARY:Torah: Leviticus 19:32
DESCRIPTION:מִפְּנֵי שֵׂיבָה תָּקוּם וְהָדַרְ
 תָּ פְּנֵי זָקֵן וְיָרֵאתָ מֵּאֱלֹהֶיךָ
  אֲנִי יְהוָה׃\nMipenei seivah takum vehadarta penei zaken vey
 areta me'Elohekha ani Adonai\nThou shalt rise up before the hoary head\, a
 nd honour the face of the old man\, and thou shalt fear thy God: I am the 
 LORD.\n\nRise before the elderly and honour them. Age brings wisdom\, and 
 the Torah asks us to show it respect.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.o
 nrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270808@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270808
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270809
SUMMARY:Torah: Leviticus 25:10
DESCRIPTION:וְקִדַּשְׁתֶּם אֵת שְׁנַת הַחֲמִ
 שִּׁים שָׁנָה וּקְרָאתֶם דְּרוֹר בָּאָ
 רֶץ לְכָל־יֹשְׁבֶיהָ יוֹבֵל הִוא תִּהְ
 יֶה לָכֶם וְשַׁבְתֶּם אִישׁ אֶל־אֲחֻזָּ
 תוֹ וְאִישׁ אֶל־מִשְׁפַּחְתּוֹ תָּשֻׁב
 וּ׃\nVekidashtem et shenat hachamishim shanah ukeratem deror ba'aretz l
 ekhol-yosheveha yovel hiv tihyeh lakhem veshavtem ish el-achuzato ve'ish e
 l-mishpachto tashuvu\nAnd ye shall hallow the fiftieth year\, and proclaim
  liberty throughout the land unto all the inhabitants thereof\; it shall b
 e a jubilee unto you\; and ye shall return every man unto his possession\,
  and ye shall return every man unto his family.\n\n"Proclaim liberty throu
 ghout the land." These words about the Jubilee year are cast on the Libert
 y Bell in Philadelphia.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/
 morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270809@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270809
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270810
SUMMARY:Torah: Numbers 6:24
DESCRIPTION:יְבָרֶכְךָ יְהוָה וְיִשְׁמְרֶךָ׃\
 nYevarekhkha Adonai veyishmerekha\nThe LORD bless thee\, and keep thee\;\n
 \nThe first line of the Priestly Blessing\, still said in synagogues and b
 y parents to children on Friday night.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.
 onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270810@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270810
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270811
SUMMARY:Torah: Numbers 6:26
DESCRIPTION:יִשָּׂא יְהוָה פָּנָיו אֵלֶיךָ וְ
 יָשֵׂם לְךָ שָׁלוֹם׃\nYisa Adonai panav elekha veyasem l
 ekha shalom\nThe LORD lift up His countenance upon thee\, and give thee pe
 ace.\n\nThe Priestly Blessing ends with shalom\, peace. In Hebrew\, shalom
  also means wholeness: everything in its right place.\n\nOpen Aleph: https
 ://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270811@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270811
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270812
SUMMARY:Torah: Numbers 11:29
DESCRIPTION:וַיֹּאמֶר לוֹ מֹשֶׁה הַמְקַנֵּא 
 אַתָּה לִי וּמִי יִתֵּן כָּל־עַם יְהוָה 
 נְבִיאִים כִּי־יִתֵּן יְהוָה אֶת־רוּח
 וֹ עֲלֵיהֶם׃\nVayomer lo Mosheh hamkane atah li umi yiten kol-a
 m Adonai nevi'im ki-yiten Adonai et-rucho aleihem\nAnd Moses said unto him
 : ‘Art thou jealous for my sake? would that all the LORD’S people were
  prophets\, that the LORD would put His spirit upon them! ’\n\nWhen othe
 rs begin to prophesy\, Moses is not jealous. He wishes everyone could shar
 e God's spirit. Great leaders lift others up.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-
 review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270812@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270812
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270813
SUMMARY:Torah: Numbers 15:39
DESCRIPTION:וְהָיָה לָכֶם לְצִיצִת וּרְאִיתֶם
  אֹתוֹ וּזְכַרְתֶּם אֶת־כָּל־מִצְוֹת יְ
 הוָה וַעֲשִׂיתֶם אֹתָם וְלֹא־תָתֻרוּ אַ
 חֲרֵי לְבַבְכֶם וְאַחֲרֵי עֵינֵיכֶם אֲ
 שֶׁר־אַתֶּם זֹנִים אַחֲרֵיהֶם׃\nVehayah lakhem
  letzitzit ure'item oto uzekhartem et-kol-mitzvot Adonai va'asitem otam ve
 lo-taturu acharei levavkhem ve'acharei eineikhem asher-atem zonim achareih
 em\nAnd it shall be unto you for a fringe\, that ye may look upon it\, and
  remember all the commandments of the LORD\, and do them\; and that ye go 
 not about after your own heart and your own eyes\, after which ye use to g
 o astray\;\n\nThis verse is about the tzitzit\, the fringes on the tallit.
  Seeing them is a reminder of the commandments and of who we want to be.\n
 \nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270813@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270813
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270814
SUMMARY:Torah: Numbers 24:5
DESCRIPTION:מַה־טֹּבוּ אֹהָלֶיךָ יַעֲקֹב מִ
 שְׁכְּנֹתֶיךָ יִשְׂרָאֵל׃\nMah-tovu ohalekha Ya'ak
 ov mishkenotekha Yisra'el\nHow goodly are thy tents\, O Jacob\, Thy dwelli
 ngs\, O Israel!\n\nMah tovu\, "How good are your tents." Many synagogues o
 pen the morning service with these words.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-revi
 ew.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270814@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270814
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270815
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 4:9
DESCRIPTION:רַק הִשָּׁמֶר לְךָ וּשְׁמֹר נַפְ
 שְׁךָ מְאֹד פֶּן־תִּשְׁכַּח אֶת־הַדְּ
 בָרִים אֲשֶׁר־רָאוּ עֵינֶיךָ וּפֶן־יָס
 וּרוּ מִלְּבָבְךָ כֹּל יְמֵי חַיֶּיךָ 
 וְהוֹדַעְתָּם לְבָנֶיךָ וְלִבְנֵי בָנֶ
 יךָ׃\nRak hishamer lekha ushemor nafshekha me'od pen-tishkach et-hadev
 arim asher-ra'u einekha ufen-yasuru milevavekha kol yemei chayekha vehodat
 am levanekha velivnei vanekha\nOnly take heed to thyself\, and keep thy so
 ul diligently\, lest thou forget the things which thine eyes saw\, and les
 t they depart from thy heart all the days of thy life\; but make them know
 n unto thy children and thy children’s children\;\n\nDo not forget what 
 you have seen\, and teach it to your children and grandchildren. Memory is
  how a people stays alive.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com
 /#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270815@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270815
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270816
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 6:4
DESCRIPTION:שְׁמַע יִשְׂרָאֵל יְהוָה אֱלֹהֵינ
 וּ יְהוָה אֶחָד׃\nShema Yisra'el Adonai Eloheinu Adonai echa
 d\nHEAR\, O ISRAEL: THE LORD OUR GOD\, THE LORD IS ONE.\n\nThe Shema\, the
  central line of Jewish prayer: "Hear\, O Israel\, the Lord is our God\, t
 he Lord is One." It is said morning and night.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef
 -review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270816@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270816
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270817
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 6:5
DESCRIPTION:וְאָהַבְתָּ אֵת יְהוָה אֱלֹהֶיךָ 
 בְּכָל־לְבָבְךָ וּבְכָל־נַפְשְׁךָ וּבְ
 כָל־מְאֹדֶךָ׃\nVe'ahavta et Adonai Elohekha bekhol-levavekha 
 uvekhol-nafshekha uvekhol-me'odekha\nAnd thou shalt love the LORD thy God 
 with all thy heart\, and with all thy soul\, and with all thy might.\n\nV'
 ahavta: love God with all your heart\, all your soul and all your strength
 . Faith in Judaism is about love\, not only belief.\n\nOpen Aleph: https:/
 /alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270817@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270817
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270818
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 6:7
DESCRIPTION:וְשִׁנַּנְתָּם לְבָנֶיךָ וְדִבַּ
 רְתָּ בָּם בְּשִׁבְתְּךָ בְּבֵיתֶךָ וּ
 בְלֶכְתְּךָ בַדֶּרֶךְ וּבְשָׁכְבְּךָ 
 וּבְקוּמֶךָ׃\nVeshinantam levanekha vedibarta bam beshivtekha 
 beveitekha uvelekhtekha vaderekh uveshakhbekha uvekumekha\nand thou shalt 
 teach them diligently unto thy children\, and shalt talk of them when thou
  sittest in thy house\, and when thou walkest by the way\, and when thou l
 iest down\, and when thou risest up.\n\nTalk about these words at home\, o
 n the road\, when you lie down and when you get up. That is why the Shema 
 is said at bedtime and in the morning.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.
 onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270818@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270818
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270819
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 8:3
DESCRIPTION:וַיְעַנְּךָ וַיַּרְעִבֶךָ וַיַּ
 אֲכִלְךָ אֶת הַמָּן אֲשֶׁר לֹא־יָדַעְ
 תָּ וְלֹא יָדְעוּן אֲבֹתֶיךָ לְמַעַן ה
 וֹדִעֲךָ כִּי לֹא עַל־הַלֶּחֶם לְבַדּוֹ
  יִחְיֶה הָאָדָם כִּי עַל־כָּל־מוֹצָא 
 פִי־יְהוָה יִחְיֶה הָאָדָם׃\nVay'anekha vayar'ive
 kha vaya'akhilkha et haman asher lo-yadata velo yad'un avotekha lema'an ho
 di'akha ki lo al-halechem levado yichyeh ha'adam ki al-kol-motza fi-Adonai
  yichyeh ha'adam\nAnd He afflicted thee\, and suffered thee to hunger\, an
 d fed thee with manna\, which thou knewest not\, neither did thy fathers k
 now\; that He might make thee know that man doth not live by bread only\, 
 but by every thing that proceedeth out of the mouth of the LORD doth man l
 ive.\n\n"A person does not live by bread alone." We need meaning\, learnin
 g and purpose as much as food.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender
 .com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270819@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270819
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270820
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 8:10
DESCRIPTION:וְאָכַלְתָּ וְשָׂבָעְתָּ וּבֵרַ
 כְתָּ אֶת־יְהוָה אֱלֹהֶיךָ עַל־הָאָרֶץ 
 הַטֹּבָה אֲשֶׁר נָתַן־לָךְ׃\nVe'akhalta vesava'et
 a uverakhta et-Adonai Elohekha al-ha'aretz hatovah asher natan-lakh\nAnd t
 hou shalt eat and be satisfied\, and bless the LORD thy God for the good l
 and which He hath given thee.\n\nEat\, be satisfied\, and bless. This vers
 e is the source of Birkat Hamazon\, the blessing after meals.\n\nOpen Alep
 h: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270820@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270820
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270821
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 10:19
DESCRIPTION:וַאֲהַבְתֶּם אֶת־הַגֵּר כִּי־גֵ
 רִים הֱיִיתֶם בְּאֶרֶץ מִצְרָיִם׃\nVa'ahavte
 m et-hager ki-gerim heyitem be'eretz Mitzrayim\nLove ye therefore the stra
 nger\; for ye were strangers in the land of Egypt.\n\nLove the stranger\, 
 because you were strangers in Egypt. The Torah asks for more than not hurt
 ing newcomers\; it asks us to love them.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-revie
 w.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270821@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270821
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270822
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 16:20
DESCRIPTION:צֶדֶק צֶדֶק תִּרְדֹּף לְמַעַן תִּ
 חְיֶה וְיָרַשְׁתָּ אֶת־הָאָרֶץ אֲשֶׁר־
 יְהוָה אֱלֹהֶיךָ נֹתֵן לָךְ׃\nTzedek tzedek tirdo
 f lema'an tichyeh veyarashta et-ha'aretz asher-Adonai Elohekha noten lakh\
 nJustice\, justice shalt thou follow\, that thou mayest live\, and inherit
  the land which the LORD thy God giveth thee.\n\nTzedek tzedek tirdof: "Ju
 stice\, justice you shall pursue." The word is said twice\, to show how ha
 rd we should work for it.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/
 #/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270822@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270822
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270823
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 30:14
DESCRIPTION:כִּי־קָרוֹב אֵלֶיךָ הַדָּבָר מְאֹ
 ד בְּפִיךָ וּבִלְבָבְךָ לַעֲשֹׂתוֹ׃\nKi-ka
 rov elekha hadavar me'od befikha uvilvavekha la'asoto\nBut the word is ver
 y nigh unto thee\, in thy mouth\, and in thy heart\, that thou mayest do i
 t.\n\nThe Torah is not far away: it is in your mouth and in your heart. It
  is within reach\, one word at a time.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.
 onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270823@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270823
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270824
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 30:19
DESCRIPTION:הַעִידֹתִי בָכֶם הַיּוֹם אֶת־הַ
 שָּׁמַיִם וְאֶת־הָאָרֶץ הַחַיִּים וְהַ
 מָּוֶת נָתַתִּי לְפָנֶיךָ הַבְּרָכָה וְ
 הַקְּלָלָה וּבָחַרְתָּ בַּחַיִּים לְמַ
 עַן תִּחְיֶה אַתָּה וְזַרְעֶךָ׃\nHa'idoti vakh
 em hayom et-hashamayim ve'et-ha'aretz hachayim vehamavet natati lefanekha 
 haberakhah vehakelalah uvacharta bachayim lema'an tichyeh atah vezar'ekha\
 nI call heaven and earth to witness against you this day\, that I have set
  before thee life and death\, the blessing and the curse\; therefore choos
 e life\, that thou mayest live\, thou and thy seed\;\n\n"Choose life." Eve
 ry day brings choices\, and the Torah asks us to choose the ones that lead
  to life and blessing.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/m
 orning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270824@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270824
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270825
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 31:6
DESCRIPTION:חִזְקוּ וְאִמְצוּ אַל־תִּירְאוּ 
 וְאַל־תַּעַרְצוּ מִפְּנֵיהֶם כִּי יְה
 וָה אֱלֹהֶיךָ הוּא הַהֹלֵךְ עִמָּךְ לֹא 
 יַרְפְּךָ וְלֹא יַעַזְבֶךָּ׃\nChizku ve'imtzu al
 -tir'u ve'al-ta'artzu mipeneihem ki Adonai Elohekha hu haholekh imakh lo y
 arpekha velo ya'azveka\nBe strong and of good courage\, fear not\, nor be 
 affrighted at them\; for the LORD thy God\, He it is that doth go with the
 e\; He will not fail thee\, nor forsake thee.’\n\nChazak ve'ematz: "Be s
 trong and of good courage." Moses says this before the people enter the la
 nd without him.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270825@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270825
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270826
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 6:6
DESCRIPTION:וְהָיוּ הַדְּבָרִים הָאֵלֶּה אֲ
 שֶׁר אָנֹכִי מְצַוְּךָ הַיּוֹם עַל־לְבָ
 בֶךָ׃\nVehayu hadevarim ha'eleh asher anokhi metzavekha hayom al-leva
 vekha\nAnd these words\, which I command thee this day\, shall be upon thy
  heart\;\n\n"These words shall be upon your heart." Learning Torah is mean
 t to go deeper than memory\, into who we are.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-
 review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270826@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270826
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270827
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 31:16
DESCRIPTION:וְשָׁמְרוּ בְנֵי־יִשְׂרָאֵל אֶת־
 הַשַּׁבָּת לַעֲשׂוֹת אֶת־הַשַּׁבָּת לְ
 דֹרֹתָם בְּרִית עוֹלָם׃\nVeshamru venei-Yisra'el et-h
 ashabat la'asot et-hashabat ledorotam berit olam\nWherefore the children o
 f Israel shall keep the sabbath\, to observe the sabbath throughout their 
 generations\, for a perpetual covenant.\n\nV'shamru: the people of Israel 
 shall keep the Shabbat for all generations. This verse is sung on Friday n
 ight and Shabbat morning.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/
 #/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270827@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270827
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270828
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 34:10
DESCRIPTION:וְלֹא־קָם נָבִיא עוֹד בְּיִשְׂרָ
 אֵל כְּמֹשֶׁה אֲשֶׁר יְדָעוֹ יְהוָה פָּ
 נִים אֶל־פָּנִים׃\nVelo-kam navi od beyisra'el kemosheh as
 her yeda'o Adonai panim el-panim\nAnd there hath not arisen a prophet sinc
 e in Israel like unto Moses\, whom the LORD knew face to face\;\n\nNear th
 e very end of the Torah: no prophet arose like Moses\, who knew God face t
 o face. Then we roll the scroll back and start again.\n\nOpen Aleph: https
 ://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270828@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270828
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270829
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 1:1
DESCRIPTION:בְּרֵאשִׁית בָּרָא אֱלֹהִים אֵת 
 הַשָּׁמַיִם וְאֵת הָאָרֶץ׃\nBereshit bara Elohim e
 t hashamayim ve'et ha'aretz\nIn the beginning God created the heaven and t
 he earth.\n\nThe Torah opens with its first word\, Bereshit\, "in the begi
 nning." Everything that follows starts here: the world has a Maker\, and i
 t did not come about by chance.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrende
 r.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270829@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270829
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270830
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 1:3
DESCRIPTION:וַיֹּאמֶר אֱלֹהִים יְהִי אוֹר וַ
 יְהִי־אוֹר׃\nVayomer Elohim yehi or vayhi-or\nAnd God said: ‘
 Let there be light.’ And there was light.\n\nThe first thing God makes i
 s light\, and He makes it with words. In Judaism speech has real power\, s
 o the words we choose each day matter.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.
 onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270830@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270830
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270831
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 1:27
DESCRIPTION:וַיִּבְרָא אֱלֹהִים אֶת־הָאָדָם 
 בְּצַלְמוֹ בְּצֶלֶם אֱלֹהִים בָּרָא אֹת
 וֹ זָכָר וּנְקֵבָה בָּרָא אֹתָם׃\nVayivra Eloh
 im et-ha'adam betzalmo betzelem Elohim bara oto zakhar unekevah bara otam\
 nAnd God created man in His own image\, in the image of God created He him
 \; male and female created He them.\n\nEvery person is made in the image o
 f God. That is why each human life has worth\, whoever the person is and w
 herever they come from.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/
 morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270831@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270831
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270901
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 1:31
DESCRIPTION:וַיַּרְא אֱלֹהִים אֶת־כָּל־אֲשֶׁ
 ר עָשָׂה וְהִנֵּה־טוֹב מְאֹד וַיְהִי־עֶ
 רֶב וַיְהִי־בֹקֶר יוֹם הַשִּׁשִּׁי׃\nVayar
  Elohim et-kol-asher asah vehineh-tov me'od vayhi-erev vayhi-voker yom has
 hishi\nAnd God saw every thing that He had made\, and\, behold\, it was ve
 ry good. And there was evening and there was morning\, the sixth day.\n\nA
 fter each day God saw that it was good. On the sixth day\, with people in 
 the world\, it became "very good." Look for the good in your own day.\n\nO
 pen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270901@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270901
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270902
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 2:3
DESCRIPTION:וַיְבָרֶךְ אֱלֹהִים אֶת־יוֹם הַ
 שְּׁבִיעִי וַיְקַדֵּשׁ אֹתוֹ כִּי בוֹ 
 שָׁבַת מִכָּל־מְלַאכְתּוֹ אֲשֶׁר־בָּרָ
 א אֱלֹהִים לַעֲשׂוֹת׃\nVayvarekh Elohim et-yom hashevi'
 i vaykadesh oto ki vo shavat mikol-melakhto asher-bara Elohim la'asot\nAnd
  God blessed the seventh day\, and hallowed it\; because that in it He res
 ted from all His work which God in creating had made.\n\nThis is the first
  Shabbat. God rested on the seventh day and made it holy\, and we rest on 
 it too. Shabbat is a gift of time\, not only a rule.\n\nOpen Aleph: https:
 //alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270902@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270902
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270903
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 2:15
DESCRIPTION:וַיִּקַּח יְהוָה אֱלֹהִים אֶת־הָ
 אָדָם וַיַּנִּחֵהוּ בְגַן־עֵדֶן לְעָבְ
 דָהּ וּלְשָׁמְרָהּ׃\nVayikach Adonai Elohim et-ha'adam v
 ayanichehu vegan-eden le'avedah uleshamerah\nAnd the LORD God took the man
 \, and put him into the garden of Eden to dress it and to keep it.\n\nAdam
  was put in the garden to work it and to guard it. The earth is placed in 
 our care\, and looking after it is part of our job.\n\nOpen Aleph: https:/
 /alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270903@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270903
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270904
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 2:18
DESCRIPTION:וַיֹּאמֶר יְהוָה אֱלֹהִים לֹא־טוֹ
 ב הֱיוֹת הָאָדָם לְבַדּוֹ אֶעֱשֶׂהּ־לּ
 וֹ עֵזֶר כְּנֶגְדּוֹ׃\nVayomer Adonai Elohim lo-tov hey
 ot ha'adam levado e'eseh-lo ezer kenegdo\nAnd the LORD God said: ‘It is 
 not good that the man should be alone\; I will make him a help meet for hi
 m.’\n\n"It is not good to be alone." People need each other. Community\,
  friendship and family are part of how we were made.\n\nOpen Aleph: https:
 //alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270904@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270904
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270905
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 4:9
DESCRIPTION:וַיֹּאמֶר יְהוָה אֶל־קַיִן אֵי הֶ
 בֶל אָחִיךָ וַיֹּאמֶר לֹא יָדַעְתִּי הֲ
 שֹׁמֵר אָחִי אָנֹכִי׃\nVayomer Adonai el-kayin ei hevel
  achikha vayomer lo yadati hashomer achi anokhi\nAnd the LORD said unto Ca
 in: ‘Where is Abel thy brother?’ And he said: ‘I know not\; am I my 
 brother’s keeper?’\n\nCain asks\, "Am I my brother's keeper?" The rest
  of the Torah answers yes. We are responsible for one another.\n\nOpen Ale
 ph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270905@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270905
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270906
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 12:1
DESCRIPTION:וַיֹּאמֶר יְהוָה אֶל־אַבְרָם לֶךְ
 ־לְךָ מֵאַרְצְךָ וּמִמּוֹלַדְתְּךָ וּ
 מִבֵּית אָבִיךָ אֶל־הָאָרֶץ אֲשֶׁר אַרְ
 אֶךָּ׃\nVayomer Adonai el-Avram lekh-lekha me'artzekha umimoladtekha
  umibeit avikha el-ha'aretz asher ar'eka\nNow the LORD said unto Abram: 
 ‘Get thee out of thy country\, and from thy kindred\, and from thy fathe
 r’s house\, unto the land that I will show thee.\n\nLech lecha: "go for 
 yourself." Abraham leaves everything familiar to follow God. Every new sta
 rt\, including learning Hebrew\, takes a first step like this.\n\nOpen Ale
 ph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270906@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270906
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270907
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 12:2
DESCRIPTION:וְאֶעֶשְׂךָ לְגוֹי גָּדוֹל וַאֲבָ
 רֶכְךָ וַאֲגַדְּלָה שְׁמֶךָ וֶהְיֵה בְּ
 רָכָה׃\nVe'e'eskha legoy gadol va'avarekhkha va'agadelah shemekha ve
 hyeh berakhah\nAnd I will make of thee a great nation\, and I will bless t
 hee\, and make thy name great\; and be thou a blessing.\n\nAbraham is told
  not only that he will be blessed but that he will be a blessing. A good l
 ife is one that brings good to others.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.
 onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270907@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270907
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270908
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 15:5
DESCRIPTION:וַיּוֹצֵא אֹתוֹ הַחוּצָה וַיֹּאמֶ
 ר הַבֶּט־נָא הַשָּׁמַיְמָה וּסְפֹר הַכּ
 וֹכָבִים אִם־תּוּכַל לִסְפֹּר אֹתָם וַ
 יֹּאמֶר לוֹ כֹּה יִהְיֶה זַרְעֶךָ׃\nVayotze 
 oto hachutzah vayomer habet-na hashamaymah usefor hakokhavim im-tukhal lis
 por otam vayomer lo koh yihyeh zar'ekha\nAnd He brought him forth abroad\,
  and said: ‘Look now toward heaven\, and count the stars\, if thou be ab
 le to count them’\; and He said unto him: ‘So shall thy seed be.’\n\
 nGod takes Abraham outside to count the stars. When things feel small or u
 ncertain\, step back and look at the bigger picture.\n\nOpen Aleph: https:
 //alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270908@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270908
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270909
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 18:25
DESCRIPTION:חָלִלָה לְּךָ מֵעֲשֹׂת כַּדָּבָר 
 הַזֶּה לְהָמִית צַדִּיק עִם־רָשָׁע וְהָ
 יָה כַצַדִּיק כָּרָשָׁע חָלִלָה לָּךְ 
 הֲשֹׁפֵט כָּל־הָאָרֶץ לֹא יַעֲשֶׂה מִ
 שְׁפָּט׃\nChalilah lekha me'asot kadavar hazeh lehamit tzadik im-r
 asha vehayah khatzadik karasha chalilah lakh hashofet kol-ha'aretz lo ya'a
 seh mishpat\nThat be far from Thee to do after this manner\, to slay the r
 ighteous with the wicked\, that so the righteous should be as the wicked\;
  that be far from Thee\; shall not the judge of all the earth do justly?
 ’\n\nAbraham argues with God to save the people of Sodom. In Jewish trad
 ition it is right to speak up for justice\, even before the highest author
 ity.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270909@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270909
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270910
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 28:15
DESCRIPTION:וְהִנֵּה אָנֹכִי עִמָּךְ וּשְׁמַ
 רְתִּיךָ בְּכֹל אֲשֶׁר־תֵּלֵךְ וַהֲשִׁ
 בֹתִיךָ אֶל־הָאֲדָמָה הַזֹּאת כִּי לֹא 
 אֶעֱזָבְךָ עַד אֲשֶׁר אִם־עָשִׂיתִי אֵת
  אֲשֶׁר־דִּבַּרְתִּי לָךְ׃\nVehineh anokhi imakh u
 shemartikha bekhol asher-telekh vahashivotikha el-ha'adamah hazot ki lo e'
 ezavekha ad asher im-asiti et asher-dibarti lakh\nAnd\, behold\, I am with
  thee\, and will keep thee whithersoever thou goest\, and will bring thee 
 back into this land\; for I will not leave thee\, until I have done that w
 hich I have spoken to thee of.’\n\nJacob is alone and running away\, and
  God promises: I am with you\, wherever you go. You are never as alone as 
 you feel.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270910@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270910
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270911
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 28:16
DESCRIPTION:וַיִּיקַץ יַעֲקֹב מִשְּׁנָתוֹ וַ
 יֹּאמֶר אָכֵן יֵשׁ יְהוָה בַּמָּקוֹם הַ
 זֶּה וְאָנֹכִי לֹא יָדָעְתִּי׃\nVayikatz Ya'ako
 v mishenato vayomer akhen yesh Adonai bamakom hazeh ve'anokhi lo yada'eti\
 nAnd Jacob awaked out of his sleep\, and he said: ‘Surely the LORD is in
  this place\; and I knew it not.’\n\nJacob wakes from his dream and says
  God was in this place and he did not know it. Holiness can be right where
  you are\, if you notice it.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.c
 om/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270911@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270911
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270912
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 32:11
DESCRIPTION:קָטֹנְתִּי מִכֹּל הַחֲסָדִים וּמִ
 כָּל־הָאֱמֶת אֲשֶׁר עָשִׂיתָ אֶת־עַבְ
 דֶּךָ כִּי בְמַקְלִי עָבַרְתִּי אֶת־הַ
 יַּרְדֵּן הַזֶּה וְעַתָּה הָיִיתִי לִ
 שְׁנֵי מַחֲנוֹת׃\nKatoneti mikol hachasadim umikol-ha'emet 
 asher asita et-avdekha ki vemakli avarti et-hayarden hazeh ve'atah hayiti 
 lishnei machanot\nI am not worthy of all the mercies\, and of all the trut
 h\, which Thou hast shown unto Thy servant\; for with my staff I passed ov
 er this Jordan\; and now I am become two camps.\n\nBefore meeting his brot
 her Esau\, Jacob says he is not worthy of all the kindness he has received
 . Gratitude and humility go together.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.o
 nrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270912@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270912
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270913
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 45:4
DESCRIPTION:וַיֹּאמֶר יוֹסֵף אֶל־אֶחָיו גְּשׁ
 וּ־נָא אֵלַי וַיִּגָּשׁוּ וַיֹּאמֶר אֲ
 נִי יוֹסֵף אֲחִיכֶם אֲשֶׁר־מְכַרְתֶּם 
 אֹתִי מִצְרָיְמָה׃\nVayomer yosef el-echav geshu-na elai 
 vayigashu vayomer ani yosef achikhem asher-mekhartem oti mitzrayemah\nAnd 
 Joseph said unto his brethren: ‘Come near to me\, I pray you.’ And the
 y came near. And he said: ‘I am Joseph your brother\, whom ye sold into 
 Egypt.\n\nJoseph says to the brothers who sold him\, "Come close to me." I
 t is one of the great moments of forgiveness in the Torah.\n\nOpen Aleph: 
 https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270913@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270913
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270914
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 50:20
DESCRIPTION:וְאַתֶּם חֲשַׁבְתֶּם עָלַי רָעָה 
 אֱלֹהִים חֲשָׁבָהּ לְטֹבָה לְמַעַן עֲ
 שֹׂה כַּיּוֹם הַזֶּה לְהַחֲיֹת עַם־רָב׃
 \nVe'atem chashavtem alai ra'ah Elohim chashavah letovah lema'an asoh kayo
 m hazeh lehachayot am-rav\nAnd as for you\, ye meant evil against me\; but
  God meant it for good\, to bring to pass\, as it is this day\, to save mu
 ch people alive.\n\nJoseph tells his brothers that what they meant for har
 m\, God turned to good. Hard chapters of a life can lead somewhere good.\n
 \nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270914@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270914
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270915
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 3:5
DESCRIPTION:וַיֹּאמֶר אַל־תִּקְרַב הֲלֹם שַׁל
 ־נְעָלֶיךָ מֵעַל רַגְלֶיךָ כִּי הַמָּק
 וֹם אֲשֶׁר אַתָּה עוֹמֵד עָלָיו אַדְמַת
 ־קֹדֶשׁ הוּא׃\nVayomer al-tikrav halom shal-ne'alekha me'al ra
 glekha ki hamakom asher atah omed alav admat-kodesh hu\nAnd He said: ‘Dr
 aw not nigh hither\; put off thy shoes from off thy feet\, for the place w
 hereon thou standest is holy ground.’\n\nAt the burning bush Moses is to
 ld to take off his shoes\, because the ground is holy. Some moments call f
 or us to slow down and pay attention.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.o
 nrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270915@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270915
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270916
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 3:14
DESCRIPTION:וַיֹּאמֶר אֱלֹהִים אֶל־מֹשֶׁה אֶ
 הְיֶה אֲשֶׁר אֶהְיֶה וַיֹּאמֶר כֹּה תֹא
 מַר לִבְנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל אֶהְיֶה שְׁלָחַ
 נִי אֲלֵיכֶם׃\nVayomer Elohim el-Mosheh ehyeh asher ehyeh vayo
 mer koh tomar livnei Yisra'el ehyeh shelachani aleikhem\nAnd God said unto
  Moses: ‘I AM THAT I AM’\; and He said: ‘Thus shalt thou say unto th
 e children of Israel: I AM hath sent me unto you.’\n\nEhyeh asher ehyeh:
  "I will be what I will be." God's name here is about being present\, in e
 very time and place.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/mor
 ning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270916@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270916
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270917
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 13:8
DESCRIPTION:וְהִגַּדְתָּ לְבִנְךָ בַּיּוֹם הַ
 הוּא לֵאמֹר בַּעֲבוּר זֶה עָשָׂה יְהוָה 
 לִי בְּצֵאתִי מִמִּצְרָיִם׃\nVehigadta levinkha b
 ayom hahu lemor ba'avur zeh asah Adonai li betzeti mimitzrayim\nAnd thou s
 halt tell thy son in that day\, saying: It is because of that which the LO
 RD did for me when I came forth out of Egypt.\n\nThis verse is why we tell
  the Passover story at the Seder. Each generation tells it as if it happen
 ed to them.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270917@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270917
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270918
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 14:14
DESCRIPTION:יְהוָה יִלָּחֵם לָכֶם וְאַתֶּם 
 תַּחֲרִישׁוּן׃\nAdonai yilachem lakhem ve'atem tacharishun\n
 The LORD will fight for you\, and ye shall hold your peace.’\n\nAt the S
 ea of Reeds\, Moses tells the frightened people that God will fight for th
 em. Sometimes the right move is to stay calm and trust.\n\nOpen Aleph: htt
 ps://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270918@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270918
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270919
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 15:2
DESCRIPTION:עָזִּי וְזִמְרָת יָהּ וַיְהִי־לִי
  לִישׁוּעָה זֶה אֵלִי וְאַנְוֵהוּ אֱלֹ
 הֵי אָבִי וַאֲרֹמְמֶנְהוּ׃\nAzi vezimrat yah vayhi
 -li lishu'ah zeh eli ve'anvehu elohei avi va'aromemenhu\nThe LORD is my st
 rength and song\, And He is become my salvation\; This is my God\, and I w
 ill glorify Him\; My father’s God\, and I will exalt Him.\n\nFrom the So
 ng at the Sea: "The Lord is my strength and my song." These words are sung
  in synagogue every morning.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.c
 om/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270919@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270919
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270920
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 15:11
DESCRIPTION:מִי־כָמֹכָה בָּאֵלִם יְהוָה מִי 
 כָּמֹכָה נֶאְדָּר בַּקֹּדֶשׁ נוֹרָא תְ
 הִלֹּת עֹשֵׂה פֶלֶא׃\nMi-khamokhah ba'elim Adonai mi kam
 okhah nedar bakodesh nora tehilot oseh fele\nWho is like unto Thee\, O LOR
 D\, among the mighty? Who is like unto Thee\, glorious in holiness\, Fearf
 ul in praises\, doing wonders?\n\nMi chamocha\, "Who is like You?" This li
 ne from the Song at the Sea is part of the daily prayers\, just after the 
 Shema.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270920@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270920
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270921
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 19:6
DESCRIPTION:וְאַתֶּם תִּהְיוּ־לִי מַמְלֶכֶת 
 כֹּהֲנִים וְגוֹי קָדוֹשׁ אֵלֶּה הַדְּבָ
 רִים אֲשֶׁר תְּדַבֵּר אֶל־בְּנֵי יִשְׂ
 רָאֵל׃\nVe'atem tihyu-li mamlekhet kohanim vegoy kadosh eleh hadevar
 im asher tedaber el-benei Yisra'el\nand ye shall be unto Me a kingdom of p
 riests\, and a holy nation. These are the words which thou shalt speak unt
 o the children of Israel.’\n\nAt Sinai the whole people is called a king
 dom of priests and a holy nation. Holiness is meant for everyone\, not onl
 y for a few.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270921@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270921
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270922
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 20:2
DESCRIPTION:אָנֹכִי יְהוָה אֱלֹהֶיךָ אֲשֶׁר ה
 וֹצֵאתִיךָ מֵאֶרֶץ מִצְרַיִם מִבֵּית עֲ
 בָדִים׃\nAnokhi Adonai Elohekha asher hotzetikha me'eretz Mitzrayim
  mibeit avadim\nI am the LORD thy God\, who brought thee out of the land o
 f Egypt\, out of the house of bondage.\n\nThe Ten Commandments begin with 
 who God is: the One who brought us out of slavery. Freedom comes first\, a
 nd the commandments follow.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.co
 m/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270922@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270922
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270923
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 20:8
DESCRIPTION:זָכוֹר אֶת־יוֹם הַשַׁבָּת לְקַדְּ
 שׁוֹ\nZakhor et-yom hashabat lekadesho\nRemember the sabbath day\, to 
 keep it holy.\n\nZachor: "Remember the Shabbat day." We remember it with c
 andles\, Kiddush\, rest and time with the people we love.\n\nOpen Aleph: h
 ttps://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270923@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270923
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270924
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 20:12
DESCRIPTION:כַּבֵּד אֶת־אָבִיךָ וְאֶת־אִמֶּ
 ךָ לְמַעַן יַאֲרִכוּן יָמֶיךָ עַל הָאֲ
 דָמָה אֲשֶׁר־יְהוָה אֱלֹהֶיךָ נֹתֵן לָ
 ךְ׃\nKabed et-avikha ve'et-imekha lema'an ya'arikhun yamekha al ha'adam
 ah asher-Adonai Elohekha noten lakh\nHonour thy father and thy mother\, th
 at thy days may be long upon the land which the LORD thy God giveth thee.\
 n\nHonour your father and your mother. It is one of the Ten Commandments\,
  and the first that comes with a promise of long life.\n\nOpen Aleph: http
 s://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270924@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270924
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270925
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 22:20
DESCRIPTION:וְגֵר לֹא־תוֹנֶה וְלֹא תִלְחָצֶנּ
 וּ כִּי־גֵרִים הֱיִיתֶם בְּאֶרֶץ מִצְרָ
 יִם׃\nVeger lo-toneh velo tilchatzenu ki-gerim heyitem be'eretz Mitzra
 yim\nAnd a stranger shalt thou not wrong\, neither shalt thou oppress him\
 ; for ye were strangers in the land of Egypt.\n\nDo not wrong the stranger
 \, because you were strangers in Egypt. This idea comes up again and again
  in the Torah.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270925@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270925
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270926
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 23:2
DESCRIPTION:לֹא־תִהְיֶה אַחֲרֵי־רַבִּים לְרָ
 עֹת וְלֹא־תַעֲנֶה עַל־רִב לִנְטֹת אַחֲ
 רֵי רַבִּים לְהַטֹּת׃\nLo-tihyeh acharei-rabim lera'ot 
 velo-ta'aneh al-riv lintot acharei rabim lehatot\nThou shalt not follow a 
 multitude to do evil\; neither shalt thou bear witness in a cause to turn 
 aside after a multitude to pervert justice\;\n\nDo not follow the crowd to
  do wrong. Doing the right thing sometimes means standing apart.\n\nOpen A
 leph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270926@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270926
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270927
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 23:9
DESCRIPTION:וְגֵר לֹא תִלְחָץ וְאַתֶּם יְדַעְ
 תֶּם אֶת־נֶפֶשׁ הַגֵּר כִּי־גֵרִים הֱיִ
 יתֶם בְּאֶרֶץ מִצְרָיִם׃\nVeger lo tilchatz ve'atem 
 yedatem et-nefesh hager ki-gerim heyitem be'eretz Mitzrayim\nAnd a strange
 r shalt thou not oppress\; for ye know the heart of a stranger\, seeing ye
  were strangers in the land of Egypt.\n\n"You know the heart of the strang
 er." Our own history should make us kind to newcomers.\n\nOpen Aleph: http
 s://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270927@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270927
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270928
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 25:8
DESCRIPTION:וְעָשׂוּ לִי מִקְדָּשׁ וְשָׁכַנְ
 תִּי בְּתוֹכָם׃\nVe'asu li mikdash veshakhanti betokham\nAnd
  let them make Me a sanctuary\, that I may dwell among them.\n\n"Make Me a
  sanctuary\, and I will dwell among them." Not "in it\," but among them: G
 od lives among people\, in the places they make holy.\n\nOpen Aleph: https
 ://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270928@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270928
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270929
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 33:13
DESCRIPTION:וְעַתָּה אִם־נָא מָצָאתִי חֵן בְּ
 עֵינֶיךָ הוֹדִעֵנִי נָא אֶת־דְּרָכֶךָ 
 וְאֵדָעֲךָ לְמַעַן אֶמְצָא־חֵן בְּעֵי
 נֶיךָ וּרְאֵה כִּי עַמְּךָ הַגּוֹי הַ
 זֶּה׃\nVe'atah im-na matzati chen be'einekha hodi'eni na et-derakhekh
 a ve'eda'akha lema'an emtza-chen be'einekha ure'eh ki amekha hagoy hazeh\n
 Now therefore\, I pray Thee\, if I have found grace in Thy sight\, show me
  now Thy ways\, that I may know Thee\, to the end that I may find grace in
  Thy sight\; and consider that this nation is Thy people.’\n\nMoses asks
  God\, "Show me Your ways\, so that I may know You." Learning is one of th
 e ways Jews come close to God.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender
 .com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270929@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270929
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270930
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 34:6
DESCRIPTION:וַיַּעֲבֹר יְהוָה עַל־פָּנָיו וַ
 יִּקְרָא יְהוָה יְהוָה אֵל רַחוּם וְחַ
 נּוּן אֶרֶךְ אַפַּיִם וְרַב־חֶסֶד וֶאֱ
 מֶת\nVaya'avor Adonai al-panav vayikra Adonai Adonai el rachum vechanun
  erekh apayim verav-chesed ve'emet\nAnd the LORD passed by before him\, an
 d proclaimed: ‘The LORD\, the LORD\, God\, merciful and gracious\, long-
 suffering\, and abundant in goodness and truth\;\n\nThese are God's qualit
 ies of mercy\, sung on the High Holy Days: compassionate\, gracious\, slow
  to anger\, full of kindness and truth.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review
 .onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20270930@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270930
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271001
SUMMARY:Torah: Leviticus 19:2
DESCRIPTION:דַּבֵּר אֶל־כָּל־עֲדַת בְּנֵי־יִ
 שְׂרָאֵל וְאָמַרְתָּ אֲלֵהֶם קְדֹשִׁים 
 תִּהְיוּ כִּי קָדוֹשׁ אֲנִי יְהוָה אֱלֹ
 הֵיכֶם׃\nDaber el-kol-adat benei-Yisra'el ve'amarta alehem kedoshim
  tihyu ki kadosh ani Adonai Eloheikhem\nSpeak unto all the congregation of
  the children of Israel\, and say unto them: Ye shall be holy\; for I the 
 LORD your God am holy.\n\n"You shall be holy\, for I am holy." The chapter
  that follows shows what that means: honesty\, kindness and fairness in ev
 eryday life.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271001@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271001
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271002
SUMMARY:Torah: Leviticus 19:3
DESCRIPTION:אִישׁ אִמּוֹ וְאָבִיו תִּירָאוּ 
 וְאֶת־שַׁבְּתֹתַי תִּשְׁמֹרוּ אֲנִי יְ
 הוָה אֱלֹהֵיכֶם׃\nIsh imo ve'aviv tira'u ve'et-shabetotai t
 ishmoru ani Adonai Eloheikhem\nYe shall fear every man his mother\, and hi
 s father\, and ye shall keep My sabbaths: I am the LORD your God.\n\nRespe
 ct your parents and keep Shabbat. Both are about honouring where we come f
 rom.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271002@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271002
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271003
SUMMARY:Torah: Leviticus 19:9
DESCRIPTION:וּבְקֻצְרְכֶם אֶת־קְצִיר אַרְצְ
 כֶם לֹא תְכַלֶּה פְּאַת שָׂדְךָ לִקְצֹר 
 וְלֶקֶט קְצִירְךָ לֹא תְלַקֵּט׃\nUvekutzrekhem
  et-ketzir artzekhem lo tekhaleh pe'at sadekha liktzor veleket ketzirekha 
 lo telaket\nAnd when ye reap the harvest of your land\, thou shalt not who
 lly reap the corner of thy field\, neither shalt thou gather the gleaning 
 of thy harvest.\n\nLeave the corners of your field for people in need. Giv
 ing to others is built right into how we earn and spend.\n\nOpen Aleph: ht
 tps://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271003@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271003
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271004
SUMMARY:Torah: Leviticus 19:14
DESCRIPTION:לֹא־תְקַלֵּל חֵרֵשׁ וְלִפְנֵי עִ
 וֵּר לֹא תִתֵּן מִכְשֹׁל וְיָרֵאתָ מֵּ
 אֱלֹהֶיךָ אֲנִי יְהוָה׃\nLo-tekalel cheresh velifnei 
 iver lo titen mikhshol veyareta me'Elohekha ani Adonai\nThou shalt not cur
 se the deaf\, nor put a stumbling-block before the blind\, but thou shalt 
 fear thy God: I am the LORD.\n\nDo not curse the deaf or put a stumbling b
 lock before the blind. Treat everyone with care\, especially those who can
 not defend themselves.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/m
 orning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271004@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271004
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271005
SUMMARY:Torah: Leviticus 19:16
DESCRIPTION:לֹא־תֵלֵךְ רָכִיל בְּעַמֶּיךָ לֹא
  תַעֲמֹד עַל־דַּם רֵעֶךָ אֲנִי יְהוָה׃\nL
 o-telekh rakhil be'amekha lo ta'amod al-dam re'ekha ani Adonai\nThou shalt
  not go up and down as a talebearer among thy people\; neither shalt thou 
 stand idly by the blood of thy neighbour: I am the LORD.\n\nDo not spread 
 gossip\, and do not stand by while your neighbour is in danger. Words can 
 hurt\, and silence can too.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.co
 m/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271005@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271005
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271006
SUMMARY:Torah: Leviticus 19:18
DESCRIPTION:לֹא־תִקֹּם וְלֹא־תִטֹּר אֶת־בְּ
 נֵי עַמֶּךָ וְאָהַבְתָּ לְרֵעֲךָ כָּמוֹ
 ךָ אֲנִי יְהוָה׃\nLo-tikom velo-titor et-benei amekha ve'aha
 vta lere'akha kamokha ani Adonai\nThou shalt not take vengeance\, nor bear
  any grudge against the children of thy people\, but thou shalt love thy n
 eighbour as thyself: I am the LORD.\n\n"Love your neighbour as yourself." 
 Rabbi Akiva called this the great principle of the whole Torah.\n\nOpen Al
 eph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271006@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271006
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271007
SUMMARY:Torah: Leviticus 19:32
DESCRIPTION:מִפְּנֵי שֵׂיבָה תָּקוּם וְהָדַרְ
 תָּ פְּנֵי זָקֵן וְיָרֵאתָ מֵּאֱלֹהֶיךָ
  אֲנִי יְהוָה׃\nMipenei seivah takum vehadarta penei zaken vey
 areta me'Elohekha ani Adonai\nThou shalt rise up before the hoary head\, a
 nd honour the face of the old man\, and thou shalt fear thy God: I am the 
 LORD.\n\nRise before the elderly and honour them. Age brings wisdom\, and 
 the Torah asks us to show it respect.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.o
 nrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271007@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271007
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271008
SUMMARY:Torah: Leviticus 25:10
DESCRIPTION:וְקִדַּשְׁתֶּם אֵת שְׁנַת הַחֲמִ
 שִּׁים שָׁנָה וּקְרָאתֶם דְּרוֹר בָּאָ
 רֶץ לְכָל־יֹשְׁבֶיהָ יוֹבֵל הִוא תִּהְ
 יֶה לָכֶם וְשַׁבְתֶּם אִישׁ אֶל־אֲחֻזָּ
 תוֹ וְאִישׁ אֶל־מִשְׁפַּחְתּוֹ תָּשֻׁב
 וּ׃\nVekidashtem et shenat hachamishim shanah ukeratem deror ba'aretz l
 ekhol-yosheveha yovel hiv tihyeh lakhem veshavtem ish el-achuzato ve'ish e
 l-mishpachto tashuvu\nAnd ye shall hallow the fiftieth year\, and proclaim
  liberty throughout the land unto all the inhabitants thereof\; it shall b
 e a jubilee unto you\; and ye shall return every man unto his possession\,
  and ye shall return every man unto his family.\n\n"Proclaim liberty throu
 ghout the land." These words about the Jubilee year are cast on the Libert
 y Bell in Philadelphia.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/
 morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271008@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271008
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271009
SUMMARY:Torah: Numbers 6:24
DESCRIPTION:יְבָרֶכְךָ יְהוָה וְיִשְׁמְרֶךָ׃\
 nYevarekhkha Adonai veyishmerekha\nThe LORD bless thee\, and keep thee\;\n
 \nThe first line of the Priestly Blessing\, still said in synagogues and b
 y parents to children on Friday night.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.
 onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271009@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271009
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271010
SUMMARY:Torah: Numbers 6:26
DESCRIPTION:יִשָּׂא יְהוָה פָּנָיו אֵלֶיךָ וְ
 יָשֵׂם לְךָ שָׁלוֹם׃\nYisa Adonai panav elekha veyasem l
 ekha shalom\nThe LORD lift up His countenance upon thee\, and give thee pe
 ace.\n\nThe Priestly Blessing ends with shalom\, peace. In Hebrew\, shalom
  also means wholeness: everything in its right place.\n\nOpen Aleph: https
 ://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271010@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271010
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271011
SUMMARY:Torah: Numbers 11:29
DESCRIPTION:וַיֹּאמֶר לוֹ מֹשֶׁה הַמְקַנֵּא 
 אַתָּה לִי וּמִי יִתֵּן כָּל־עַם יְהוָה 
 נְבִיאִים כִּי־יִתֵּן יְהוָה אֶת־רוּח
 וֹ עֲלֵיהֶם׃\nVayomer lo Mosheh hamkane atah li umi yiten kol-a
 m Adonai nevi'im ki-yiten Adonai et-rucho aleihem\nAnd Moses said unto him
 : ‘Art thou jealous for my sake? would that all the LORD’S people were
  prophets\, that the LORD would put His spirit upon them! ’\n\nWhen othe
 rs begin to prophesy\, Moses is not jealous. He wishes everyone could shar
 e God's spirit. Great leaders lift others up.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-
 review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271011@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271011
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271012
SUMMARY:Torah: Numbers 15:39
DESCRIPTION:וְהָיָה לָכֶם לְצִיצִת וּרְאִיתֶם
  אֹתוֹ וּזְכַרְתֶּם אֶת־כָּל־מִצְוֹת יְ
 הוָה וַעֲשִׂיתֶם אֹתָם וְלֹא־תָתֻרוּ אַ
 חֲרֵי לְבַבְכֶם וְאַחֲרֵי עֵינֵיכֶם אֲ
 שֶׁר־אַתֶּם זֹנִים אַחֲרֵיהֶם׃\nVehayah lakhem
  letzitzit ure'item oto uzekhartem et-kol-mitzvot Adonai va'asitem otam ve
 lo-taturu acharei levavkhem ve'acharei eineikhem asher-atem zonim achareih
 em\nAnd it shall be unto you for a fringe\, that ye may look upon it\, and
  remember all the commandments of the LORD\, and do them\; and that ye go 
 not about after your own heart and your own eyes\, after which ye use to g
 o astray\;\n\nThis verse is about the tzitzit\, the fringes on the tallit.
  Seeing them is a reminder of the commandments and of who we want to be.\n
 \nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271012@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271012
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271013
SUMMARY:Torah: Numbers 24:5
DESCRIPTION:מַה־טֹּבוּ אֹהָלֶיךָ יַעֲקֹב מִ
 שְׁכְּנֹתֶיךָ יִשְׂרָאֵל׃\nMah-tovu ohalekha Ya'ak
 ov mishkenotekha Yisra'el\nHow goodly are thy tents\, O Jacob\, Thy dwelli
 ngs\, O Israel!\n\nMah tovu\, "How good are your tents." Many synagogues o
 pen the morning service with these words.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-revi
 ew.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271013@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271013
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271014
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 4:9
DESCRIPTION:רַק הִשָּׁמֶר לְךָ וּשְׁמֹר נַפְ
 שְׁךָ מְאֹד פֶּן־תִּשְׁכַּח אֶת־הַדְּ
 בָרִים אֲשֶׁר־רָאוּ עֵינֶיךָ וּפֶן־יָס
 וּרוּ מִלְּבָבְךָ כֹּל יְמֵי חַיֶּיךָ 
 וְהוֹדַעְתָּם לְבָנֶיךָ וְלִבְנֵי בָנֶ
 יךָ׃\nRak hishamer lekha ushemor nafshekha me'od pen-tishkach et-hadev
 arim asher-ra'u einekha ufen-yasuru milevavekha kol yemei chayekha vehodat
 am levanekha velivnei vanekha\nOnly take heed to thyself\, and keep thy so
 ul diligently\, lest thou forget the things which thine eyes saw\, and les
 t they depart from thy heart all the days of thy life\; but make them know
 n unto thy children and thy children’s children\;\n\nDo not forget what 
 you have seen\, and teach it to your children and grandchildren. Memory is
  how a people stays alive.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com
 /#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271014@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271014
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271015
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 6:4
DESCRIPTION:שְׁמַע יִשְׂרָאֵל יְהוָה אֱלֹהֵינ
 וּ יְהוָה אֶחָד׃\nShema Yisra'el Adonai Eloheinu Adonai echa
 d\nHEAR\, O ISRAEL: THE LORD OUR GOD\, THE LORD IS ONE.\n\nThe Shema\, the
  central line of Jewish prayer: "Hear\, O Israel\, the Lord is our God\, t
 he Lord is One." It is said morning and night.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef
 -review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271015@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271015
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271016
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 6:5
DESCRIPTION:וְאָהַבְתָּ אֵת יְהוָה אֱלֹהֶיךָ 
 בְּכָל־לְבָבְךָ וּבְכָל־נַפְשְׁךָ וּבְ
 כָל־מְאֹדֶךָ׃\nVe'ahavta et Adonai Elohekha bekhol-levavekha 
 uvekhol-nafshekha uvekhol-me'odekha\nAnd thou shalt love the LORD thy God 
 with all thy heart\, and with all thy soul\, and with all thy might.\n\nV'
 ahavta: love God with all your heart\, all your soul and all your strength
 . Faith in Judaism is about love\, not only belief.\n\nOpen Aleph: https:/
 /alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271016@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271016
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271017
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 6:7
DESCRIPTION:וְשִׁנַּנְתָּם לְבָנֶיךָ וְדִבַּ
 רְתָּ בָּם בְּשִׁבְתְּךָ בְּבֵיתֶךָ וּ
 בְלֶכְתְּךָ בַדֶּרֶךְ וּבְשָׁכְבְּךָ 
 וּבְקוּמֶךָ׃\nVeshinantam levanekha vedibarta bam beshivtekha 
 beveitekha uvelekhtekha vaderekh uveshakhbekha uvekumekha\nand thou shalt 
 teach them diligently unto thy children\, and shalt talk of them when thou
  sittest in thy house\, and when thou walkest by the way\, and when thou l
 iest down\, and when thou risest up.\n\nTalk about these words at home\, o
 n the road\, when you lie down and when you get up. That is why the Shema 
 is said at bedtime and in the morning.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.
 onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271017@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271017
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271018
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 8:3
DESCRIPTION:וַיְעַנְּךָ וַיַּרְעִבֶךָ וַיַּ
 אֲכִלְךָ אֶת הַמָּן אֲשֶׁר לֹא־יָדַעְ
 תָּ וְלֹא יָדְעוּן אֲבֹתֶיךָ לְמַעַן ה
 וֹדִעֲךָ כִּי לֹא עַל־הַלֶּחֶם לְבַדּוֹ
  יִחְיֶה הָאָדָם כִּי עַל־כָּל־מוֹצָא 
 פִי־יְהוָה יִחְיֶה הָאָדָם׃\nVay'anekha vayar'ive
 kha vaya'akhilkha et haman asher lo-yadata velo yad'un avotekha lema'an ho
 di'akha ki lo al-halechem levado yichyeh ha'adam ki al-kol-motza fi-Adonai
  yichyeh ha'adam\nAnd He afflicted thee\, and suffered thee to hunger\, an
 d fed thee with manna\, which thou knewest not\, neither did thy fathers k
 now\; that He might make thee know that man doth not live by bread only\, 
 but by every thing that proceedeth out of the mouth of the LORD doth man l
 ive.\n\n"A person does not live by bread alone." We need meaning\, learnin
 g and purpose as much as food.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender
 .com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271018@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271018
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271019
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 8:10
DESCRIPTION:וְאָכַלְתָּ וְשָׂבָעְתָּ וּבֵרַ
 כְתָּ אֶת־יְהוָה אֱלֹהֶיךָ עַל־הָאָרֶץ 
 הַטֹּבָה אֲשֶׁר נָתַן־לָךְ׃\nVe'akhalta vesava'et
 a uverakhta et-Adonai Elohekha al-ha'aretz hatovah asher natan-lakh\nAnd t
 hou shalt eat and be satisfied\, and bless the LORD thy God for the good l
 and which He hath given thee.\n\nEat\, be satisfied\, and bless. This vers
 e is the source of Birkat Hamazon\, the blessing after meals.\n\nOpen Alep
 h: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271019@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271019
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271020
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 10:19
DESCRIPTION:וַאֲהַבְתֶּם אֶת־הַגֵּר כִּי־גֵ
 רִים הֱיִיתֶם בְּאֶרֶץ מִצְרָיִם׃\nVa'ahavte
 m et-hager ki-gerim heyitem be'eretz Mitzrayim\nLove ye therefore the stra
 nger\; for ye were strangers in the land of Egypt.\n\nLove the stranger\, 
 because you were strangers in Egypt. The Torah asks for more than not hurt
 ing newcomers\; it asks us to love them.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-revie
 w.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271020@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271020
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271021
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 16:20
DESCRIPTION:צֶדֶק צֶדֶק תִּרְדֹּף לְמַעַן תִּ
 חְיֶה וְיָרַשְׁתָּ אֶת־הָאָרֶץ אֲשֶׁר־
 יְהוָה אֱלֹהֶיךָ נֹתֵן לָךְ׃\nTzedek tzedek tirdo
 f lema'an tichyeh veyarashta et-ha'aretz asher-Adonai Elohekha noten lakh\
 nJustice\, justice shalt thou follow\, that thou mayest live\, and inherit
  the land which the LORD thy God giveth thee.\n\nTzedek tzedek tirdof: "Ju
 stice\, justice you shall pursue." The word is said twice\, to show how ha
 rd we should work for it.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/
 #/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271021@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271021
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271022
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 30:14
DESCRIPTION:כִּי־קָרוֹב אֵלֶיךָ הַדָּבָר מְאֹ
 ד בְּפִיךָ וּבִלְבָבְךָ לַעֲשֹׂתוֹ׃\nKi-ka
 rov elekha hadavar me'od befikha uvilvavekha la'asoto\nBut the word is ver
 y nigh unto thee\, in thy mouth\, and in thy heart\, that thou mayest do i
 t.\n\nThe Torah is not far away: it is in your mouth and in your heart. It
  is within reach\, one word at a time.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.
 onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271022@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271022
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271023
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 30:19
DESCRIPTION:הַעִידֹתִי בָכֶם הַיּוֹם אֶת־הַ
 שָּׁמַיִם וְאֶת־הָאָרֶץ הַחַיִּים וְהַ
 מָּוֶת נָתַתִּי לְפָנֶיךָ הַבְּרָכָה וְ
 הַקְּלָלָה וּבָחַרְתָּ בַּחַיִּים לְמַ
 עַן תִּחְיֶה אַתָּה וְזַרְעֶךָ׃\nHa'idoti vakh
 em hayom et-hashamayim ve'et-ha'aretz hachayim vehamavet natati lefanekha 
 haberakhah vehakelalah uvacharta bachayim lema'an tichyeh atah vezar'ekha\
 nI call heaven and earth to witness against you this day\, that I have set
  before thee life and death\, the blessing and the curse\; therefore choos
 e life\, that thou mayest live\, thou and thy seed\;\n\n"Choose life." Eve
 ry day brings choices\, and the Torah asks us to choose the ones that lead
  to life and blessing.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/m
 orning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271023@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271023
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271024
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 31:6
DESCRIPTION:חִזְקוּ וְאִמְצוּ אַל־תִּירְאוּ 
 וְאַל־תַּעַרְצוּ מִפְּנֵיהֶם כִּי יְה
 וָה אֱלֹהֶיךָ הוּא הַהֹלֵךְ עִמָּךְ לֹא 
 יַרְפְּךָ וְלֹא יַעַזְבֶךָּ׃\nChizku ve'imtzu al
 -tir'u ve'al-ta'artzu mipeneihem ki Adonai Elohekha hu haholekh imakh lo y
 arpekha velo ya'azveka\nBe strong and of good courage\, fear not\, nor be 
 affrighted at them\; for the LORD thy God\, He it is that doth go with the
 e\; He will not fail thee\, nor forsake thee.’\n\nChazak ve'ematz: "Be s
 trong and of good courage." Moses says this before the people enter the la
 nd without him.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271024@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271024
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271025
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 6:6
DESCRIPTION:וְהָיוּ הַדְּבָרִים הָאֵלֶּה אֲ
 שֶׁר אָנֹכִי מְצַוְּךָ הַיּוֹם עַל־לְבָ
 בֶךָ׃\nVehayu hadevarim ha'eleh asher anokhi metzavekha hayom al-leva
 vekha\nAnd these words\, which I command thee this day\, shall be upon thy
  heart\;\n\n"These words shall be upon your heart." Learning Torah is mean
 t to go deeper than memory\, into who we are.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-
 review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271025@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271025
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271026
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 31:16
DESCRIPTION:וְשָׁמְרוּ בְנֵי־יִשְׂרָאֵל אֶת־
 הַשַּׁבָּת לַעֲשׂוֹת אֶת־הַשַּׁבָּת לְ
 דֹרֹתָם בְּרִית עוֹלָם׃\nVeshamru venei-Yisra'el et-h
 ashabat la'asot et-hashabat ledorotam berit olam\nWherefore the children o
 f Israel shall keep the sabbath\, to observe the sabbath throughout their 
 generations\, for a perpetual covenant.\n\nV'shamru: the people of Israel 
 shall keep the Shabbat for all generations. This verse is sung on Friday n
 ight and Shabbat morning.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/
 #/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271026@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271026
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271027
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 34:10
DESCRIPTION:וְלֹא־קָם נָבִיא עוֹד בְּיִשְׂרָ
 אֵל כְּמֹשֶׁה אֲשֶׁר יְדָעוֹ יְהוָה פָּ
 נִים אֶל־פָּנִים׃\nVelo-kam navi od beyisra'el kemosheh as
 her yeda'o Adonai panim el-panim\nAnd there hath not arisen a prophet sinc
 e in Israel like unto Moses\, whom the LORD knew face to face\;\n\nNear th
 e very end of the Torah: no prophet arose like Moses\, who knew God face t
 o face. Then we roll the scroll back and start again.\n\nOpen Aleph: https
 ://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271027@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271027
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271028
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 1:1
DESCRIPTION:בְּרֵאשִׁית בָּרָא אֱלֹהִים אֵת 
 הַשָּׁמַיִם וְאֵת הָאָרֶץ׃\nBereshit bara Elohim e
 t hashamayim ve'et ha'aretz\nIn the beginning God created the heaven and t
 he earth.\n\nThe Torah opens with its first word\, Bereshit\, "in the begi
 nning." Everything that follows starts here: the world has a Maker\, and i
 t did not come about by chance.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrende
 r.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271028@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271028
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271029
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 1:3
DESCRIPTION:וַיֹּאמֶר אֱלֹהִים יְהִי אוֹר וַ
 יְהִי־אוֹר׃\nVayomer Elohim yehi or vayhi-or\nAnd God said: ‘
 Let there be light.’ And there was light.\n\nThe first thing God makes i
 s light\, and He makes it with words. In Judaism speech has real power\, s
 o the words we choose each day matter.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.
 onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271029@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271029
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271030
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 1:27
DESCRIPTION:וַיִּבְרָא אֱלֹהִים אֶת־הָאָדָם 
 בְּצַלְמוֹ בְּצֶלֶם אֱלֹהִים בָּרָא אֹת
 וֹ זָכָר וּנְקֵבָה בָּרָא אֹתָם׃\nVayivra Eloh
 im et-ha'adam betzalmo betzelem Elohim bara oto zakhar unekevah bara otam\
 nAnd God created man in His own image\, in the image of God created He him
 \; male and female created He them.\n\nEvery person is made in the image o
 f God. That is why each human life has worth\, whoever the person is and w
 herever they come from.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/
 morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271030@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271030
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271031
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 1:31
DESCRIPTION:וַיַּרְא אֱלֹהִים אֶת־כָּל־אֲשֶׁ
 ר עָשָׂה וְהִנֵּה־טוֹב מְאֹד וַיְהִי־עֶ
 רֶב וַיְהִי־בֹקֶר יוֹם הַשִּׁשִּׁי׃\nVayar
  Elohim et-kol-asher asah vehineh-tov me'od vayhi-erev vayhi-voker yom has
 hishi\nAnd God saw every thing that He had made\, and\, behold\, it was ve
 ry good. And there was evening and there was morning\, the sixth day.\n\nA
 fter each day God saw that it was good. On the sixth day\, with people in 
 the world\, it became "very good." Look for the good in your own day.\n\nO
 pen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271031@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271031
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271101
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 2:3
DESCRIPTION:וַיְבָרֶךְ אֱלֹהִים אֶת־יוֹם הַ
 שְּׁבִיעִי וַיְקַדֵּשׁ אֹתוֹ כִּי בוֹ 
 שָׁבַת מִכָּל־מְלַאכְתּוֹ אֲשֶׁר־בָּרָ
 א אֱלֹהִים לַעֲשׂוֹת׃\nVayvarekh Elohim et-yom hashevi'
 i vaykadesh oto ki vo shavat mikol-melakhto asher-bara Elohim la'asot\nAnd
  God blessed the seventh day\, and hallowed it\; because that in it He res
 ted from all His work which God in creating had made.\n\nThis is the first
  Shabbat. God rested on the seventh day and made it holy\, and we rest on 
 it too. Shabbat is a gift of time\, not only a rule.\n\nOpen Aleph: https:
 //alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271101@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271101
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271102
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 2:15
DESCRIPTION:וַיִּקַּח יְהוָה אֱלֹהִים אֶת־הָ
 אָדָם וַיַּנִּחֵהוּ בְגַן־עֵדֶן לְעָבְ
 דָהּ וּלְשָׁמְרָהּ׃\nVayikach Adonai Elohim et-ha'adam v
 ayanichehu vegan-eden le'avedah uleshamerah\nAnd the LORD God took the man
 \, and put him into the garden of Eden to dress it and to keep it.\n\nAdam
  was put in the garden to work it and to guard it. The earth is placed in 
 our care\, and looking after it is part of our job.\n\nOpen Aleph: https:/
 /alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271102@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271102
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271103
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 2:18
DESCRIPTION:וַיֹּאמֶר יְהוָה אֱלֹהִים לֹא־טוֹ
 ב הֱיוֹת הָאָדָם לְבַדּוֹ אֶעֱשֶׂהּ־לּ
 וֹ עֵזֶר כְּנֶגְדּוֹ׃\nVayomer Adonai Elohim lo-tov hey
 ot ha'adam levado e'eseh-lo ezer kenegdo\nAnd the LORD God said: ‘It is 
 not good that the man should be alone\; I will make him a help meet for hi
 m.’\n\n"It is not good to be alone." People need each other. Community\,
  friendship and family are part of how we were made.\n\nOpen Aleph: https:
 //alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271103@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271103
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271104
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 4:9
DESCRIPTION:וַיֹּאמֶר יְהוָה אֶל־קַיִן אֵי הֶ
 בֶל אָחִיךָ וַיֹּאמֶר לֹא יָדַעְתִּי הֲ
 שֹׁמֵר אָחִי אָנֹכִי׃\nVayomer Adonai el-kayin ei hevel
  achikha vayomer lo yadati hashomer achi anokhi\nAnd the LORD said unto Ca
 in: ‘Where is Abel thy brother?’ And he said: ‘I know not\; am I my 
 brother’s keeper?’\n\nCain asks\, "Am I my brother's keeper?" The rest
  of the Torah answers yes. We are responsible for one another.\n\nOpen Ale
 ph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271104@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271104
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271105
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 12:1
DESCRIPTION:וַיֹּאמֶר יְהוָה אֶל־אַבְרָם לֶךְ
 ־לְךָ מֵאַרְצְךָ וּמִמּוֹלַדְתְּךָ וּ
 מִבֵּית אָבִיךָ אֶל־הָאָרֶץ אֲשֶׁר אַרְ
 אֶךָּ׃\nVayomer Adonai el-Avram lekh-lekha me'artzekha umimoladtekha
  umibeit avikha el-ha'aretz asher ar'eka\nNow the LORD said unto Abram: 
 ‘Get thee out of thy country\, and from thy kindred\, and from thy fathe
 r’s house\, unto the land that I will show thee.\n\nLech lecha: "go for 
 yourself." Abraham leaves everything familiar to follow God. Every new sta
 rt\, including learning Hebrew\, takes a first step like this.\n\nOpen Ale
 ph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271105@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271105
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271106
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 12:2
DESCRIPTION:וְאֶעֶשְׂךָ לְגוֹי גָּדוֹל וַאֲבָ
 רֶכְךָ וַאֲגַדְּלָה שְׁמֶךָ וֶהְיֵה בְּ
 רָכָה׃\nVe'e'eskha legoy gadol va'avarekhkha va'agadelah shemekha ve
 hyeh berakhah\nAnd I will make of thee a great nation\, and I will bless t
 hee\, and make thy name great\; and be thou a blessing.\n\nAbraham is told
  not only that he will be blessed but that he will be a blessing. A good l
 ife is one that brings good to others.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.
 onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271106@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271106
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271107
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 15:5
DESCRIPTION:וַיּוֹצֵא אֹתוֹ הַחוּצָה וַיֹּאמֶ
 ר הַבֶּט־נָא הַשָּׁמַיְמָה וּסְפֹר הַכּ
 וֹכָבִים אִם־תּוּכַל לִסְפֹּר אֹתָם וַ
 יֹּאמֶר לוֹ כֹּה יִהְיֶה זַרְעֶךָ׃\nVayotze 
 oto hachutzah vayomer habet-na hashamaymah usefor hakokhavim im-tukhal lis
 por otam vayomer lo koh yihyeh zar'ekha\nAnd He brought him forth abroad\,
  and said: ‘Look now toward heaven\, and count the stars\, if thou be ab
 le to count them’\; and He said unto him: ‘So shall thy seed be.’\n\
 nGod takes Abraham outside to count the stars. When things feel small or u
 ncertain\, step back and look at the bigger picture.\n\nOpen Aleph: https:
 //alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271107@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271107
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271108
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 18:25
DESCRIPTION:חָלִלָה לְּךָ מֵעֲשֹׂת כַּדָּבָר 
 הַזֶּה לְהָמִית צַדִּיק עִם־רָשָׁע וְהָ
 יָה כַצַדִּיק כָּרָשָׁע חָלִלָה לָּךְ 
 הֲשֹׁפֵט כָּל־הָאָרֶץ לֹא יַעֲשֶׂה מִ
 שְׁפָּט׃\nChalilah lekha me'asot kadavar hazeh lehamit tzadik im-r
 asha vehayah khatzadik karasha chalilah lakh hashofet kol-ha'aretz lo ya'a
 seh mishpat\nThat be far from Thee to do after this manner\, to slay the r
 ighteous with the wicked\, that so the righteous should be as the wicked\;
  that be far from Thee\; shall not the judge of all the earth do justly?
 ’\n\nAbraham argues with God to save the people of Sodom. In Jewish trad
 ition it is right to speak up for justice\, even before the highest author
 ity.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271108@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271108
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271109
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 28:15
DESCRIPTION:וְהִנֵּה אָנֹכִי עִמָּךְ וּשְׁמַ
 רְתִּיךָ בְּכֹל אֲשֶׁר־תֵּלֵךְ וַהֲשִׁ
 בֹתִיךָ אֶל־הָאֲדָמָה הַזֹּאת כִּי לֹא 
 אֶעֱזָבְךָ עַד אֲשֶׁר אִם־עָשִׂיתִי אֵת
  אֲשֶׁר־דִּבַּרְתִּי לָךְ׃\nVehineh anokhi imakh u
 shemartikha bekhol asher-telekh vahashivotikha el-ha'adamah hazot ki lo e'
 ezavekha ad asher im-asiti et asher-dibarti lakh\nAnd\, behold\, I am with
  thee\, and will keep thee whithersoever thou goest\, and will bring thee 
 back into this land\; for I will not leave thee\, until I have done that w
 hich I have spoken to thee of.’\n\nJacob is alone and running away\, and
  God promises: I am with you\, wherever you go. You are never as alone as 
 you feel.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271109@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271109
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271110
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 28:16
DESCRIPTION:וַיִּיקַץ יַעֲקֹב מִשְּׁנָתוֹ וַ
 יֹּאמֶר אָכֵן יֵשׁ יְהוָה בַּמָּקוֹם הַ
 זֶּה וְאָנֹכִי לֹא יָדָעְתִּי׃\nVayikatz Ya'ako
 v mishenato vayomer akhen yesh Adonai bamakom hazeh ve'anokhi lo yada'eti\
 nAnd Jacob awaked out of his sleep\, and he said: ‘Surely the LORD is in
  this place\; and I knew it not.’\n\nJacob wakes from his dream and says
  God was in this place and he did not know it. Holiness can be right where
  you are\, if you notice it.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.c
 om/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271110@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271110
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271111
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 32:11
DESCRIPTION:קָטֹנְתִּי מִכֹּל הַחֲסָדִים וּמִ
 כָּל־הָאֱמֶת אֲשֶׁר עָשִׂיתָ אֶת־עַבְ
 דֶּךָ כִּי בְמַקְלִי עָבַרְתִּי אֶת־הַ
 יַּרְדֵּן הַזֶּה וְעַתָּה הָיִיתִי לִ
 שְׁנֵי מַחֲנוֹת׃\nKatoneti mikol hachasadim umikol-ha'emet 
 asher asita et-avdekha ki vemakli avarti et-hayarden hazeh ve'atah hayiti 
 lishnei machanot\nI am not worthy of all the mercies\, and of all the trut
 h\, which Thou hast shown unto Thy servant\; for with my staff I passed ov
 er this Jordan\; and now I am become two camps.\n\nBefore meeting his brot
 her Esau\, Jacob says he is not worthy of all the kindness he has received
 . Gratitude and humility go together.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.o
 nrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271111@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271111
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271112
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 45:4
DESCRIPTION:וַיֹּאמֶר יוֹסֵף אֶל־אֶחָיו גְּשׁ
 וּ־נָא אֵלַי וַיִּגָּשׁוּ וַיֹּאמֶר אֲ
 נִי יוֹסֵף אֲחִיכֶם אֲשֶׁר־מְכַרְתֶּם 
 אֹתִי מִצְרָיְמָה׃\nVayomer yosef el-echav geshu-na elai 
 vayigashu vayomer ani yosef achikhem asher-mekhartem oti mitzrayemah\nAnd 
 Joseph said unto his brethren: ‘Come near to me\, I pray you.’ And the
 y came near. And he said: ‘I am Joseph your brother\, whom ye sold into 
 Egypt.\n\nJoseph says to the brothers who sold him\, "Come close to me." I
 t is one of the great moments of forgiveness in the Torah.\n\nOpen Aleph: 
 https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271112@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271112
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271113
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 50:20
DESCRIPTION:וְאַתֶּם חֲשַׁבְתֶּם עָלַי רָעָה 
 אֱלֹהִים חֲשָׁבָהּ לְטֹבָה לְמַעַן עֲ
 שֹׂה כַּיּוֹם הַזֶּה לְהַחֲיֹת עַם־רָב׃
 \nVe'atem chashavtem alai ra'ah Elohim chashavah letovah lema'an asoh kayo
 m hazeh lehachayot am-rav\nAnd as for you\, ye meant evil against me\; but
  God meant it for good\, to bring to pass\, as it is this day\, to save mu
 ch people alive.\n\nJoseph tells his brothers that what they meant for har
 m\, God turned to good. Hard chapters of a life can lead somewhere good.\n
 \nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271113@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271113
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271114
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 3:5
DESCRIPTION:וַיֹּאמֶר אַל־תִּקְרַב הֲלֹם שַׁל
 ־נְעָלֶיךָ מֵעַל רַגְלֶיךָ כִּי הַמָּק
 וֹם אֲשֶׁר אַתָּה עוֹמֵד עָלָיו אַדְמַת
 ־קֹדֶשׁ הוּא׃\nVayomer al-tikrav halom shal-ne'alekha me'al ra
 glekha ki hamakom asher atah omed alav admat-kodesh hu\nAnd He said: ‘Dr
 aw not nigh hither\; put off thy shoes from off thy feet\, for the place w
 hereon thou standest is holy ground.’\n\nAt the burning bush Moses is to
 ld to take off his shoes\, because the ground is holy. Some moments call f
 or us to slow down and pay attention.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.o
 nrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271114@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271114
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271115
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 3:14
DESCRIPTION:וַיֹּאמֶר אֱלֹהִים אֶל־מֹשֶׁה אֶ
 הְיֶה אֲשֶׁר אֶהְיֶה וַיֹּאמֶר כֹּה תֹא
 מַר לִבְנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל אֶהְיֶה שְׁלָחַ
 נִי אֲלֵיכֶם׃\nVayomer Elohim el-Mosheh ehyeh asher ehyeh vayo
 mer koh tomar livnei Yisra'el ehyeh shelachani aleikhem\nAnd God said unto
  Moses: ‘I AM THAT I AM’\; and He said: ‘Thus shalt thou say unto th
 e children of Israel: I AM hath sent me unto you.’\n\nEhyeh asher ehyeh:
  "I will be what I will be." God's name here is about being present\, in e
 very time and place.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/mor
 ning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271115@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271115
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271116
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 13:8
DESCRIPTION:וְהִגַּדְתָּ לְבִנְךָ בַּיּוֹם הַ
 הוּא לֵאמֹר בַּעֲבוּר זֶה עָשָׂה יְהוָה 
 לִי בְּצֵאתִי מִמִּצְרָיִם׃\nVehigadta levinkha b
 ayom hahu lemor ba'avur zeh asah Adonai li betzeti mimitzrayim\nAnd thou s
 halt tell thy son in that day\, saying: It is because of that which the LO
 RD did for me when I came forth out of Egypt.\n\nThis verse is why we tell
  the Passover story at the Seder. Each generation tells it as if it happen
 ed to them.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271116@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271116
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271117
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 14:14
DESCRIPTION:יְהוָה יִלָּחֵם לָכֶם וְאַתֶּם 
 תַּחֲרִישׁוּן׃\nAdonai yilachem lakhem ve'atem tacharishun\n
 The LORD will fight for you\, and ye shall hold your peace.’\n\nAt the S
 ea of Reeds\, Moses tells the frightened people that God will fight for th
 em. Sometimes the right move is to stay calm and trust.\n\nOpen Aleph: htt
 ps://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271117@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271117
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271118
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 15:2
DESCRIPTION:עָזִּי וְזִמְרָת יָהּ וַיְהִי־לִי
  לִישׁוּעָה זֶה אֵלִי וְאַנְוֵהוּ אֱלֹ
 הֵי אָבִי וַאֲרֹמְמֶנְהוּ׃\nAzi vezimrat yah vayhi
 -li lishu'ah zeh eli ve'anvehu elohei avi va'aromemenhu\nThe LORD is my st
 rength and song\, And He is become my salvation\; This is my God\, and I w
 ill glorify Him\; My father’s God\, and I will exalt Him.\n\nFrom the So
 ng at the Sea: "The Lord is my strength and my song." These words are sung
  in synagogue every morning.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.c
 om/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271118@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271118
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271119
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 15:11
DESCRIPTION:מִי־כָמֹכָה בָּאֵלִם יְהוָה מִי 
 כָּמֹכָה נֶאְדָּר בַּקֹּדֶשׁ נוֹרָא תְ
 הִלֹּת עֹשֵׂה פֶלֶא׃\nMi-khamokhah ba'elim Adonai mi kam
 okhah nedar bakodesh nora tehilot oseh fele\nWho is like unto Thee\, O LOR
 D\, among the mighty? Who is like unto Thee\, glorious in holiness\, Fearf
 ul in praises\, doing wonders?\n\nMi chamocha\, "Who is like You?" This li
 ne from the Song at the Sea is part of the daily prayers\, just after the 
 Shema.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271119@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271119
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271120
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 19:6
DESCRIPTION:וְאַתֶּם תִּהְיוּ־לִי מַמְלֶכֶת 
 כֹּהֲנִים וְגוֹי קָדוֹשׁ אֵלֶּה הַדְּבָ
 רִים אֲשֶׁר תְּדַבֵּר אֶל־בְּנֵי יִשְׂ
 רָאֵל׃\nVe'atem tihyu-li mamlekhet kohanim vegoy kadosh eleh hadevar
 im asher tedaber el-benei Yisra'el\nand ye shall be unto Me a kingdom of p
 riests\, and a holy nation. These are the words which thou shalt speak unt
 o the children of Israel.’\n\nAt Sinai the whole people is called a king
 dom of priests and a holy nation. Holiness is meant for everyone\, not onl
 y for a few.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271120@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271120
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271121
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 20:2
DESCRIPTION:אָנֹכִי יְהוָה אֱלֹהֶיךָ אֲשֶׁר ה
 וֹצֵאתִיךָ מֵאֶרֶץ מִצְרַיִם מִבֵּית עֲ
 בָדִים׃\nAnokhi Adonai Elohekha asher hotzetikha me'eretz Mitzrayim
  mibeit avadim\nI am the LORD thy God\, who brought thee out of the land o
 f Egypt\, out of the house of bondage.\n\nThe Ten Commandments begin with 
 who God is: the One who brought us out of slavery. Freedom comes first\, a
 nd the commandments follow.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.co
 m/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271121@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271121
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271122
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 20:8
DESCRIPTION:זָכוֹר אֶת־יוֹם הַשַׁבָּת לְקַדְּ
 שׁוֹ\nZakhor et-yom hashabat lekadesho\nRemember the sabbath day\, to 
 keep it holy.\n\nZachor: "Remember the Shabbat day." We remember it with c
 andles\, Kiddush\, rest and time with the people we love.\n\nOpen Aleph: h
 ttps://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271122@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271122
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271123
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 20:12
DESCRIPTION:כַּבֵּד אֶת־אָבִיךָ וְאֶת־אִמֶּ
 ךָ לְמַעַן יַאֲרִכוּן יָמֶיךָ עַל הָאֲ
 דָמָה אֲשֶׁר־יְהוָה אֱלֹהֶיךָ נֹתֵן לָ
 ךְ׃\nKabed et-avikha ve'et-imekha lema'an ya'arikhun yamekha al ha'adam
 ah asher-Adonai Elohekha noten lakh\nHonour thy father and thy mother\, th
 at thy days may be long upon the land which the LORD thy God giveth thee.\
 n\nHonour your father and your mother. It is one of the Ten Commandments\,
  and the first that comes with a promise of long life.\n\nOpen Aleph: http
 s://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271123@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271123
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271124
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 22:20
DESCRIPTION:וְגֵר לֹא־תוֹנֶה וְלֹא תִלְחָצֶנּ
 וּ כִּי־גֵרִים הֱיִיתֶם בְּאֶרֶץ מִצְרָ
 יִם׃\nVeger lo-toneh velo tilchatzenu ki-gerim heyitem be'eretz Mitzra
 yim\nAnd a stranger shalt thou not wrong\, neither shalt thou oppress him\
 ; for ye were strangers in the land of Egypt.\n\nDo not wrong the stranger
 \, because you were strangers in Egypt. This idea comes up again and again
  in the Torah.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271124@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271124
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271125
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 23:2
DESCRIPTION:לֹא־תִהְיֶה אַחֲרֵי־רַבִּים לְרָ
 עֹת וְלֹא־תַעֲנֶה עַל־רִב לִנְטֹת אַחֲ
 רֵי רַבִּים לְהַטֹּת׃\nLo-tihyeh acharei-rabim lera'ot 
 velo-ta'aneh al-riv lintot acharei rabim lehatot\nThou shalt not follow a 
 multitude to do evil\; neither shalt thou bear witness in a cause to turn 
 aside after a multitude to pervert justice\;\n\nDo not follow the crowd to
  do wrong. Doing the right thing sometimes means standing apart.\n\nOpen A
 leph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271125@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271125
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271126
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 23:9
DESCRIPTION:וְגֵר לֹא תִלְחָץ וְאַתֶּם יְדַעְ
 תֶּם אֶת־נֶפֶשׁ הַגֵּר כִּי־גֵרִים הֱיִ
 יתֶם בְּאֶרֶץ מִצְרָיִם׃\nVeger lo tilchatz ve'atem 
 yedatem et-nefesh hager ki-gerim heyitem be'eretz Mitzrayim\nAnd a strange
 r shalt thou not oppress\; for ye know the heart of a stranger\, seeing ye
  were strangers in the land of Egypt.\n\n"You know the heart of the strang
 er." Our own history should make us kind to newcomers.\n\nOpen Aleph: http
 s://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271126@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271126
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271127
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 25:8
DESCRIPTION:וְעָשׂוּ לִי מִקְדָּשׁ וְשָׁכַנְ
 תִּי בְּתוֹכָם׃\nVe'asu li mikdash veshakhanti betokham\nAnd
  let them make Me a sanctuary\, that I may dwell among them.\n\n"Make Me a
  sanctuary\, and I will dwell among them." Not "in it\," but among them: G
 od lives among people\, in the places they make holy.\n\nOpen Aleph: https
 ://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271127@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271127
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271128
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 33:13
DESCRIPTION:וְעַתָּה אִם־נָא מָצָאתִי חֵן בְּ
 עֵינֶיךָ הוֹדִעֵנִי נָא אֶת־דְּרָכֶךָ 
 וְאֵדָעֲךָ לְמַעַן אֶמְצָא־חֵן בְּעֵי
 נֶיךָ וּרְאֵה כִּי עַמְּךָ הַגּוֹי הַ
 זֶּה׃\nVe'atah im-na matzati chen be'einekha hodi'eni na et-derakhekh
 a ve'eda'akha lema'an emtza-chen be'einekha ure'eh ki amekha hagoy hazeh\n
 Now therefore\, I pray Thee\, if I have found grace in Thy sight\, show me
  now Thy ways\, that I may know Thee\, to the end that I may find grace in
  Thy sight\; and consider that this nation is Thy people.’\n\nMoses asks
  God\, "Show me Your ways\, so that I may know You." Learning is one of th
 e ways Jews come close to God.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender
 .com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271128@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271128
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271129
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 34:6
DESCRIPTION:וַיַּעֲבֹר יְהוָה עַל־פָּנָיו וַ
 יִּקְרָא יְהוָה יְהוָה אֵל רַחוּם וְחַ
 נּוּן אֶרֶךְ אַפַּיִם וְרַב־חֶסֶד וֶאֱ
 מֶת\nVaya'avor Adonai al-panav vayikra Adonai Adonai el rachum vechanun
  erekh apayim verav-chesed ve'emet\nAnd the LORD passed by before him\, an
 d proclaimed: ‘The LORD\, the LORD\, God\, merciful and gracious\, long-
 suffering\, and abundant in goodness and truth\;\n\nThese are God's qualit
 ies of mercy\, sung on the High Holy Days: compassionate\, gracious\, slow
  to anger\, full of kindness and truth.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review
 .onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271129@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271129
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271130
SUMMARY:Torah: Leviticus 19:2
DESCRIPTION:דַּבֵּר אֶל־כָּל־עֲדַת בְּנֵי־יִ
 שְׂרָאֵל וְאָמַרְתָּ אֲלֵהֶם קְדֹשִׁים 
 תִּהְיוּ כִּי קָדוֹשׁ אֲנִי יְהוָה אֱלֹ
 הֵיכֶם׃\nDaber el-kol-adat benei-Yisra'el ve'amarta alehem kedoshim
  tihyu ki kadosh ani Adonai Eloheikhem\nSpeak unto all the congregation of
  the children of Israel\, and say unto them: Ye shall be holy\; for I the 
 LORD your God am holy.\n\n"You shall be holy\, for I am holy." The chapter
  that follows shows what that means: honesty\, kindness and fairness in ev
 eryday life.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271130@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271130
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271201
SUMMARY:Torah: Leviticus 19:3
DESCRIPTION:אִישׁ אִמּוֹ וְאָבִיו תִּירָאוּ 
 וְאֶת־שַׁבְּתֹתַי תִּשְׁמֹרוּ אֲנִי יְ
 הוָה אֱלֹהֵיכֶם׃\nIsh imo ve'aviv tira'u ve'et-shabetotai t
 ishmoru ani Adonai Eloheikhem\nYe shall fear every man his mother\, and hi
 s father\, and ye shall keep My sabbaths: I am the LORD your God.\n\nRespe
 ct your parents and keep Shabbat. Both are about honouring where we come f
 rom.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271201@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271201
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271202
SUMMARY:Torah: Leviticus 19:9
DESCRIPTION:וּבְקֻצְרְכֶם אֶת־קְצִיר אַרְצְ
 כֶם לֹא תְכַלֶּה פְּאַת שָׂדְךָ לִקְצֹר 
 וְלֶקֶט קְצִירְךָ לֹא תְלַקֵּט׃\nUvekutzrekhem
  et-ketzir artzekhem lo tekhaleh pe'at sadekha liktzor veleket ketzirekha 
 lo telaket\nAnd when ye reap the harvest of your land\, thou shalt not who
 lly reap the corner of thy field\, neither shalt thou gather the gleaning 
 of thy harvest.\n\nLeave the corners of your field for people in need. Giv
 ing to others is built right into how we earn and spend.\n\nOpen Aleph: ht
 tps://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271202@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271202
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271203
SUMMARY:Torah: Leviticus 19:14
DESCRIPTION:לֹא־תְקַלֵּל חֵרֵשׁ וְלִפְנֵי עִ
 וֵּר לֹא תִתֵּן מִכְשֹׁל וְיָרֵאתָ מֵּ
 אֱלֹהֶיךָ אֲנִי יְהוָה׃\nLo-tekalel cheresh velifnei 
 iver lo titen mikhshol veyareta me'Elohekha ani Adonai\nThou shalt not cur
 se the deaf\, nor put a stumbling-block before the blind\, but thou shalt 
 fear thy God: I am the LORD.\n\nDo not curse the deaf or put a stumbling b
 lock before the blind. Treat everyone with care\, especially those who can
 not defend themselves.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/m
 orning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271203@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271203
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271204
SUMMARY:Torah: Leviticus 19:16
DESCRIPTION:לֹא־תֵלֵךְ רָכִיל בְּעַמֶּיךָ לֹא
  תַעֲמֹד עַל־דַּם רֵעֶךָ אֲנִי יְהוָה׃\nL
 o-telekh rakhil be'amekha lo ta'amod al-dam re'ekha ani Adonai\nThou shalt
  not go up and down as a talebearer among thy people\; neither shalt thou 
 stand idly by the blood of thy neighbour: I am the LORD.\n\nDo not spread 
 gossip\, and do not stand by while your neighbour is in danger. Words can 
 hurt\, and silence can too.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.co
 m/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271204@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271204
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271205
SUMMARY:Torah: Leviticus 19:18
DESCRIPTION:לֹא־תִקֹּם וְלֹא־תִטֹּר אֶת־בְּ
 נֵי עַמֶּךָ וְאָהַבְתָּ לְרֵעֲךָ כָּמוֹ
 ךָ אֲנִי יְהוָה׃\nLo-tikom velo-titor et-benei amekha ve'aha
 vta lere'akha kamokha ani Adonai\nThou shalt not take vengeance\, nor bear
  any grudge against the children of thy people\, but thou shalt love thy n
 eighbour as thyself: I am the LORD.\n\n"Love your neighbour as yourself." 
 Rabbi Akiva called this the great principle of the whole Torah.\n\nOpen Al
 eph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271205@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271205
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271206
SUMMARY:Torah: Leviticus 19:32
DESCRIPTION:מִפְּנֵי שֵׂיבָה תָּקוּם וְהָדַרְ
 תָּ פְּנֵי זָקֵן וְיָרֵאתָ מֵּאֱלֹהֶיךָ
  אֲנִי יְהוָה׃\nMipenei seivah takum vehadarta penei zaken vey
 areta me'Elohekha ani Adonai\nThou shalt rise up before the hoary head\, a
 nd honour the face of the old man\, and thou shalt fear thy God: I am the 
 LORD.\n\nRise before the elderly and honour them. Age brings wisdom\, and 
 the Torah asks us to show it respect.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.o
 nrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271206@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271206
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271207
SUMMARY:Torah: Leviticus 25:10
DESCRIPTION:וְקִדַּשְׁתֶּם אֵת שְׁנַת הַחֲמִ
 שִּׁים שָׁנָה וּקְרָאתֶם דְּרוֹר בָּאָ
 רֶץ לְכָל־יֹשְׁבֶיהָ יוֹבֵל הִוא תִּהְ
 יֶה לָכֶם וְשַׁבְתֶּם אִישׁ אֶל־אֲחֻזָּ
 תוֹ וְאִישׁ אֶל־מִשְׁפַּחְתּוֹ תָּשֻׁב
 וּ׃\nVekidashtem et shenat hachamishim shanah ukeratem deror ba'aretz l
 ekhol-yosheveha yovel hiv tihyeh lakhem veshavtem ish el-achuzato ve'ish e
 l-mishpachto tashuvu\nAnd ye shall hallow the fiftieth year\, and proclaim
  liberty throughout the land unto all the inhabitants thereof\; it shall b
 e a jubilee unto you\; and ye shall return every man unto his possession\,
  and ye shall return every man unto his family.\n\n"Proclaim liberty throu
 ghout the land." These words about the Jubilee year are cast on the Libert
 y Bell in Philadelphia.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/
 morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271207@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271207
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271208
SUMMARY:Torah: Numbers 6:24
DESCRIPTION:יְבָרֶכְךָ יְהוָה וְיִשְׁמְרֶךָ׃\
 nYevarekhkha Adonai veyishmerekha\nThe LORD bless thee\, and keep thee\;\n
 \nThe first line of the Priestly Blessing\, still said in synagogues and b
 y parents to children on Friday night.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.
 onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271208@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271208
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271209
SUMMARY:Torah: Numbers 6:26
DESCRIPTION:יִשָּׂא יְהוָה פָּנָיו אֵלֶיךָ וְ
 יָשֵׂם לְךָ שָׁלוֹם׃\nYisa Adonai panav elekha veyasem l
 ekha shalom\nThe LORD lift up His countenance upon thee\, and give thee pe
 ace.\n\nThe Priestly Blessing ends with shalom\, peace. In Hebrew\, shalom
  also means wholeness: everything in its right place.\n\nOpen Aleph: https
 ://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271209@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271209
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271210
SUMMARY:Torah: Numbers 11:29
DESCRIPTION:וַיֹּאמֶר לוֹ מֹשֶׁה הַמְקַנֵּא 
 אַתָּה לִי וּמִי יִתֵּן כָּל־עַם יְהוָה 
 נְבִיאִים כִּי־יִתֵּן יְהוָה אֶת־רוּח
 וֹ עֲלֵיהֶם׃\nVayomer lo Mosheh hamkane atah li umi yiten kol-a
 m Adonai nevi'im ki-yiten Adonai et-rucho aleihem\nAnd Moses said unto him
 : ‘Art thou jealous for my sake? would that all the LORD’S people were
  prophets\, that the LORD would put His spirit upon them! ’\n\nWhen othe
 rs begin to prophesy\, Moses is not jealous. He wishes everyone could shar
 e God's spirit. Great leaders lift others up.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-
 review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271210@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271210
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271211
SUMMARY:Torah: Numbers 15:39
DESCRIPTION:וְהָיָה לָכֶם לְצִיצִת וּרְאִיתֶם
  אֹתוֹ וּזְכַרְתֶּם אֶת־כָּל־מִצְוֹת יְ
 הוָה וַעֲשִׂיתֶם אֹתָם וְלֹא־תָתֻרוּ אַ
 חֲרֵי לְבַבְכֶם וְאַחֲרֵי עֵינֵיכֶם אֲ
 שֶׁר־אַתֶּם זֹנִים אַחֲרֵיהֶם׃\nVehayah lakhem
  letzitzit ure'item oto uzekhartem et-kol-mitzvot Adonai va'asitem otam ve
 lo-taturu acharei levavkhem ve'acharei eineikhem asher-atem zonim achareih
 em\nAnd it shall be unto you for a fringe\, that ye may look upon it\, and
  remember all the commandments of the LORD\, and do them\; and that ye go 
 not about after your own heart and your own eyes\, after which ye use to g
 o astray\;\n\nThis verse is about the tzitzit\, the fringes on the tallit.
  Seeing them is a reminder of the commandments and of who we want to be.\n
 \nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271211@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271211
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271212
SUMMARY:Torah: Numbers 24:5
DESCRIPTION:מַה־טֹּבוּ אֹהָלֶיךָ יַעֲקֹב מִ
 שְׁכְּנֹתֶיךָ יִשְׂרָאֵל׃\nMah-tovu ohalekha Ya'ak
 ov mishkenotekha Yisra'el\nHow goodly are thy tents\, O Jacob\, Thy dwelli
 ngs\, O Israel!\n\nMah tovu\, "How good are your tents." Many synagogues o
 pen the morning service with these words.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-revi
 ew.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271212@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271212
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271213
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 4:9
DESCRIPTION:רַק הִשָּׁמֶר לְךָ וּשְׁמֹר נַפְ
 שְׁךָ מְאֹד פֶּן־תִּשְׁכַּח אֶת־הַדְּ
 בָרִים אֲשֶׁר־רָאוּ עֵינֶיךָ וּפֶן־יָס
 וּרוּ מִלְּבָבְךָ כֹּל יְמֵי חַיֶּיךָ 
 וְהוֹדַעְתָּם לְבָנֶיךָ וְלִבְנֵי בָנֶ
 יךָ׃\nRak hishamer lekha ushemor nafshekha me'od pen-tishkach et-hadev
 arim asher-ra'u einekha ufen-yasuru milevavekha kol yemei chayekha vehodat
 am levanekha velivnei vanekha\nOnly take heed to thyself\, and keep thy so
 ul diligently\, lest thou forget the things which thine eyes saw\, and les
 t they depart from thy heart all the days of thy life\; but make them know
 n unto thy children and thy children’s children\;\n\nDo not forget what 
 you have seen\, and teach it to your children and grandchildren. Memory is
  how a people stays alive.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com
 /#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271213@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271213
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271214
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 6:4
DESCRIPTION:שְׁמַע יִשְׂרָאֵל יְהוָה אֱלֹהֵינ
 וּ יְהוָה אֶחָד׃\nShema Yisra'el Adonai Eloheinu Adonai echa
 d\nHEAR\, O ISRAEL: THE LORD OUR GOD\, THE LORD IS ONE.\n\nThe Shema\, the
  central line of Jewish prayer: "Hear\, O Israel\, the Lord is our God\, t
 he Lord is One." It is said morning and night.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef
 -review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271214@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271214
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271215
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 6:5
DESCRIPTION:וְאָהַבְתָּ אֵת יְהוָה אֱלֹהֶיךָ 
 בְּכָל־לְבָבְךָ וּבְכָל־נַפְשְׁךָ וּבְ
 כָל־מְאֹדֶךָ׃\nVe'ahavta et Adonai Elohekha bekhol-levavekha 
 uvekhol-nafshekha uvekhol-me'odekha\nAnd thou shalt love the LORD thy God 
 with all thy heart\, and with all thy soul\, and with all thy might.\n\nV'
 ahavta: love God with all your heart\, all your soul and all your strength
 . Faith in Judaism is about love\, not only belief.\n\nOpen Aleph: https:/
 /alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271215@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271215
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271216
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 6:7
DESCRIPTION:וְשִׁנַּנְתָּם לְבָנֶיךָ וְדִבַּ
 רְתָּ בָּם בְּשִׁבְתְּךָ בְּבֵיתֶךָ וּ
 בְלֶכְתְּךָ בַדֶּרֶךְ וּבְשָׁכְבְּךָ 
 וּבְקוּמֶךָ׃\nVeshinantam levanekha vedibarta bam beshivtekha 
 beveitekha uvelekhtekha vaderekh uveshakhbekha uvekumekha\nand thou shalt 
 teach them diligently unto thy children\, and shalt talk of them when thou
  sittest in thy house\, and when thou walkest by the way\, and when thou l
 iest down\, and when thou risest up.\n\nTalk about these words at home\, o
 n the road\, when you lie down and when you get up. That is why the Shema 
 is said at bedtime and in the morning.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.
 onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271216@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271216
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271217
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 8:3
DESCRIPTION:וַיְעַנְּךָ וַיַּרְעִבֶךָ וַיַּ
 אֲכִלְךָ אֶת הַמָּן אֲשֶׁר לֹא־יָדַעְ
 תָּ וְלֹא יָדְעוּן אֲבֹתֶיךָ לְמַעַן ה
 וֹדִעֲךָ כִּי לֹא עַל־הַלֶּחֶם לְבַדּוֹ
  יִחְיֶה הָאָדָם כִּי עַל־כָּל־מוֹצָא 
 פִי־יְהוָה יִחְיֶה הָאָדָם׃\nVay'anekha vayar'ive
 kha vaya'akhilkha et haman asher lo-yadata velo yad'un avotekha lema'an ho
 di'akha ki lo al-halechem levado yichyeh ha'adam ki al-kol-motza fi-Adonai
  yichyeh ha'adam\nAnd He afflicted thee\, and suffered thee to hunger\, an
 d fed thee with manna\, which thou knewest not\, neither did thy fathers k
 now\; that He might make thee know that man doth not live by bread only\, 
 but by every thing that proceedeth out of the mouth of the LORD doth man l
 ive.\n\n"A person does not live by bread alone." We need meaning\, learnin
 g and purpose as much as food.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender
 .com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271217@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271217
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271218
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 8:10
DESCRIPTION:וְאָכַלְתָּ וְשָׂבָעְתָּ וּבֵרַ
 כְתָּ אֶת־יְהוָה אֱלֹהֶיךָ עַל־הָאָרֶץ 
 הַטֹּבָה אֲשֶׁר נָתַן־לָךְ׃\nVe'akhalta vesava'et
 a uverakhta et-Adonai Elohekha al-ha'aretz hatovah asher natan-lakh\nAnd t
 hou shalt eat and be satisfied\, and bless the LORD thy God for the good l
 and which He hath given thee.\n\nEat\, be satisfied\, and bless. This vers
 e is the source of Birkat Hamazon\, the blessing after meals.\n\nOpen Alep
 h: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271218@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271218
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271219
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 10:19
DESCRIPTION:וַאֲהַבְתֶּם אֶת־הַגֵּר כִּי־גֵ
 רִים הֱיִיתֶם בְּאֶרֶץ מִצְרָיִם׃\nVa'ahavte
 m et-hager ki-gerim heyitem be'eretz Mitzrayim\nLove ye therefore the stra
 nger\; for ye were strangers in the land of Egypt.\n\nLove the stranger\, 
 because you were strangers in Egypt. The Torah asks for more than not hurt
 ing newcomers\; it asks us to love them.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-revie
 w.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271219@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271219
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271220
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 16:20
DESCRIPTION:צֶדֶק צֶדֶק תִּרְדֹּף לְמַעַן תִּ
 חְיֶה וְיָרַשְׁתָּ אֶת־הָאָרֶץ אֲשֶׁר־
 יְהוָה אֱלֹהֶיךָ נֹתֵן לָךְ׃\nTzedek tzedek tirdo
 f lema'an tichyeh veyarashta et-ha'aretz asher-Adonai Elohekha noten lakh\
 nJustice\, justice shalt thou follow\, that thou mayest live\, and inherit
  the land which the LORD thy God giveth thee.\n\nTzedek tzedek tirdof: "Ju
 stice\, justice you shall pursue." The word is said twice\, to show how ha
 rd we should work for it.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/
 #/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271220@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271220
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271221
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 30:14
DESCRIPTION:כִּי־קָרוֹב אֵלֶיךָ הַדָּבָר מְאֹ
 ד בְּפִיךָ וּבִלְבָבְךָ לַעֲשֹׂתוֹ׃\nKi-ka
 rov elekha hadavar me'od befikha uvilvavekha la'asoto\nBut the word is ver
 y nigh unto thee\, in thy mouth\, and in thy heart\, that thou mayest do i
 t.\n\nThe Torah is not far away: it is in your mouth and in your heart. It
  is within reach\, one word at a time.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.
 onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271221@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271221
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271222
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 30:19
DESCRIPTION:הַעִידֹתִי בָכֶם הַיּוֹם אֶת־הַ
 שָּׁמַיִם וְאֶת־הָאָרֶץ הַחַיִּים וְהַ
 מָּוֶת נָתַתִּי לְפָנֶיךָ הַבְּרָכָה וְ
 הַקְּלָלָה וּבָחַרְתָּ בַּחַיִּים לְמַ
 עַן תִּחְיֶה אַתָּה וְזַרְעֶךָ׃\nHa'idoti vakh
 em hayom et-hashamayim ve'et-ha'aretz hachayim vehamavet natati lefanekha 
 haberakhah vehakelalah uvacharta bachayim lema'an tichyeh atah vezar'ekha\
 nI call heaven and earth to witness against you this day\, that I have set
  before thee life and death\, the blessing and the curse\; therefore choos
 e life\, that thou mayest live\, thou and thy seed\;\n\n"Choose life." Eve
 ry day brings choices\, and the Torah asks us to choose the ones that lead
  to life and blessing.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/m
 orning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271222@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271222
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271223
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 31:6
DESCRIPTION:חִזְקוּ וְאִמְצוּ אַל־תִּירְאוּ 
 וְאַל־תַּעַרְצוּ מִפְּנֵיהֶם כִּי יְה
 וָה אֱלֹהֶיךָ הוּא הַהֹלֵךְ עִמָּךְ לֹא 
 יַרְפְּךָ וְלֹא יַעַזְבֶךָּ׃\nChizku ve'imtzu al
 -tir'u ve'al-ta'artzu mipeneihem ki Adonai Elohekha hu haholekh imakh lo y
 arpekha velo ya'azveka\nBe strong and of good courage\, fear not\, nor be 
 affrighted at them\; for the LORD thy God\, He it is that doth go with the
 e\; He will not fail thee\, nor forsake thee.’\n\nChazak ve'ematz: "Be s
 trong and of good courage." Moses says this before the people enter the la
 nd without him.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271223@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271223
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271224
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 6:6
DESCRIPTION:וְהָיוּ הַדְּבָרִים הָאֵלֶּה אֲ
 שֶׁר אָנֹכִי מְצַוְּךָ הַיּוֹם עַל־לְבָ
 בֶךָ׃\nVehayu hadevarim ha'eleh asher anokhi metzavekha hayom al-leva
 vekha\nAnd these words\, which I command thee this day\, shall be upon thy
  heart\;\n\n"These words shall be upon your heart." Learning Torah is mean
 t to go deeper than memory\, into who we are.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-
 review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271224@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271224
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271225
SUMMARY:Torah: Exodus 31:16
DESCRIPTION:וְשָׁמְרוּ בְנֵי־יִשְׂרָאֵל אֶת־
 הַשַּׁבָּת לַעֲשׂוֹת אֶת־הַשַּׁבָּת לְ
 דֹרֹתָם בְּרִית עוֹלָם׃\nVeshamru venei-Yisra'el et-h
 ashabat la'asot et-hashabat ledorotam berit olam\nWherefore the children o
 f Israel shall keep the sabbath\, to observe the sabbath throughout their 
 generations\, for a perpetual covenant.\n\nV'shamru: the people of Israel 
 shall keep the Shabbat for all generations. This verse is sung on Friday n
 ight and Shabbat morning.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/
 #/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271225@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271225
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271226
SUMMARY:Torah: Deuteronomy 34:10
DESCRIPTION:וְלֹא־קָם נָבִיא עוֹד בְּיִשְׂרָ
 אֵל כְּמֹשֶׁה אֲשֶׁר יְדָעוֹ יְהוָה פָּ
 נִים אֶל־פָּנִים׃\nVelo-kam navi od beyisra'el kemosheh as
 her yeda'o Adonai panim el-panim\nAnd there hath not arisen a prophet sinc
 e in Israel like unto Moses\, whom the LORD knew face to face\;\n\nNear th
 e very end of the Torah: no prophet arose like Moses\, who knew God face t
 o face. Then we roll the scroll back and start again.\n\nOpen Aleph: https
 ://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271226@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271226
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271227
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 1:1
DESCRIPTION:בְּרֵאשִׁית בָּרָא אֱלֹהִים אֵת 
 הַשָּׁמַיִם וְאֵת הָאָרֶץ׃\nBereshit bara Elohim e
 t hashamayim ve'et ha'aretz\nIn the beginning God created the heaven and t
 he earth.\n\nThe Torah opens with its first word\, Bereshit\, "in the begi
 nning." Everything that follows starts here: the world has a Maker\, and i
 t did not come about by chance.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrende
 r.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271227@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271227
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271228
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 1:3
DESCRIPTION:וַיֹּאמֶר אֱלֹהִים יְהִי אוֹר וַ
 יְהִי־אוֹר׃\nVayomer Elohim yehi or vayhi-or\nAnd God said: ‘
 Let there be light.’ And there was light.\n\nThe first thing God makes i
 s light\, and He makes it with words. In Judaism speech has real power\, s
 o the words we choose each day matter.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.
 onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271228@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271228
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271229
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 1:27
DESCRIPTION:וַיִּבְרָא אֱלֹהִים אֶת־הָאָדָם 
 בְּצַלְמוֹ בְּצֶלֶם אֱלֹהִים בָּרָא אֹת
 וֹ זָכָר וּנְקֵבָה בָּרָא אֹתָם׃\nVayivra Eloh
 im et-ha'adam betzalmo betzelem Elohim bara oto zakhar unekevah bara otam\
 nAnd God created man in His own image\, in the image of God created He him
 \; male and female created He them.\n\nEvery person is made in the image o
 f God. That is why each human life has worth\, whoever the person is and w
 herever they come from.\n\nOpen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/
 morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271229@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271229
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271230
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 1:31
DESCRIPTION:וַיַּרְא אֱלֹהִים אֶת־כָּל־אֲשֶׁ
 ר עָשָׂה וְהִנֵּה־טוֹב מְאֹד וַיְהִי־עֶ
 רֶב וַיְהִי־בֹקֶר יוֹם הַשִּׁשִּׁי׃\nVayar
  Elohim et-kol-asher asah vehineh-tov me'od vayhi-erev vayhi-voker yom has
 hishi\nAnd God saw every thing that He had made\, and\, behold\, it was ve
 ry good. And there was evening and there was morning\, the sixth day.\n\nA
 fter each day God saw that it was good. On the sixth day\, with people in 
 the world\, it became "very good." Look for the good in your own day.\n\nO
 pen Aleph: https://alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271230@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271230
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271231
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 2:3
DESCRIPTION:וַיְבָרֶךְ אֱלֹהִים אֶת־יוֹם הַ
 שְּׁבִיעִי וַיְקַדֵּשׁ אֹתוֹ כִּי בוֹ 
 שָׁבַת מִכָּל־מְלַאכְתּוֹ אֲשֶׁר־בָּרָ
 א אֱלֹהִים לַעֲשׂוֹת׃\nVayvarekh Elohim et-yom hashevi'
 i vaykadesh oto ki vo shavat mikol-melakhto asher-bara Elohim la'asot\nAnd
  God blessed the seventh day\, and hallowed it\; because that in it He res
 ted from all His work which God in creating had made.\n\nThis is the first
  Shabbat. God rested on the seventh day and made it holy\, and we rest on 
 it too. Shabbat is a gift of time\, not only a rule.\n\nOpen Aleph: https:
 //alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aleph-torah-20271231@aleph
DTSTAMP:20261108T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271231
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20280101
SUMMARY:Torah: Genesis 2:15
DESCRIPTION:וַיִּקַּח יְהוָה אֱלֹהִים אֶת־הָ
 אָדָם וַיַּנִּחֵהוּ בְגַן־עֵדֶן לְעָבְ
 דָהּ וּלְשָׁמְרָהּ׃\nVayikach Adonai Elohim et-ha'adam v
 ayanichehu vegan-eden le'avedah uleshamerah\nAnd the LORD God took the man
 \, and put him into the garden of Eden to dress it and to keep it.\n\nAdam
  was put in the garden to work it and to guard it. The earth is placed in 
 our care\, and looking after it is part of our job.\n\nOpen Aleph: https:/
 /alef-review.onrender.com/#/morning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Aleph
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
